{"body":{"text":["**Lifetime**: whether a holon nothing holds should ever leave the field on its own. Set aside."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001997","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G000199W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's decisions, 2026-11-02, after reasoning through OpenLight's relations and six simulated fields; holding and many wholes his, 2026-11-04: maybe the store should be flat anyway, assembled only by the primitives we have.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019A4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Any whole can be taken away as a store of its own: what it holds, through every reference that holds, with every version they had and the commits that touched them. What it stands on, its types and what it points at, may come with it, each still with its id and versions, so the day it meets the store they came from again, they plug back in. Relying on other foundations is no fault; it is how anything is built. What it holds is read through its types, so a whole taken without them is not known to hold; how much of what it stands on must come with it is open."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019B9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-04: you rely upon other foundations to build yours, that's completely fine; they still have their id, their version, and would plug back in; that one can't take it completely is another question. Holding read through types the session's. How the commits that touched a whole are found is ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00019GR"},".*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019EZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00013QB"},"text":["above"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019GR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass's object model is its own, with only the smallest standards beneath it; the background, and why, are in the formats."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019GW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass's store stands in a lineage: since around 2010 several movements have tried to take data back from the servers that hold it, and most of them build on one old idea, naming data by the hash of what it holds. This brief gives that background, what box glass's store draws inside it, and why the store is made rather than adopted."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019HM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried from the session's knowledge and the sources linked, 2026-11-01; checked against the sources only where a source is linked, and the rest not checked.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019KN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A name made from the hash of the content proves the content: fetch it from anyone, hash it again, and you know it was not changed. Everything below descends from that."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019MJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Ralph Merkle described trees of such hashes in 1979, BitTorrent used them to fetch pieces of files from strangers, and git made them everyday in 2005, where every file, folder and commit is an object named by its hash and a branch is a pointer to a commit."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019NM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried, not checked.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019Q6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Each family came at the same problem from its own side, and each has a culture as well as a format."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019QD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried, the session's survey of 2026-11-01.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019R4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["IPFS came from Juan Benet and Protocol Labs around 2015, aiming at a permanent web where content is found by what it is, not where it sits. Its data layer, IPLD, names objects by CIDs, encodes them as DAG-JSON or DAG-CBOR, links them by those names, and bundles them in CAR files. A [trustless gateway](https://specs.ipfs.tech/http-gateways/trustless-gateway/) serves objects over plain HTTP for a client to verify itself."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019RE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It is neutral and well specified, with no opinion on what objects mean. Its culture is idealistic and decentralist, and tied to cryptocurrency through Filecoin, which colours its reputation."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019TN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The gateway checked against its spec, 2026-11-01; the rest carried.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019VN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Bluesky's protocol began in 2019 as a Twitter-funded effort to make social media a protocol. Each user has a repository of typed records, each record with a key, every change a signed commit, the records in a Merkle tree, the whole exportable as a CAR file on top of IPLD. Records are typed by Lexicon schemas, and a repository lives on a server its owner chooses and can leave."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019W3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It is the closest thing in use to holons with ids, typed and committed and owned. It also brings its own identity system, record layout and server protocol, built for a social network of millions."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019YC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried from [library documentation](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/jcalabro/atmos/repo), not from the spec at atproto.com, which was not read.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G00019ZJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Local-first software keeps your data on your own devices and merges it with others' when they meet, so no server stands between you and your work."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001A06","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The 2019 essay [*Local-first software: You own your data, in spite of the cloud*](https://inkandswitch.com/local-first/), by Kleppmann, Wiggins, van Hardenberg and McGranaghan at Ink & Switch, named its ideals: no spinners, work offline, across devices, together, for a long time, privately, with final authority over your data. Its technique is CRDTs, structures that merge edits made apart without conflict, in libraries such as Automerge and Yjs."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001A12","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Its culture is a research lab's, close to tools for thought and to OpenLight's own. It is strongest at merging two people's work, and what it syncs are documents, between peers and servers, where glass publishes a store anyone can fetch."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001A39","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The essay and its authors checked, 2026-11-01; the rest carried.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001A4N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Secure Scuttlebutt gossiped between friends, Dat and Hypercore kept signed append-only logs, Nostr passes signed JSON events through relays, and [Willow](https://lwn.net/Articles/1005639), with Earthstar, syncs namespaces of paths with capabilities saying who may read and write. They are built for peers finding each other, small communities and life off the grid, which is further from a client fetching from a host than glass needs."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001A53","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Willow checked against LWN's account, 2026-11-01; the rest carried.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001A77","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Tim Berners-Lee's answer, from 2016: your data in a pod, described in RDF, with applications asking the pod for permission. It is the web's inventor's own attempt, and it keeps the data on a server and names it by where it is rather than by what it holds."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001A7M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried, not checked.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001A97","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Inside the box: objects named by their hash, never changed, linking to each other by hash; history as commit objects; a store published as plain files any host can serve; and a client that fetches only what it needs and checks every object itself."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001A9E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Outside it lies what the format does not decide, among them proving who published, merging, finding a store by name, networking between peers and who may read what; those still to be settled are gathered in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001AC2"},"."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AAW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001P4W"},"text":["the plan"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AC2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AC6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["None of the families is a medium for programs and interfaces as well as data, and none has types that govern what may be written. That is what OpenLight adds, and it lives in the object model, so the object model is glass's own: holons with ids, versions, an index, commits and refs."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001ACE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Beneath the model, glass borrows the smallest standards there are: canonical JSON and SHA-256, readable by hand and needing nothing. IPLD would give an ecosystem glass has no use for yet, at the cost of binding the encoding to it, and an IPLD encoding of the same objects stays possible if that use ever comes."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AE6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Proposed and reasoned by the session, 2026-11-01; agreed by the author, who found nothing in OpenLight's earlier studies against it.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AG0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Git versions files that hold no history of their own, and glass's objects carry their history in themselves, so git would hold history about history. Git also knows nothing of types or holons, and running it in a browser takes a library of its own. It remains useful as a way of carrying a store's files."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AGR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["SQLite is one engine's storage, not a format for a field that travels between engines. A store published as a database file binds every reader to SQLite, while a store of objects lets each engine keep whatever storage suits it, in the browser or on a machine."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AJM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: SQLite is not the answer to the object model OpenLight discussed, and glass is not to be based on git.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AM6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Proposed by the session and agreed by the author, 2026-11-01.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AN0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What an integration allows is its own to say: to be only read, or written through its programs, and how. A holon pointing into one may be pinned, as a reference to a file is pinned to the git commit it was read at."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001ARV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-04: why can't the stores we are talking about be the same first-class citizen as the other integrations; it's up to the integration if you can manipulate the holons or not; a git repository is its own store, its own source of truth, you never include it into your own; is an integration just a program, his question carried from OpenLight. Format, transport and integration kept apart the session's. How git in particular is integrated, its files edited from the field, their content shown or only addressed, its commits meeting the field's, is open; so is what an integration's programs owe the engine, waiting for programs to run.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001ATA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The client holds the engine and the interface, and it is the whole application, as capable as one on your own machine."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AXY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The client is the whole application: a chassis that hosts the page, a real engine that runs in the browser, and the interface that draws from it, speaking one protocol. It pulls a store and runs over it, so whoever opens it touches a real engine they can change things with, and the data they work on is theirs."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001AYQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's decision, 2026-11-01: we are running an engine in the client, over data in the client, that you can change in the browser.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001B0N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Anything more than reading needs a real engine near the reader. Editing in place, tabs, a layout that can be changed, all are state, and state needs a field and an engine to govern it; without them everything stays primitive."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001B1H","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine could stand on the internet, with every visitor's interface speaking to it, but then what each visitor may run and commit must be scoped, and authentication comes first. Or the site serves only the store, and each client runs its own engine over what it pulled: then nobody touches the author's engine, and whatever a reader does lands in their own field, which is how they own their data."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001B2W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's reasoning and decision, 2026-11-01: if there is to be any WYSIWYG it requires a real engine; the engine on the internet needs authentication or a scope to what can be committed; the client's own engine gives data ownership.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001B56","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Nothing a reader does reaches back to the author by itself: their notes and their visits stay in their own client, unless something is built to receive them. An engine on the internet stays possible later, as narrow as the field declares."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001B6J","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001B7Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The parts are OpenLight's, and each keeps to its own work."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001B87","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried from OpenLight's engine, chassis and view specs, read 2026-11-01.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001B8M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis is the page itself: it serves an almost empty document, starts the engine, installs the channel between the engine and the interface, and turns what the browser gives, its address and its back and forward, into input for the engine. Which components draw, what is attached and what the layout is are all field data, read through the engine, so nothing in the chassis is policy."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001B92","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried from OpenLight's chassis.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BB9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine holds the field and is the only way into it. It reads, commits and runs programs, and it judges every act against what the field declares, whoever asks: a program, a component, the reader. It draws nothing and serves no pages; its one contract is the protocol, so nothing that speaks to it depends on how it is built."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BBH","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried from OpenLight's engine: the wire is its only contract.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BDJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The interface is the components and what mounts them. It mounts the root, reads for each mount what it is given, and draws it again when a commit touches what it read. What a component does, it does as an ordinary commit or run, judged by the engine. What lasts is in the field, never in the interface."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BE0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried from OpenLight's view.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BFZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Everything that speaks to the engine uses the same few operations: read, commit, run, await, cancel and subscribe. In the browser they travel as messages to the engine's own thread, so the engine never holds up the drawing."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BG7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The operations OpenLight's; the browser's thread reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01. How a read is asked is ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001BJ5"},".*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BHG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001P4W"},"text":["open"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BJ5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Running glass on one's own machine is the same store and the same interface with another engine and another chassis: the engine as a program of its own, the chassis as a window. Nothing in the store or the interface depends on which."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BMP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: we are virtually creating a full capable client, it just comes preloaded with its default settings and connection. The consent and isolation are OpenLight's.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BSN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: the engine you have locally has its own field, and it is not mixing with the one which is public.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BXT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The home is a store like any other, written by the engine and kept in the browser's own storage. It holds six things:"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001BYN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The entry**: the mount the client boots into, at first the one the attached store ships."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001C0C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The root**: the mount the reader looks through, holding what is theirs, the component it calls and what it offers."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001C11","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The history**: where the reader has looked, a visit added with each move."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001C1T","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The runs**: every program the reader's engine has run."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001C2C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The reader's branches**: their own commits on the stores they pulled, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001C3A"},"."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001C2T","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001CF7"},"text":["beneath"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001C3A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01; the home as a store with its attachments and its entry is OpenLight's, where the arrangement is called the session.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001C47","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: do you care about the runs that someone else did?*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001C6G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Editing the layout and editing the data are different acts, so they land in different places."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CA7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: there is a difference between editing the data and editing the layout; let's say that layout is partitioned to local.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CAS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How things are drawn, which component draws a holon and what the reader looks at, is how the reader looks at the field, so changing it never touches the store. The root starts as the entry the store ships, and the reader follows the author's changes to it until they move themselves; from then on they hold their own root in the home."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CBM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The partition the author's, 2026-11-01; following the store's entry until the first move is the session's proposal, from OpenLight's desktop, where the session is the writable home of the arrangement. What was the arrangement, a layout of panes, became the root mount on 2026-11-03.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CDP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A holon's title, prose and data are what the store says, so changing them changes the source. The change is a commit on the reader's own branch of the pulled store, kept in the home. On a reload the reader stands on their branch or on the store's head, both always there, and one day a branch can be offered back."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CF8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01, answering the author's question of whether a reload loads the public data or the persisted data. In OpenLight, editing what you only read is a clone attached for writing, which its object model was meant to replace.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CH9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Governing the home is done by programs, judged by the engine like any act: resetting the root, clearing what is local, attaching another store, pulling the latest. What the reader stands on, which store, which commit, whether behind, is a place, drawn by a component like anything else. Nothing is managed from outside the field."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CJR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: there is no special chrome on top, it's all first-class native, as if Unix were built on programs and files.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CMK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Where the reader looks is the page's address, so going back and forward is only the address changing, and a reload lands where the address says. What the reader has looked at is kept in the home as their history, a holon each move adds a visit to and nothing rewrites; the root mount holds only what is the reader's, the component it calls and what it offers, and no longer changes with every move."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CNE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01, answering the author's question of what a virtual history stack means; the root's versions were the history from 2026-11-03 until the author found, the same night, that walking back by writing old versions again is not real history, since commits are a line you can't reverse, ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001CSJ"},". As ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001CSQ"}," tells.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CQW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0000MCS"},"text":["said"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CSJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001G6Q"},"text":["the interface"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CSQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["What is kept in the home is kept in the shape the engine wrote it in, and when that shape changes, what is kept may stop fitting. The floor is that the home is typed and reset is a program, so the reader is never stuck. How kept state follows a change of shape is open, as it is in OpenLight."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CSW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's concern, 2026-11-01; open.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CVX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What the client draws is the field, from a root mount, each place a holon called by a mount, so the interface is a mirror of the field."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CW5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The interface draws the field as it is. Every place in it is a holon called by a mount: a component given what it reads. Whatever a holon holds that points further is mounted in turn, by what it is, so the interface's holarchy is the field's, read through its types, and nothing in a component's code decides the shape of what another draws."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CX4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001CZE"},": the interface truly becomes a mirror of the field; carried from OpenLight's view, read again the same day. Built the same day: a brief's parts are a list of mounts, and the wildcard draws whatever nothing closer does.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CZ8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0000DK0"},"text":["2026-11-03"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001CZE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["The primitives themselves are still: they hold no state, take no press and move nowhere. Looking around is something built on them, and what it needs is a place to look and a way to move: the root mount, offered where the page's address says, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001D54"}," tells."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001D3K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001G6Q"},"text":["§8"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001D54","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-03: for the location of a brief it is always just one brief, unless it truly is an array, and then naturally a list; a mount sets an expression or a set, a location, and the component to render it, and that's it. The mount as a call, its argument as a selection, OpenLight's. Expressions were first given as holons, as OpenLight materialized every expression entering an argument; that bred a holon for every place looked at, and the author's word the same evening let it go: everything is simply everything, and expressions are not to be added where they are not needed.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001DEE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component draws its holon's own values, and opens a space for each value that points further: a reference is a mount of the holon it points at, and a list of references is a mount of the list component, whose every item is a mount in turn. What a value is, the holon's type says, since every connector has a shape, so the interface reads the type to know what to mount and where."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001DHY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component made of code may also compose by code, using other components inside its own, as OpenLight allows; only what it places as mounts are mounts. Where a holon's holarchy is meant to be seen and changed, its parts are mounts."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001DPY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-03: dissect the brief before plotting it out; mounts are made, and what renders within them depends; the reader probably not as code, preferably as layout, as data. Mounting by a connector's shape the session's reading; composition by code and by data, and the template's `$`, OpenLight's, where a template's arguments may be whole expressions over `$`; glass takes `$` alone until more is wanted. As built, each component still knows which of its values to mount, as the brief knows its parts; reading it from the type is not yet done.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001DRB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How a component is found is not settled. Glass now matches by type each time it draws. OpenLight ruled instead that the engine never infers a component: the one composing picks, from a table of defaults held in the field with the wildcard last, and the pick is recorded in the mount, so what is seen never depends on a table changing underneath. Mounts that are derived, such as a brief's parts, would be drawn through the table. Whatever is built on how a component is found is built knowing it may change, so finding a component is one function of the interface, the one place that would change."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001DZF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Switching is offered from the root mount's menu, as \"look here with\" each component that takes the place, for that one look. The override, the wildcard and switching the author's, 2026-11-03; the recorded pick OpenLight's ruling of 2026-08-23. Which glass takes the author does not know yet: \"if we do good code and good knowledge around these things, it's easy to switch later.\"*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001E32","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The contract the author's requirement, 2026-11-03: the held cannot decide for itself, for it would have to know everything that exists, so it must be a contract for that kind of communication; the vocabulary of kinds the session's; the kind as an offer, face unless offered full, the author's, the same day. Taken provisionally: \"we might be able to do with it for now\", the second decision whose rightness is not known, so anything built that depends on it is flagged before it is built.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001EDK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["As built: the kinds full and face are holons the field names; each component lists the kinds it draws, and a brief's one component draws itself both ways; the page offers full to the root mount, which offers full to what it gives."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001EGD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Built by the session, 2026-11-03, on the author's go. A slot's chrome, which turned a face into full or chose another component and kept it in the slot, was let go with the arrangement it wrote into; changing how a place is drawn is now changing the root mount, ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001EKG"},". Where a change to a slot inside a brief would be kept is still open, with the reader's own branch of a pulled store.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001EHT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001G6Q"},"text":["§8"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001EKG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Its reach is a ceiling: it reaches what it was handed, what that references and is an instance of, and what its own declared reads give back; reading a holon it was handed opens nothing further. It reads only by the forms it declares, each read one form and nothing beside it, and opens slots only for what it reaches, each held to the same ceiling; a template's mounts give only what the template was given, so they reach nothing new. A drawing that has been overtaken or closed can neither read nor open anything more. Anything else is refused by name, and every query and every list it opens is copied before it is judged, so what is judged is what is used. The reach is each slot's own: unlike OpenLight's, which narrows from parent to child with grants, a child's starts again from what its slot reads. This is a ceiling among components in one page, which keeps each honest about what it looks at; it is not isolation, for code in the page can reach everything the page can, which is why only glass's own components and the home's are run until components can run apart."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001FNF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a holder offers trickles down to everything beneath it, the nearer shadowing the farther, and a component is given it, and reaches what it names. A setting a component takes and its slot leaves unsaid is taken from what is offered under its name, where the offer fits; an offer is for everything beneath, so one that does not fit a component is passed by. So a setting chosen once, as a list's cards, is a mount's offer, and holds for whatever that mount draws."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001FVX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component is a pure function of what it is given and of the field: it draws again whole when what it read changes. What must last across a drawing lives in the slot's host, which stays while what is in it is drawn again."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001FYQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A list says nothing of what its items are, so a component that takes a type for its items, such as a timeline of a day's words, draws there only where a slot names it; otherwise one that takes nothing in particular is found. A full slot never draws in full a holon that a slot around it already draws in full; there it shows its face, so nothing stands inside itself without end. And a component a slot names that is not run, or cannot draw there, is said to be so in the slot, as OpenLight's \"not admitted here\", rather than quietly replaced, except where the nesting guard, not the slot, changed what was asked."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001G07","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reach, settings and typed bodies from OpenLight's view, read the same day; the session's reading of where glass went against it, mended after three fresh readings. The nesting guard adds to the slot contract, which is provisional; a template draws nothing of its own, so it adds nothing to the guard. Not yet built, having no use yet: acts beyond a component's own holon, and launching programs; Keeping a component's own state between drawings, as OpenLight's update does, is held open.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001G40","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-03: navigation needs a kind of history and is based on locations; the reader needs a way to see the actual location you are looking at and to be able to update it, for a face of it is not that helpful, and not by presets or raw text, but ontologically, naturally; the root holds the expression for what you are seeing, and changing it from the context menu's WYSIWYG is fine; the context menu has actual actions, made available by type matching; the history stack and the URL as an integration. Bubbling the session's proposal, which the author was open to; catching every press at the root was OpenLight's answer, not taken for granted. Programs, once they run, are where more of the menu's actions will come from. The address the author's, later that night: it still has to be real history; commits you can't reverse, so the browser's history is not walked by writing old versions again; the URL as the source of truth, either the expression broken apart in it or a history element; a parser is just a function, so the syntax can change later; a URL-adapted language, as URL-pragmatic as possible; ids need not be that big in an address. Functions are called by their titles until holons carry names of their own, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001HGA"}," tell. The search the author's, the same evening: expressions are ontology, every part has meaning; the formula said at the top, visualized and editable, a smart search across expressions, briefs and holons, narrowing by type to build an intersection, a made expression found by its name; favorites the reader looks for; a list's cards set by right-clicking it; and the search one common component, the context menu a very similar thing, its input everything or already narrowed. A setting as an offer the author's correction of the session's mount settings. Or as a join of the next part to the last let go the same night, as the author found it confusing; Or is built as any brick is. The bricks the author's, later that evening: say type, then Enter, and choose; all the Lego bricks, to add to an intersection and build an expression in place, not a plethora to search and select from. Plain words, a field and its value, and a mature feature set, the author's, the same night: what it is, by type, store rather than kept in. Only settings that are true or false are offered to set so far; a node-based builder for complex expressions is not built.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001H95","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00017N5"},"text":["the relations"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001HGA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Holding the client and its home, publishing is simple: a store is put on a static host as files, and a site is such a store with a client that comes pointed at it."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001HPZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A remote is a store served as plain files, and a site built on glass is one: the author's store on a static host, beside a page that loads the client pointed at it. Nothing on the host runs, so any host that serves files will do, and for now that is GitHub Pages, with nothing else to rely on."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001HR4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: not wanting to rely on more infrastructure than needed to get this going, and choosing GitHub Pages.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001HT3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01, answering the author's concern of putting commits on something that already contains commits.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001J5A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So the site is its field, whole and with its history, and anyone who points another client at its store reads the same field. The site installs no package and builds nothing; at most a Pages workflow file publishes it as it stands."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001J80","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Of three ways the session proposed on 2026-11-01, a package, a git submodule, or loading glass from where glass publishes itself, the author chose the third, for now.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001J9E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Last comes the address bar, which OpenLight never had: what a URL carries when the client is the whole application."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JFC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["With glass the domain delivers a client and its default store, and nothing more, so a URL says how to start the client, which store, which commit, what to mount, and where the reader looks. On the bare domain it carries nothing, and the client starts with its defaults."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JG3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: today the domain is everything; now the domain just hosts the client, and on the bare domain you see no `at` and no mount, because they are default loaded for you.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JHQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a URL may carry is what a chassis can be started with: a store to attach when it is not the default, a commit to pin a read to, and a mount to boot into; and beside them where one looks, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001JMA"},". Opened on the bare domain, the client takes the store it ships with and the entry that store holds, and the URL stays empty."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JJX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001JNV"},"text":["beneath"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JMA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The bare domain the author's, 2026-11-01; the flags carried from OpenLight's chassis: `--at`, `--entry`, `--mount`.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JN6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Whether glass will want anything like pages, with a whole other way of drawing behind a press, is left until there is a site to want it."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JRG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*On 2026-11-01 the author found a holon's address in the URL strange, and the root's versions were to be the history; ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001JT5"}," he took the URL as the source of truth, as it still has to be real history.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JSD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0000MCS"},"text":["late on 2026-11-03"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JT5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["A link carries where one looks and nothing of the reader's own: their favorites and settings stay in their home, so whoever opens it sees the same place drawn by their own root. Pinning a link to a commit, so it shows what was there however far the store has moved, is not yet written."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JTV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's, 2026-11-04, from what the address became; the first thought, a program writing a URL as an act of sharing, the session's of 2026-11-01, is no longer needed for where one looks.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JWN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01, from reading glass's first iteration against OpenLight; the parts and their order the session's.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JXS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The first thing the store holds is knowledge, this wiki among it, so how knowledge stands in the store and is read comes next."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JYD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The first thing glass's store holds is knowledge, starting with this wiki, so the first thing glass must do well is present it: along the gradient, the biggest understanding first and the rest beneath, never flat. The rule already says what knowledge is made of, and glass takes it as it stands."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001JZ8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: knowledge has to be presented, not in a flat manner, but along the gradient.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001K0Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Under [the rule](https://github.com/Cwejman/the-rule/blob/main/rule.md#3-what-knowledge-is-made-of) a brief is one piece of prose giving one understanding, and a brief with everything beneath it is a holon, so in the store a brief is a holon."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001K1M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What stands beneath it is ordered, each brief standing on those before it. Links are its free relations, and in the store a link points at a holon's identity, so it survives the holon moving. Some briefs keep their parts by time rather than by importance, like the author's words kept by day, and say so; the rule calls such a file a record, and glass reads it as a brief kept by time, its parts not numbered. Time-ordered knowledge is in time better held as typed holons with their time as a value, gathered and ordered by expression, as the relations say."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001K2Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried from the rule and its practice; the link by identity the session's, 2026-11-01.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001K63","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Some wholes carry an ontological weight that what stands beneath them shares: a domain, the workflows of an application, an audience. Such a brief says so in its own body, with a look of its own, an icon and a colour, and everything it holds, and everything beneath that, shows the look of each such whole above it, so a reader sees what a holon belongs to. A brief that does not say it is only a whole."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001K6N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["This is the brief's schema, not the substrate's: the substrate gives holding, and reads belonging upward through it, and the Brief type says what it is for a brief to mark what it holds, drawn by the components made for briefs. The brief is glass's own way of holding knowledge, a proposal and never fixed, so whoever holds knowledge otherwise may say it otherwise. A way of looking kept as a function is not a dimension but a favorite, the session's reading of the author's remark that such views are not strictly dimensions; whether it may carry a look as well is left until it is wanted."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001K97","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-04 and ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001KCY"},": in the holon for workflow, for domain, I want to say this is a dimension, all briefs under it part of it, with an icon, a colour; and really what we're doing is schema, the primitives are the primitives; the brief is the pilot's way, a proposal, meaning glass's own first way, and if someone wants to do something else, that's fine. Being a dimension said in the body rather than by a type or a second holon the session's, since unmarked a brief is still the same brief. How far a mark reaches is no question of the data: belonging is read upward through holding, as far as the expression that reads it says, the author's of 2026-11-05. Whether what is beneath may refuse a mark is open.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001KCP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0000381"},"text":["2026-11-05"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001KCY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05: Markdown is probably going to be replaced, and when it is, we're going native again; a standard native format for prose is what is truly agnostic, and the brief holds it and gives it its structure; native prose is not markdown and supersedes it, all markdown can be converted to native prose, but native prose would not be lossless in conversion to markdown. The files dropped once glass can show the files and their relation to the field, the author's, 2026-11-04; the first build's markdown the session's, 2026-11-01.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001KMN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A word may be only characters, its meaning left to be inferred, or a symbol, standing for something in the field. One that stands for something is a Term, a holon holding a reference to what it means, and is then a link of its own kind. Emphasis and its like are no reserved words either: an emphasised phrase is a holon whose type is Emphasis, and the material says how it looks."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001M3R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-05: words carry such meaning, words may be symbols; sometimes prose is just characters put together, and the meaning is to be inferred; when you want true ontological mapping, that very word is a word with a reference; bolding and the like are just reserved strings, whilst holons and types would be different. Term and Emphasis as types the session's, not yet ratified.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001M65","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The reader is what is wanted, as OpenLight held: a component that draws whatever a selection reaches, in every place it stands. The first build needs something smaller, enough to read this wiki from the store: one brief whole, then the briefs beneath it in order, each by its title and first paragraph, entered to read deeper, with links followed in place."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001MDQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The reader as what is wanted, and settling something small as the first goal, the author's, 2026-11-01; the small reader's shape the session's proposal.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001MFR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The catch-22 and the wish to put the spec in the store the author's, 2026-11-01; birthing it from the files the session's proposal, agreed in the outline. The files kept as the source the author's, 2026-11-02: no need to move from markdown and git prematurely.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001MR9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["With that held, the plan proposes what is built first, what waits, and what is still open."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001MSV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Proposed, the session's, 2026-11-01, on the author's call to settle something small as a clear goal; built 2026-11-03, on his word that the whole of what is to be built is now to be seen.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001MWA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Five steps, each standing on the one before, and none a shortcut: the reader is built on the interface, not in its place, and the wiki is born in once a person can really navigate it."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001MXH","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"on":"2026-11-03","status":"done","text":["**The store.** Its format written as test vectors that any implementation must pass: given objects, their canonical text and their names; given changes, the commits, indexes and versions they make. Then a writer and a reader that pass them. The store needs almost no code, and no language of its own."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001MYR","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"on":"2026-11-03","status":"done","text":["**The engine.** It attaches a store over HTTP, checks everything it fetches, keeps its own store for the home, and answers reads and commits in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001N1F"},", tested at its own layer with no interface."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N0J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001BG6"},"text":["the one protocol"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N1F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"on":"2026-11-03","status":"done","text":["**The interface.** Components as holons that declare the type they take, mounts as calls to them, layouts held as data, and a component enclosing what it is given and opening space in it for what matches, so ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001N36"}," assembles itself level by level. The chassis hosts it and decides nothing."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N1X","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00012YG"},"text":["the interface"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N36","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"on":"2026-11-03","status":"done","text":["**The reader component.** A component on that interface that draws a brief along the gradient, and ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001N4B"}," built from it: a person can move through the whole wiki, down into parts and back."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N3Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001MDP"},"text":["the first reader"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N4B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"on":"2026-11-03","status":"done","text":["**The wiki in the store.** This wiki born into a store as its first commit, each brief an instance of the brief type, whose fields are said in prose, so the store holds its own spec."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N50","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"text":["It is done when the author opens the page and navigates this wiki from the store, everything beneath it well made."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N68","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Proposed, the session's, 2026-11-01; the interface built properly before the reader, and the wiki born in once it can be navigated, the author's, ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001N7S"},": if there is no reason to shortcut, build it with quality.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N6Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0000VQD"},"text":["2026-11-02"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N7S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Tests come first at every layer, and the work is done by agents orchestrated to it, with rigour and freedom both: every finished piece is taken up by a new agent, fresh to it, who reads it from its own angle, and what that agent finds is mended before the next piece stands on it."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001N88","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-02: for every finished thing there always spawns a new agent to take its angle.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001NA1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine and the interface are written in TypeScript first. The store asks almost no code of any language, and the browser hashes natively, so nothing yet argues for another. The store's test vectors keep the door open: an engine in Rust compiled to WebAssembly, one engine for the browser and the author's machine with programs contained in it, can come later and pass the same tests without any store rewritten."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001NPH","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's recommendation, which the author saw no reason against, 2026-11-02.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001NRW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The components are written in TSX, so a component reads as the shape of what it draws. A small factory of glass's own turns the markup into the page's own elements, with no framework between: a component stays a function from what it is given to what it draws, drawn again whole when what it read changes, which asks for nothing a framework's reactivity would add."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001NSA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's, agreed by the author, 2026-11-03; OpenLight chose Solid.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001NVF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"status":"waiting","text":["**The fully immersive interface.** Editing in place, with the reader's own branch of a pulled store; what drew each holon, and why that component matched it, shown and edited where it stands; a context menu of actions; and the code and the JSON of anything readable where it is drawn, nothing locked away in a panel."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001NWY","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"status":"waiting","text":["**The home**, kept in the browser: what is attached, the entry, the root, and reset and clear as programs."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001NYV","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"status":"waiting","text":["**Runs, visible.** Runs kept in the home and drawn as they go, like an agent session; actions a component declares, such as adding a holon, that run a program; and the harness with its completion model and tools."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001NZK","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"status":"under way","text":["**Components as code and as data**: expressive components and layout components written as code, and components that are data, templates."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P0Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"status":"under way","text":["**The URL**, and sharing as an act."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P1Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"status":"waiting","text":["**OpenLight's reader**, with selections, intersection and many places."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P23","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"status":"waiting","text":["**Publishing**: glass's pinned builds on its own Pages, and the author's site as a store beside a client pointed at it."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P2G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"status":"waiting","text":["**The engine on the author's own machine**, the other engine and chassis."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P3A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"status":"waiting","text":["**Glass's components as a store** of their own."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P3V","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z","1M6YBY3G000001A"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Proposed, the session's, 2026-11-01; the immersive interface, visible runs and components as code and data are the author's, 2026-10-31.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P46","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Questions the first mark meets, and those beyond it, each to be settled when the work reaches it."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P4X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**How a component is found for a mount**: matched by type each time it draws, as now, or picked from a table of defaults and recorded in the mount, as OpenLight ruled, in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001P6Q"},". The author does not know yet; whatever is built on it is built knowing it may change."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P5J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001DVH"},"text":["the interface"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P6Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["**What kind a slot is**: a contract between holder and held over a vocabulary of kinds, full and face, with the slot's own data first, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001P8C"}," proposes. Taken provisionally; the author does not know it is right."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P7E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001E57"},"text":["the interface"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P8C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["These two, how a component is found and what kind a slot is, are decisions whose rightness is not known: whatever would be built depending on either is named before it is built, so the author can weigh it."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001P8V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The material.** How things look is held in the field as a holon of its own, a style sheet of named colours, type and spacing that every component draws with, so the chassis holds no style. It was built on 2026-11-03, named from the author's word for what one builds in; whether this decoupling serves, and whether the word should mean that or something wider, he does not know yet."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PA5","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Provenance.** A published commit says nothing of the run that made it, so only the runner's home knows; whether published history should say how it was made."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PFD","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Events as holons.** Thousands of visits nobody edits or points at may be better as rows within one holon each day."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PGD","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**How a read is asked.** Glass reads by identity and by expressions of its functions; whether the engine plans an expression as one request, as OpenLight's does, is open."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PHT","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The wholes of the field**, left open by the author on 2026-11-04 and gathered in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001PN2"},": a single owner, how a bare name is found."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PMF","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001967"},"text":["the relations"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PN2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Who published, provably**: keys and signatures on what a store's ref points at."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PQ4","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**When the shape of kept state changes**, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001PR2"}," says."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PQP","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001CSV"},"text":["the home"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PR2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Beneath it all lies where glass comes from: OpenLight, the rule, and glass's own first iteration, built and then cleared."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PS1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass comes from two of the author's works and one attempt of its own. OpenLight gave the vision and most of the architecture, the rule gave the shape knowledge takes, and glass's first iteration, built and cleared in three days, showed what building ahead of the architecture costs."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PSR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-10-30 to 2026-11-01.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PVB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["[OpenLight](https://github.com/Cwejman/OpenLight) claims that completion should happen from a point in a field, not from a pasted transcript. When knowledge, programs and interfaces live as typed, versioned structure in one medium, programs compound, interfaces build on primitives as data does, and the field keeps everything. Its specs, many hours of thinking about what is wanted, name the engine, the chassis, the view and the reader that glass carries."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PVM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass is its successor, written in a different spaciousness. The author began OpenLight with a context window of at most two hundred thousand tokens and very different models; writing it, he met many details that do not matter. Glass assembles a core set of primitives, done with quality, aligned with OpenLight's vision."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PXW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-10-30, 2026-10-31 and 2026-11-01; OpenLight's claim carried from its README.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001PZM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Read in OpenLight's specs, 2026-11-01.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001Q2D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["OpenLight's pilot was a desktop window, with no address bar; glass is first a client in a browser, so the URL needs an answer. The store as a remote was on OpenLight's horizon, as the object model to come; glass begins with it. And knowledge, which OpenLight deferred, comes first, laid by the gradient the rule found after OpenLight's specs were written."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001Q2P","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01; the URL as new the author's.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001Q4R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["[The rule](https://github.com/Cwejman/the-rule) is the author's law for knowledge: the biggest understanding first, each breaking down into smaller ones, as briefs in a holarchy joined by links. Its last section reaches past prose, to a medium where programs meet by matching, a model's context is a selection from the medium, and the harness dissolves, and it names OpenLight as where that is pursued."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001Q56","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["This wiki is written under the rule, and the store's first content is knowledge, so glass is also where the rule's medium is first lived beyond markdown and git."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001Q78","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Carried from the rule, sections 1, 3 and 6; the rule as how we embody things the author's, 2026-10-30.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001Q87","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["From 2026-10-30 to 2026-11-01 glass was built ahead of its architecture: a SQLite field, an engine that was also the web server, Solid components drawing the field, every visit kept as a holon, editing in place, and runs. Much of it was faked until made, and on 2026-11-01 it was cleared, kept in this repository's git history rather than carried."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001Q8Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What it showed is in this wiki, each part as the decision it led to. The engine served pages and spoke to the interface directly, with no protocol between them, and now the client holds the engine. Runs were written into the field that would be published, and now they belong to the home. Choosing another component rewrote the published layout, and now layout is partitioned to the reader. And tabs and views were added that the author never asked for."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QAX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: a lot about glass is fake till you make it, and the tabs he never asked for; the lessons drawn are the session's reading of what was built.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QDM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then the work itself, told over its commits as it happened, until the store can hold it."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QEP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Begun 2026-11-02, on the author's word that the effort be noted in the log as the work goes. Each story reasoned by the session that did the work, from the commits and the author's words.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QH9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What was said left the wiki to stand as a root of its own, the wiki's flow still showing its face by pointing, so the wiki holds knowledge alone. The union was let go, since nothing read it and the probe finds the roots itself. This session was kept in brief at the author's word, and with it the voice it signed its stale marks in."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QJJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Of the 64 roots the main store had, 53 were pieces nothing had been made to hold. What already pointed said where each belonged: a source holds what stands upon it, a session its sources, condensations and voice, and the paper's licence the permission it grants. The sessions went under one holder, and the statistics and functions under another. The union now lists the roots as they are."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QMS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The paper and its readings were named as the main store was, so a title is a name in all three stores and no slug stands beside one. The control character the reading of the PDF left before 42 headings did not come with them, and no word of the paper changed."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QQ3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Files gone, the author weighed what a brief still is. A boundary stays a deliberate act: a brief mounted in the flow of another is a break, as starting a file was, and is mounted as anything is. Its sections read through after the flow, and nothing follows them, since nothing can follow a heading and not belong to it. Whether to show a face was not computed from what fits, for a document may be meant to be read through. A title became the holon's name, with no slug beside it. Bar and address were left to common sense: results as one types, from a buffer, the address moved on Enter."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QRV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a session left uncommitted was kept, and no session is to start on local changes. Briefs the work has overtaken were measured stale rather than rewritten, each mark saying what no longer holds and what still does, and the README says what comes next."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QWK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The marks on the author's record became measures of what it adds to the briefs, the record itself was measured so a reader need not read it whole, and the measures that only repeated their threads were let go. The record stays as it is."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QY4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Each session and the highlights within it were measured, so that a new session can read the measures and reason about what to read, with no flag and no conclusion drawn for it."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001QZN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The author's record was gone over the way a person marks a book, with curiosity rather than as one who knows what is good, and few were kept: what is not to be forgotten and no brief owns yet. Each mark is a measure on a whole or on a range of its parts, graded, with a note in the margin."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001R0S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What the author's own words hold and no brief owns was read by four agents with curiosity, and held as threads pointing at the sentences it was said in, each measured as not yet owned by the build structure. The session itself was kept as it was said, and the author's words on measures measured as verbatim."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001R2T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["History and the plan's steps became data: each a step, with where it stands, when, what it comes after and the commits that carried it. The briefs keep their prose, and each step after this one is added as data."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001R4Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A mark split at its space was made whole, the words a first write left behind were taken out, and the lexemes a fork had kept apart were folded into the lexicon."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001R63","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A fork read the web appropriately: feeds, relays, licences and elevating others, its prompts kept and its answers condensed. Claims, following, permission, voice and condensation were imagined as types before the interface."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001R76","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The paper was held one to one as holons beside its PDF and its licence, and the readings built upon it became a store of their own. The licence read anew says both may be public, and the union reads the three stores as one."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001R8A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A second session was born beside the first, and glass was named an operating system. Its utterances were kept word by word, with its paths of evolution, and two forks met it: one on selection and layering, one on the paper's licence."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001R9V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The wiki, the types, the lexicon and the second session were born into the store as packs, in 81 slices in the order things came. The packs became the store, and the birth from markdown ended: the holons are the source now."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001RB9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Asked for the right open-ended way to dimensions, the session first made a dimension a holon of its own with a gathering expression, and the author found it a take without reasoning: a brief that is a dimension would need a twin. Reasoned again, being a dimension is what a brief's own body says, with a look, marking all it holds, and the author saw it is knowledge schema, the brief only the pilot's proposal, and nothing the substrate must know."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001RCQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then how Markdown is replaced. Prose became a list of typed elements, its three links three types, its parts read from the flow and its confidence line a paragraph of its own type, with Markdown only its text form."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001RFB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The author asked what is lost if this is all one body, whether words should be addressable, and whether reserved names are what remain; the answer was a holon's interior, elements shaped as holons at a smaller scale, each with a local id and a type of its own, pointed into from outside."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001RGN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Reading a piece of the store brief written that way, he took a holon's name out of its body to stand beside its identity, and a type's fields with it, and found it double that a holon is a type both by being an instance of Type and by having fields. None of it is built. Decided: dimension as brief schema, the name and the fields out of the body, nested lists, the confidence line as prose."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001RJC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then he ratified the interior, the type of types let go, and mould, for now, as the word for what a type gives its instances, and set Markdown right: native prose supersedes it, and is not its text form."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001RMX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Pressed further, he found that a prose list typed to hold only typed things made the interior a primitive of its own, and asked whether, since an act should be kept at the fidelity of the act, the elements should not be holons, the whole their namespace. The session, which had argued for the interior, found its reasons wrong or not telling, and said so when he asked what had shifted; prose became holons held by their brief, values within them, and the interior went. What a holon per paragraph costs is to be measured, and leads into the index."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001RP6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
