{"body":{"text":["Asked to show plainly how a brief is drawn, the session laid it out, and the author saw the kind of a slot as a holon passed down as an offer: face unless a parent offers full. The interface was aligned to it: the page offers full to the arrangement, a layout to its panes, a brief and a list offer face to what they hold, and a slot's own word comes first. Slots are now opened at a single `where`, an id, several, or an expression, and a brief opens its parts as what it holds under parts. The record type, a bad name for knowledge kept by time, gave way to a brief that says its parts are kept by time; such knowledge is likely to become typed holons in time."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001SS3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
