{"body":{"text":["Seeing the field laid out, the author found the entry went straight into the wiki, which is not the root, and asked how the hierarchy truly exists in the field. It does not, as a hierarchy: every holon stands flat in the store, and nesting lives only in bodies. He then laid out the interface as he sees it: a place, a mount on it, and what renders there depending on what it is, one brief at a brief's place, a list only where something truly is a list, and a wildcard for whatever nothing closer draws, which a layout can always override. The session read OpenLight's view again and found one point glass departs from, how a component is found, which the author left open. The interface was then built so: the entry stands at the field, a type shows its fields and instances, a brief's parts are a list of mounts, and the wildcard draws any holon by its values."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001TEK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
