{"body":{"text":["The author asked whether keeping classes was still the session's reasoning, and said not to hold to how things were coded before. Every class went: stores, backends, the engine, the connection and the interface are each made by a function, and the store was split by what it is, checked objects, the tree and the store, and the interface into the arrangement, the drawing, the materials and the mount. The session then began writing the core as dense expressions, and the author said it was thinking too bluntly at the top and the bottom: understanding comes from good structure, so one need not shadow code before it settles, and blank lines matter. The core was written again as plain steps with names and room, the whole kept in one form, and a fresh agent read it as a newcomer. It found the components' contract without a home, nested choices, a wall in the drawing, a comment no longer true, the tree's rule told twice, and helpers in the wrong files, and each was mended."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001TM5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
