{"body":{"text":["Asked whether classes and imperative code matter, the author answered that the material one builds in goes into everything: every component, the code and the styling. The engine's core became a pure field value, plain data with the stores' past asked for by its own name, and the engine a thin shell that keeps the field as it stands and takes acts in turn. The birth became functions of what its files hold, with the reading and writing kept at the edge. The material, the colours, type and measure everything is drawn with, became a holon in the field, laid by the interface, and the chassis page holds no style of its own. A fresh agent then read all of it for how it reads; it found the field still holding stores, a comment saying the interface holds nothing, one cast written ten times, two pairs of colliding names, and styles going around the material, and each was mended."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001TT3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
