{"body":{"text":["On 2026-11-03 a subagent weighed glass as a name against OpenLight's own naming: it serves this iteration, and would not pass as a public name, being an everyday word held already by Apple and Google, and in OpenLight's reasoning a word for what has no structure. The author then asked whether code and markdown were mixing at the root. The session first proposed gathering the field and the vectors into the code, then, asked to reconsider, found the root holds real kinds side by side: the knowledge, the field, the contract, the code and the site. It went on to say code would one day leave the files for the field, which the author did not see the point of: code stays as files in git, its source and history, and is born into the field. The briefs that leaned that way were reworded."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001TZJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
