{"body":{"text":["The author asked whether OpenLight's relates was worth anything, and then asked the same of ownership. A first run of subagents went ahead of him and away from what he could follow, so he forked the session back to before it and reasoned it through himself: OpenLight is built bottom up, knowledge either explains its connections in prose or has typed fields, and namespace is only the possibility of where."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001VS4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["He then asked for wide simulations, and six were run, each a whole field across stores rather than one case at a time. They converged: a holon stores its identity, what it is an instance of and its body; every other relation is a reference in a body, seen without types; whoever can write holds the relation, which across stores is always one's own home; and part and whole are read from the whole's body. Ownership, relates and a universal membership were let go. One whole simulated field was written out as chunk-script data for him to read, where he renamed a run's `came` to its result."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001VVD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
