{"body":{"text":["The author spoke of a web of gradient knowledge, programs and code ontologically connected rather than hung off the briefs, and asked the session to lead. The session proposed that a type's contract be written in language as well as structure, and he agreed: a holon's fields are the contact points for prose, the connectors where holons meet into a larger ontology. That is now in the type primitive, and in the grounds that code is looked upon as built on the primitives."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001W58","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
