{"body":{"text":["On 2026-11-03 a subagent weighed glass as a name against OpenLight's own naming: it serves this iteration, and would not pass as a public name, being an everyday word held already by Apple and Google, and in OpenLight's reasoning a word for what has no structure. The author then asked whether code and markdown were mixing at the root. The session first proposed gathering the field and the vectors into the code, then, asked to reconsider, found the root holds real kinds side by side: the knowledge, the field, the contract, the code and the site. It went on to say code would one day leave the files for the field, which the author did not see the point of: code stays as files in git, its source and history, and is born into the field. The briefs that leaned that way were reworded."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001WAX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned on 2026-11-03 by the session.*"]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001WFK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Asked what comes next, the session proposed building the first mark in one orchestrated run, with the store as language-free test vectors and the engine in TypeScript. The author saw no reason against TypeScript, since the store asks almost no code, and asked whether a reader before the interface was a shortcut. It was. The plan now builds the interface primitive before the reader, births the wiki only once it can be navigated, and has every finished piece taken up by a fresh agent from its own angle. A misheard word first took TypeScript out, and Rust in; the author set it right, and TypeScript stands, with Rust kept possible by the vectors."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001WFX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["On 2026-11-01 the author turned glass back to its architecture: no faking until making, the engine in the client, the store glass's own object model served as files. The first iteration was cleared and this wiki written in its place, outlined first, read by fresh heads, and then read by the author, who named the store and the engine as primitives."]},"id":"1M6YBY3G0001WKN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
