{"body":{"text":["Text in a store is JSON in one canonical form, so the same content is always the same text. A block of versions is named by the SHA-256 hash of its text, and a commit by the hash of its line, and whoever fetches either hashes it again and knows it is what was asked for. A commit lists the blocks it wrote, and each commit names the one before it, so the ref proves everything behind it."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E064","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G000148N"},"text":["its identity"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E06Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["A holon is not named by what it holds, since what it holds changes. It has an id given at birth, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YC9SH5T5E06Y"}," tells."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E071","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store holds three kinds of thing: the ref, the log of commits, and the blocks of versions. Reading the latest of anything walks them from the top, and costs the ref, one volume of the log and one block."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E08D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The three as they stand the session's, 2026-11-08; the index and its tree, and the packs, are in git's history.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E094","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A commit is one change to the field, whole, and one line of the log. It says when it was made and what it says of itself, the hash of the line before it, the blocks it wrote, the first id and how many of the new holons each holds, the holons it gave a new version, and those it took out. It holds no contents. Following the lines back walks the whole history of the field, one change at a time, with nothing but the log fetched."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E0DQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The table is not kept apart from the log. Each log volume opens with it whole, a checkpoint, and the lines after say what changed since, so a client reads the ref and one volume and knows where everything stands. A volume closes at about 64 KB, which keeps that small. Past about 5,000 commits the hashes of small blocks are what grow; folding them together would answer it, and changes no id, so that is left until it is wanted."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E0P3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-02: a smart index rather than one that bloats, done right from the start; its first shape, a tree, the session's, left to it by the author, and built 2026-11-03. The table and its checkpoints the session's, 2026-11-08, after a log fetched whole was attacked as the worst way to grow.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E0QY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["At the conversion of 2026-11-08 each store's holons were given ids anew in place order, so a whole sits together. Each old ULID and its id are in `conversion/ids.json`, which no reader needs."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E0W9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Counted ids were chosen first, and let go the same day: the author would not have a store that could not be taken away and brought back, and short unique ids cost about 10% more in the field, gzipped. The session's, 2026-11-08; a ULID before it, the session's, 2026-11-03.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E0XY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00017N5"},"text":["the relations"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E0Z3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["A holon carries its own name, in its version beside its identity, and it is unique only among what one whole holds; an address is to be a route of names through wholes, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YC9SH5T5E0Z3"}," tell. A store keeps no map of names: what a name gives is found by reading the holons. `entry`, the mount a client boots into, is a holon of glass's store so named."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E108","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The store as the namespace the author's, 2026-11-02; a holon's own name the author's, 2026-11-04. The one map of names was let go with the index, 2026-11-08, its last state kept in the conversion line. Routes are not built.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E11J","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A version holds what the store needs and the holon's body: its id, the block holding the version before it, what it is an instance of, and, where it has them, its name and its mould. The body is whatever the holon holds itself, shaped by its types. Versions are the atoms: they stand one to a line in a block, and everything else in the store only points at them."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E13X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-02: a holon is what the storage needs and then its body, and title and prose go into the body. `kind` was let go with the packs, 2026-11-08: every line in a block is a version.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E157","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A holon is a type by having a mould, the fields its instances hold, each with its prose and the shape the engine checks. It is an instance of nothing to be one, and the type of types is let go."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E16K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-05: name first class; fields goes out of the body, for whether you are a type by being an instance of Type or by having fields was double; yes, we drop the type type; mould, for now, for a cast, but a cast for children, not for its own fields.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E18B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Changing one holon writes a new version of it in a new block, whose `prev` is the hash of the block before, then appends one line to the log, and writes the ref last."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E19G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Nothing old is touched. The block that held the old version still holds it, and the table simply points past it, so the past stays whole. A reader fetching that block for a neighbour receives the old version with it, which costs bytes and never a wrong read; a whole whose edits have scattered it can be placed together again by an ordinary commit."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1BQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A change may also take holons out of the field: they are listed as gone from that commit on, while every version they had stays, read from the commits before."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1CQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field's history is read along the log: each line one change. A holon's history is read from version to version, following `prev` from block to block: every state it has had, whichever acts made them. Both are in the store, and each is fetched only when asked for."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1EC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A commit fixes the whole field by one hash. The field as it stood after it is had by folding the log up to it from the nearest checkpoint, so a reader pinned to it could see exactly what was there, however far the store has moved since."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1FZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Proved at the conversion of 2026-11-08: the field drawn again at each of 147 old commits, every holon matching. Pinning a read through the engine is not yet written.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1H1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A first visit needs no bundle. Ids follow place, so a whole sits together, and a block is fetched whole, so a host can gzip it: the wiki's first page costs about 94 KB of gzipped files, where the packs cost hundreds of requests for one brief. A question about everything fetches every block, about 1.2 MB, once. A client keeps each block by its hash, so a host giving every file a new tag at each publish causes nothing to be fetched again."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1KZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*A bundle for the first visit the session's, 2026-11-01, let go with the objects it bundled. Measured by size and on this machine, 2026-11-08, never on a slow network. The way down to a brief asks about everything, so today a first visit fetches the rest soon after its words.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1NP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["On disk and on a host, a store is a directory:"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1P3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Lines of JSON are no matter of git. A block is many small texts travelling as one file, so a host can gzip it, a reader can split it by lines, and anyone can search it with nothing but a text editor. A store leaves git as easily as it came."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1QW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The format is fixed by test vectors anyone can run, in any language: canonical texts with their hashes, and commits applied to an empty store with every byte each writes. They are made apart from glass's own code, named by the system's own hasher."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1SB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01; the layout as it stands, 2026-11-08.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1SR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a store is, written as cases any implementation must pass, in any language. An implementation that writes these bytes and reads them back is writing glass's store; nothing else about it matters."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E1TW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
