{"body":{"text":["*The name beside the identity the author's, 2026-11-05. Whole pieces the author's, from the grant; part of the field his, 2026-11-02: everything is part of the field; that holons have ids and history his, 2026-11-01 (\"holons have to have ids I think and have to have commits\"); the shape of versions the session's, laid out in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YC9SH5T5E21H"},".*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E21N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00014EB"},"text":["the store"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E22X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-05: fields goes out of the body; being a type both by being an instance of Type and by having fields was double, so yes, we drop the type type; mould for now. Built, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YC9SH5T5E22X"}," tells.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E231","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The primitives are still: they hold no state, take no press and move nowhere. Looking around the field is built on them, as one mount the reader keeps in their home, offered where the page's address says each time they look elsewhere."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E24E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00017N5"},"text":["beneath"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E255","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Two more stand beside them, out of the body, since the engine reads them whatever a holon's type: its name, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YC9SH5T5E255"},", and, for a type, its mould, what its instances hold. The body is then only what a holon holds itself."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E25W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The store says it, and the engine reads it: Children of, Parents of and the field's roots read holding alone, the roots being what nothing holds, and Points to and Pointed from read the rest."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E271","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's, 2026-11-04, from the code; built 2026-11-08.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E27C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["In a brief written as Markdown, a link standing alone in a paragraph placed a part there, with the sentence before it saying why, and a link inside a sentence only mentioned. That was a convention read from the text, not a reference the store knew, and it lasted as long as briefs were files. Prose is holons now, so a part is a reference that holds."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E29N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A reference points at a holon's identity, so it follows the holon as it changes. It could be pinned to one version, so it keeps saying what it said, as a note pinning the version of the brief it was written against; no reference is pinned yet."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E2B7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass works on top of JSON rather than in it: a syntax of its own laid on objects, so it could be specified without JSON at all, JSON being one way to write it down. Inside a body, what is glass's is known by a leading `$`, and everything else is the holon's own: a reference is `$ref`, says it holds by `$holds`, and would be pinned by `$at`. A version's own places, its id, instance, name and body, and a mould's words, are the store's and carry no `$`."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E2E7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's, 2026-11-05, answering the author's nested universes that you don't clutter unless you care for them. Built, further than it says, down to the word. What it costs a client was measured on 2026-11-08: a whole is one read, and the wiki's first page about 53 KB gzipped.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E2K8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A holon may carry a name of its own, kept beside its identity rather than in its body; its title is that name, and no slug stands beside it. The name is the holon's, not given by whoever holds it, so it is the same in every whole that holds it, and each whole asks only that what it holds be unique by name. Two holons named `Type` can stand in the field, a function and the component that draws a type, never in one whole."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E2P2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A brief's prose is a list of references that hold, each to a holon: a Paragraph, a List, a Quote, Code, or a holon of a kind no one has thought of yet, drawn by the component its type finds, so whoever adds a kind adds what draws it and nothing else changes. A reference that only points stands among them too, a holon shown from its own tree and not made a part, so Brief's mould leaves holding unsaid for its prose and each reference says it for itself, by `$holds`. The rule's practice has three links: one in a sentence, which mentions; a lone link, standing in a paragraph of its own, which places a part; and a quoted lone link, which shows a brief from its own tree. So the practice's lone link is a reference that holds, and its quoted lone link one that points. A brief's sections are not read from its flow: they stand in its `parts`, read through after it, and nothing follows them."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E2VM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Within a holon of prose is what is not typed: its sentences, each its words, and among them a link to where they lead, an emphasis or a strong. A List holds its items, each a Paragraph or another List, so lists nest as holons hold holons. Code is a string, and a real file is a holon from an integration, placed like any other."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E2XS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-05: you can place anything, any holon, and by placing it you place the reference, and it becomes a mount; a list of anything means any JSON can be typed and things can't be matched, so it has to say its contents are interior holons, which is a new primitive, a critique that led to prose as holons; the list has to contain a holon, and that holon may take another list; nesting of bullet points, there's nothing wrong with that; for code we start with a string, and real files are another component you mount anyway. Part and Card as one reference that holds or points his too: it is just a mount that either holds or points. Prose held as holons the session's; the flow and its sections, 2026-11-08.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E321","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The store holds these, each said here by what it holds:"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E32E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Term, Image and Ground were drafted and not born. The author wondered whether a paragraph is only spacing in a list; Paragraph is kept for what the rule makes it, one point, so a paragraph is a thing of its own and not the space between. A ground stands in the flow as a paragraph of emphasis, which allows one after each claim as this wiki writes them."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E34Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-05: we need to confirm the spec of the types we declare for prose before we can let it go for implementation; ground, I thought it is per brief. Drafted by the session; what was born, as the store holds it, 2026-11-08.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E366","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The prose of a brief was one piece of markdown, its parts placed by a link standing alone in a paragraph, a reading convention the store did not know. Prose is native now: holons the store holds, each typed, down to the word, the links among them references the store sees. Native prose supersedes markdown: any markdown can be read into it, and it cannot be written back to markdown without loss. What markdown's surface held is kept apart, as holons of its own, under wiki-markdown."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E392","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Built again on prose as holons, it is one component drawing a brief two ways: in full, with the way down to it, its name, its flow with anything in it that is not prose drawn as a face, and its sections read through beneath; and as a face, by its name and first paragraph. Its words are one read, however many holons they are, with no slot for each. A link into the field places the reader there; a link to the web stays a link; one to where the field cannot reach, such as a git commit, is shown as text, and so is an image, which is never fetched, since fetching it would tell whoever serves it who reads."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E3D0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Built by the session, 2026-11-03, and again 2026-11-08; the record type let go on the first of those days for a brief kept by time, the author finding \"record\" a bad name and time-ordered knowledge likely superseded by typed holons.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E3EB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Each step is built, tested, read by a fresh agent and mended, twice now: on the first store of 2026-11-03, and on the blocks of 2026-11-08:"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E3KE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What waited after the first mark, as it was proposed then, kept as a record. The packs and then the blocks came first, which it does not name, and the home, the URL, components as data and much of OpenLight's reader have since been built, at least in part. What comes next is in the root README."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E3ZP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Merging**, when two lines of commits meet: a copy written apart now lands on another, its blocks unchanged, and stops if both changed one holon. How two people decide between them is a question for peers."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E410","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Open, 2026-11-01; those since settled, prose made native and the mould, taken out 2026-11-08.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E42A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How glass came to be what it is, told over its commits, newest first, each day by the runs of work it held, with the commits standing beneath as leaves. It moved into the store with everything else, and each step since is told in its commits and its sessions as well as here."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E443","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["On 2026-11-08 the format was settled by attack: six agents reasoned about it apart and tried to break what was joined, and the store went from packs to blocks and a log, each of 91,284 versions proved to its old hash and the field drawn again at all 147 old commits. Counted ids were chosen and let go in a day, when the author would not have a store that could not be taken away and brought back. Then the engine, the interface and the tools were rewritten upon one implementation of it, what the client ships became a store of its own, and three fresh readings each found real faults, which were mended."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E47X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's, in brief: a fifth session, under Sessions.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E48A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Anything a component opens for something it holds is a slot, what stands in a brief's flow as much as a list's items: a slot is a mount, opened where what it reads stands, one holon by its id, or several by theirs; what an expression gathers is opened as those holons. Whether what stands in it is drawn whole or as its face is settled by a contract between the one that holds and the one held, which share only a small vocabulary, the kinds of slot, held in the field as holons: *full* and *face* to begin with."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E4BK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The kind travels as an offer, as OpenLight's offers do: a holder offers it to the slot it opens and to everything beneath, the nearest offer shadowing the farther, and where nothing offers, a holon shows its face. The page offers full to the root mount, and a mount to what it gives; a brief offers face to what stands in its flow, and reads its sections through itself, so its fullness never trickles into what it shows; a list offers face to its items. Each component says which kinds it draws, and the slot is drawn by the component for its holon's type that draws its kind, else by the wildcard, which draws every kind. Neither looks at the other: the holder never inside what it holds, the held never at what holds it."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E4FZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A slot's own word comes before any offer: a template's mount says its kind."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E4GF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component is made of code, or of data. As data it is a template: mounts held in order, each giving what the component itself is given, in the kind of slot it says, by the component it names or else the one found. The reader is such a component: the search, saying where one stands, above what it is given, drawn in full, the ground where more ways of looking can stand beside it."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E4WY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A mount can name its component, and then that one draws, whatever else would. Otherwise one is found for it: one whose types the holon is an instance of, or else the wildcard, which takes any holon and draws it as its values, so nothing in the field is ever left undrawn. Switching to another available component is for that one look, said in the page's address."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E4Z6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component declares itself in its own module, beside its code: what it is, the types it takes and the kinds of slot it draws in, by their names, what it is given, the settings it takes, each said in prose with its shape as a type declares its fields, and the reads it makes beyond what it is handed. What a slot gives is checked against the settings before the component draws. A component is then given what its slot reads, and its reads answered with the shape their form gives."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E5HS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It is told what it may do, as OpenLight delivers reach facts rather than have a component work them out: whether it may write the holon it was given. That one act, a new version of its own holon, in one commit with any new holons it comes to point at, born in the home, is all a component may do so far, but for a mount the reader may write, which may also move, to a new address; what it brings into being is never a component, since a component in the home is run, and a holon may be written where it is the reader's, in the home, or the entry while it is still the root, which the first write makes the reader's own; once the reader has a root of their own, the entry is only shown."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E5P9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A press does not need catching from above. Every slot says where it is: its element carries the holons it reads as its location, and a link in prose carries the one it mentions. A press rises through the page from where it landed, past those locations, to whatever holds them and cares. The mount component cares, where the reader may write it: a press inside it finds the innermost location it passed, and the mount moves there, drawn by the component the entry calls, the reader. A press where one already stands moves nowhere. The brief that was pressed never knows it was read; a mount that may not be written lets a press rise on."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E63A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The secondary press rises the same way, and the mount lays the same search where it landed, given the place pressed, the component it is drawn by, and the settings its slot gave, so what can be done there is found as anything is. The place was drawn, not held, so the menu changes nothing of it: its parts are said from here, not changed or let go, and what is built from them is looked at instead. It offers to look there, a holon or a way of looking alike; to look there with each other component that takes it, for that one look; to set what that component takes and nothing gave it, as cards for a list or for a grouping's collections, which the mount then offers to all it draws; a face stands in what holds it, as an item in a list, so its settings to set are its own and its holder's; to keep a way of looking on the favorites, born then as a function of one's own that takes nothing and gives it, which opens in the search as what it gives, so its parts can be seen and changed, or to place a holon there or take it off. The search is what the mount is offered as its search, and the favorites what it offers, so both are the reader's to change, as data."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6AS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A client reads a remote the way the store is laid out: the ref, then the open log volume, then the blocks it needs, each checked against its hash. Blocks never change, so a client keeps them for good; the ref and the log are fetched fresh."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6CB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Every block is plain lines of JSON at an address of its own, so anyone can also read a holon's data directly, without a client, knowing which block holds it. And since any client may attach any store, a remote is served with the headers that let other sites read it. GitHub Pages was measured on 2026-11-08, with synthetic files: it gzips every file type tried, `.jsonl` among them, lets any origin read them, and showed a publish about 21 seconds after it was pushed."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6F8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00010GT"},"text":["2026-10-30"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6FR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01; data fetched directly as JSON was the author's wish on ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6FR"},".*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6FW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["To publish is to upload the blocks the remote does not have, which is always safe since the same block is always the same file, then the log, and then to move the ref, but only if it still names the commit the publisher started from. If someone else moved it first, nothing is lost: the publisher's commits land on theirs, chained on again with no block changed, and if both changed one holon, landing stops and asks."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6JF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01; said again for blocks, and landing built, 2026-11-08.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6JY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store kept in a git repository costs little extra, because its blocks are files only ever added. A publish is a git commit that adds new blocks and a line of the log and changes the ref, and git keeps each block once. What git's history adds is a log of when things were published, not a second copy of the field's history."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6N2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Git is only what carries it. Nothing in the format needs it: a store is plain files, so it serves from any host, and lives as well in a browser's storage, as the home does."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6P8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Objects stayed loose at first, then were packed, then blocks; said again 2026-11-08.*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6PS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The code stays where it is written, as files kept in git, and that is its source and its history. Made into the field, it is a holon the engine can match and the interface can run and show; being in the field does not take it out of the files."]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6TN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0000D9X"},"text":["2026-11-03"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6VK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Reasoned, the session's, 2026-11-01; a direction then, built 2026-11-08. That code is kept as files in git and born into the field, not moved into it, the author's, ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6VK"},".*"]},"id":"1M6YC9SH5T5E6VQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-05: we do not work in JSON, we work on top of JSON, creating our own syntax upon objects having reserved internal fields; perhaps id is one such thing, just like references are; one could spec the JSON without the JSON. The `$` for all of them, and the names `$at` and `$holds`, the session's proposal; `$holds` is built.*"]},"id":"1M6ZTEEYXFFP01Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Built by the session, 2026-11-03, and again 2026-11-08; the handles from the author's word of that day: you can always send in a reference on the way. A whole to a depth and a set's level, the session's, 2026-11-09.*"]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG405N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine shows some things as places that are not holons in any store: a store's commits, whether a store is behind the host it was fetched from. Commits are objects in the store, but they are not holons, and the engine draws them as a place when one is read. Such a place reads and draws like any other and holds nothing of its own."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG407V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: the engine sometimes projects things, like commits, which are not things in the field per se. Projected places are OpenLight's. What is attached became holons kept in the home, 2026-11-09.*"]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG408Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0000GBX"},"text":["2026-11-03"]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG40FV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M72MZCW4XG40FV"},": there is no state, no interaction and no navigation in the primitives, and that is something to birth upon them; the root should be an actual reading, not a custom component. That the entry once stood at the field itself as a projection, drawn by a component of its own, is let go in it. The entry giving what is attached, everything reached from it by reference, and the bare address the author's, 2026-11-09: the root is a mount, and of course you mount stores at the root;/ should just give the root; a brief loaded by itself sounds like custom glue.*"]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG40K4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A mount is a component and what it is given: a location, holons in order, its argument; or a way of looking, an expression held in the mount itself. One holon is drawn as itself; several, which truly are a list, are drawn as a list, by the list component; a way of looking, as what it gathers. An expression is born as a holon of its own only where it is kept, on the favorites; a way of looking kept so, given to a mount, is looked through. A component says what it is given, one holon, a list, a selection, either, or a way of looking, with the list it gathers, so the list component is found for a list and for a way of looking alike: given a way of looking, a list draws what it gathers, and, where it groups, its collections first, each a way of looking seen as a face by the collection component, closed as a card with the value it narrows to and how many it holds, or, set open, as a sublist, that name and the holons it holds named beneath it by spacing alone, the rest counted, and a collection of one as that one holon. A way of looking is seen at its level, what nothing it gathers holds, each opened to go down; Flat is the deliberate way to see all of it. A list draws two hundred places at most and counts the rest, for a page cannot hold every holon of a field."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG40VC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001BQ6"},"text":["the client"]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG40WV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component is code, and runs in the page with everything the page can reach, so for now only the components the entry offers and those of the home are run; another store's components wait until what they draw can run apart, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M72MZCW4XG40WV"}," asks."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG40WY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-03: expressions are just data, so no language is invented; open the power to look upon data from different angles, which is what the reader will become. The forms the session's. A form for what a holon holds, by key, was let go the same day as convoluted: a holon's parts are its own to open. Grouping the author's, the same day: expressions are grouping, expressions are locations, in layers, a collection opened to see what is inside; if nothing is chosen, everything grouped by the strongest, and play welcome to see what works. The axes and how strength is weighed the session's, a first try. Programs the author's, that night: an expression is taking a program and putting something into it; set operations are programs too, not reserved functionality, so one can add one's own just the same; held by and holds are simply parents and children; and not is needed. OpenLight had its core verbs as native programs, discoverable and called like any other; glass takes that, and sets as what they take, so they compose. Functions apart from programs the author's, the next day: a function is pure and used in what is drawn, a program is run and its return kept with its run, so a function's result is never stored; both first class. The roots the author's, the same night: a group of holons is a holon, so looking upon the field one sees only the roots of the trees its references make; orphans still collect under their type; written as a pure expression. Then the author, 2026-11-09: group by auto is strange; perhaps you always see that level of the holarchy, which reflects the nature of the interface, and of consuming the engine as well; group only for special cases, and seeing everything flat an explicit expression of how you drill into things. Auto and its weighing were let go.*"]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG41MR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The store**: its vectors, made apart from its code; one implementation over plain files, whether a folder, a static host or the browser's storage; every block checked by its hash, and the log by its chain up to the ref."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG42CZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The engine**: stores attached and read as one, fetching only what a read needs, holding told apart from pointing by the moulds, every commit judged against its types and taken in turn, the home the one store written, on its own thread in the browser."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG42EF","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The interface**: the chassis, components as holons in a store of their own, type-matched spaces, and the root mount kept in the home, where one looks said by the page's address, so moving through the wiki, back and forward, and a reload all stand on it."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG42G0","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001CX3"},"text":["the interface as a mirror of the field"]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG42GD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The reader**, then ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M72MZCW4XG42GD"},": the entry is a mount giving what is attached to the reader, a component made of data; a press on a face or a link moves the root, and its menu offers what takes the place pressed; a type shows its fields and its instances; a brief is drawn by its own words; and the wildcard draws any other holon by its values, every reference in them entered from there."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG42JN","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The wiki in the store**: holons down to the word, the files gone, each brief with its history, and what the code is checked against every holon in the field."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG42KP","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Built and written by the session, 2026-11-03; said again 2026-11-08 and 2026-11-09.*"]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG42P8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Being an instance of a type says what a holon is, never where it stands. A type holds none of its instances: they are a set the engine reads, from every store, with no order and no names. Holons of a kind that are to be found together are held by a whole made for it, as glass's functions, components, kinds and types are, each by a whole made for them, and the main store's types by one too."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG42RV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["On 2026-11-09 the author looked at the field through the interface and found it flat: words, sentences and lexemes before anything they make, the main store's types standing at its top, looking at everything able to take the page down, and a press in the search that reset rather than moved. The press was a real fault: a real click lets promises run between listeners, and the search drew its rows anew before the mount found what was pressed. Grouping first took holding into account by itself, and the author found that strange: one always sees the level of the holarchy one stands on, and flat and grouped are deliberate. So a way of looking is seen at its level, Flat sees all of it, Group by takes an axis chosen, and a list draws two hundred places at most."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG431W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Types and glass's pieces were held by wholes made for them, so a store's top is few. The entry stopped naming a brief, which the author called custom glue: it gives what is attached, kept in the home, and the address says nothing at the root. The interface stopped finding what it needs by name in a store the page happened to call glass: the page names the entry, and everything else is reached from what the entry offers."]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG434F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's, in brief; the seventh session, under Sessions.*"]},"id":"1M72MZCW4XG434W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A slot can read more than one holon: what an expression gathers. An expression is calls of functions, data held in a body like any other, and the engine's kernel works it out to a value: a holon, `{ $ref: H }`; a call, `{ call: F, with: [ … ] }`, the function F given what it takes; a lambda, `{ fn: [m], gives: … }`, a function written in place, and `{ var: m }`, what it was given; a list or a record; or a value standing for itself. Every value a holon holds can be used: its id, name, store, what it is an instance of, and every field of its body. Every function is a holon of the type Function, and gives one of two ways: natively, worked out by the kernel, or by an expression of other functions written in the field, as `text`, `measure`, `parts`, `digest`, `outline` and `level` are, so one's own stands beside glass's and reads as they do. A function is pure: given values it gives one, and nothing it gives is kept."]},"id":"1M735YKNB8FV05G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001674"},"text":["the relations"]},"id":"1M735YKNB8FV0M9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Gathered, a set is flat, so that sets compose; looked at, it is seen at its level: what nothing in it holds, each opened to go down, so what a whole holds is never met flat beside it. `flat` is the deliberate way to see all of a set. `group` gives what it is given in collections instead, one for each value along the axis chosen, type, parent or store; none is chosen for it. Each collection is itself an expression, narrowed by one value, so it opens like any place, at its level. Types are held by a whole made for them, as any holons to be found together are, so they stand in the holarchy and not beside it at the top. References build direction, from what holds to what is held; instanceship, from an instance to its type, groups crosswise and makes nothing anyone's child, so types do not swallow their instances. A mention in prose only points, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M735YKNB8FV0M9"}," decide, so it makes nothing a child."]},"id":"1M735YKNB8FV0MJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-10: values in the functional expressions are a must, how else are we to utilise the field; counting and folding are important, and prose as text a function definitely needed; a good way to write expressions and patterns, for use in TypeScript and at the command line; names one word, a name and a title being one field; lambdas sound fine, we can always refactor later. The kernel drawn into the engine, its forms, the one lattice and the language the session's, each read afresh by agents and mended.*"]},"id":"1M735YKNB8FV0QN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["As built, a read asks for a holon by identity, for a whole with what it holds, to a depth if asked, so one level is one read, for what a name gives, for what holds or points at a holon, for a type's instances, for a store's log, for a holon's versions, for whatever an expression gathers, for the value an expression gives, or for what it shows at its level, what nothing in it holds. Beside read, commit and subscribe there is attach, which the chassis uses to attach the stores the page names; run, await and cancel wait for programs. A commit may bring holons into being under handles of its own, as `~1`, and the engine gives them their ids as it lands, so whoever asks need not wait to refer to what it is making."]},"id":"1M735YKNB8FV0W5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Where one is looking is said above it by the search, the first of the reader's two mounts, given what the second draws, and a brief in full says the way down to it, by the same `route` function the address is said by. An expression is said by its parts, each a function and what it is given, as a field and a value: type: brief, children: The plan, search: reader, not: store: home, group: type, flat, each a chip pressed to change it, or, given holons, to add one or take one out, and let go with its ×; a holon by what it is, each type a way to its kind, and what it is called, let go for everything. Every function that gathers is a brick, glass's own and one's own alike, offered by its name; at the top, the parts standing side by side are and, and no part at all is everything, while within a brick, and and everything are taken like any other. Typing finds the brick, Enter takes it, and what it takes is chosen in turn: a set among what is in view, the types and parents of what one is looking at, each with how many it holds, a store among the stores in view, or among the holons whose name says what is typed, or built of another brick taken within it; words as they are typed; an axis to group by. Once all it takes is given, it stands as one more part beside the others, under and; a part given holons is given another by pressing it and choosing a second, as type: brief or component, and or builds an either of any parts; Open goes to one holon. Typed with no brick taken, the words find the values in view as well, as type: brief; and words that read as an expression in the language, as `level(store(\"main\"))`, are offered first, as a way of looking of their own. Backspace lets go of the brick taken last, then of the last part; Escape lets go of what was typed, then of what was taken; in a menu, it closes the menu. Typed, the words find first the holons whose name begins with them, so a holon is found by its name. Before anything is typed it offers the favorites and the bricks, and asks nothing. Each thing it offers that leads somewhere is a press that says where, and rises to the mount like any other: a place, a place drawn by a component, an expression, what the mount offers, or an expression to keep. Nothing is born as one moves: the mount holds the expression it gives."]},"id":"1M736Y7EM7FJ0T3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-10: the address work, sounds good, go; the session's proposal of the day before, a place as a route of names, put in the query rather than the path so that any host that serves files will do, and the old syntax of titles let go for the one language.*"]},"id":"1M736Y7EM7FJ0VT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001G6Q"},"text":["the interface"]},"id":"1M736Y7EM7FJ0Y7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Where the reader looks is the URL's to say: one holon by its route of names, or the expression the root is offered, said in the language, and the component it is looked at with. So a URL is shared, bookmarked or reloaded as it is, and lands where it says, and back and forward are only the address changing; how it is said, and what is kept of it in the field, ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M736Y7EM7FJ0Y7"}," tells. A reader laid over another place, not the root, needs no address."]},"id":"1M736Y7EM7FJ0YQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An expression is said as text in a language of its own, the face an agent types and code writes in a template: a call by the function's name, a holon after `@` by its id, its name or a route of names through what holds it, a lambda as `m => …`, `m.key` for what m holds under key, and `a | f(b)` for f(a, b). The field holds the data, never the text, so how it is written can change without anything that holds it changing. The address says an expression in it too, and a holon by its route, which may begin at a store: `@main:types/brief`."]},"id":"1M736Y7EM7FJ126","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A function gives a third way, beside natively and by an expression: by a pattern of facts. A holon is read as facts, each one thing it says, holon, key and value: what it is an instance of, its name, its store, and each value its body holds under a key, a reference under it at any depth, a string, number or truth at the top or as an item of a list. What it holds as a part is said once more under glass's own mark, `$holds`, so holding is joined like anything else. A list gives a fact for each item, so a fact says what is held and not in what order; order lives in the body, read by `get`."]},"id":"1M7385Y7DNBC041","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A pattern says what must hold, not how: `find`, given what it finds, `?x` or a record of variables, and its clauses. A clause is a fact `[e, a, v]`, any of the three a variable; `not(…)`, clauses that must not hold, with variables of its own; `or(…)`, branches of which any may hold, each binding the same variables; or a test, a lambda given the variables its words name. Variables shared between clauses are the links. It gives a set, each value or record once, and counting, order and a window are said after it by the expressions that already do them."]},"id":"1M7385Y7DNBC07D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-10: why don't you go ahead with the patterns; taken from Datomic in the seventh session, a store's integration answering, indexing neither the engine's nor coupled to it. The facts, the clauses, the plan and the four orders the session's, the design attacked by a fresh agent before it was built, which asked for find as a function, records for several variables, or from the start, tests as lambdas and holding as a fact.*"]},"id":"1M7385Y7DNBC0GK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-11: a store is just the field, so it shouldn't say the integration; an integration, the shape it gives and what it takes are a trinity of connection. Reasoned with the session through the evening of 2026-11-10 and into the next day, beside OpenLight's attach record and federation, read anew.*"]},"id":"1M757E3XPXX804R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An act is one commit, however many stores it touches, and the same commit in each of them. A commit has two hashes: one over its content, the act alone, the same wherever it is kept; and one over its history, its line in one store's log together with the line before it, its predecessor. The content hash proves every version the act wrote, in every store; the history hash proves where it stands in each store's line."]},"id":"1M757F3484D302K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-10 and 2026-11-11: why does the engine really need a store, because it needs to place commits somewhere, and that's kind of strange; it's a governance module; it must run from a preset of attachments, or change its attachments dynamically; if it is given no store to hold them, nothing is persisted, and that's fine, but if you want to, you can, and you point to that when you start, not as a two-step process. The attach record, write declared at attach, and commits routed to the store that owns what they change were OpenLight's, read anew that evening.*"]},"id":"1M757F3484D30SW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Every store has one root, a holon of the type store: what the store holds, the shape its field keeps, the stores its field depends on, and, where it is known, its origin. Nothing in the root says where the store is served or how it is stored, so a store moved, copied or served another way is the same store, root and all."]},"id":"1M757F3484D30WR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
