{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-10: lists are always ordered, one can't respectfully treat them as sets when they are ordered in the field; I always want as much simplicity as possible, but maybe practically it's a mix, built-in indexing, and additional indexing where a store needs it; go with the flow, we are early and experimental. The clause as the contract, the measures and answering once for all the session's; the arrays attacked by a fresh agent before they were built, and the joins read by another after, each fault mended.*"]},"id":"1M757JEKTNGX2DN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-11: there isn't a src dir anymore, just modules in the root; the site is also a module, in a first-class manner, a website that uses the modules and consumes their stores; knowledge might ship with the core, for it explains the primitives, though you needn't depend on both; the sessions, the paper and my exploring in author for now, perhaps later my own store; are stores read raw from git, published through CI, or shipped with the package; the integration could read a store from any open https. This repository may become the project he has dreamed of, under its real name, its site this project's and his CV depending on it. The modules and the two ways stores travel the session's.*"]},"id":"1M757JEKTNGX2RB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
