{"body":{"text":["Reading how the engine meets its stores, and OpenLight's attach record anew, the author asked why the engine needs a store at all. Through the night and into 2026-11-11 the frame was settled with him, none of it built: a store is a field with one root, saying its shape, contents, dependencies and origin; shape, integration and origin stand apart, and an integration is a program; an attachment is what an engine uses, writing granted there alone; an act is one commit in every store it touches, with two hashes, its content and its history; and the code is to be modules at the root, each with its store in `.glass/`."]},"id":"1M757JEKTNGX37B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's, in brief; the ninth session, under Sessions.*"]},"id":"1M757JEKTNGX37R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store is where a field is kept and how it travels: every version of every holon and every commit that changed them, which glass's own store keeps as files that never change, with one pointer saying which commit is current. A store can be copied, served and attached anywhere, and every copy is whole. Its root, one holon, says what its field is, and never where it is served."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G029","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
