{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-04, told in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M7585EX7H7G02H"},"; its root, and an integration as a program, the author's, 2026-11-11, told in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M7585EX7H7G033"},".*"]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G037","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine holds the stores it attaches and is the only way into them. It reads them, carries out every change as a commit sent to the stores that hold what it changes, and runs programs, integrations among them, and it judges every act against what the field declares, whoever asks. Nothing reaches a store but through an engine, and the engine keeps no store of its own: it holds what it has attached, and may keep that in a store."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G05W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A working application, a site among them, needs state. State needs a field to hold it, an engine to govern it, and an interface connected to the engine. Glass keeps the field in stores, and puts the engine and the interface in a client, in the reader's own browser, that attaches the stores and runs over them."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G09T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass's own store comes first, since everything glass makes is kept in it."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G0A9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then what any store is to the engine, glass's or another's, and how one is reached."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G0AV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Any store is a field kept somewhere. Its root says what the field is, and never where it is kept or how. An engine reaches a store by an attachment. The attachment names an integration, a program that reads one way of keeping into a field, and gives it what it takes. So the store holds what is known, the integration how it is reached, and the attachment that this engine reaches it now."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G0DB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An integration gives the same ids each time it reads the same source, derived from what it reads, so what points into its field holds from one read to the next."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G0T9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A dependency is a store this field needs to be whole: its types, or what it points into. Two stores may depend on each other, and neither is beneath the other. A dependency is named by the store it stands for, and says the shape it is read as and, where it is known, its origin, so whoever wants it can attach it in one act. It is never attached by itself."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G10S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A location of one's own, a local copy or a mirror, lives only in one's own attachment, as what its integration is given. The dependency keeps the public origin, so a store pushed carries that, and never one's machine."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G123","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-10: if I'm running locally and point it to a local store, that's a question of configuration, not of the field itself, so that when I push my update it still depends on the public one, not mine; the off-the-shelf definition, or your own location.*"]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G13P","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A reference into a store that is not attached falls under one of its own store's dependencies, so it could say which store it leads into and how one would reach it, rather than show an empty id. How a bare id finds its dependency is not yet designed."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G15B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An attachment is a store as one engine uses it: the shape it is read as, the integration that reads it, what that integration is given, and whether this engine may write there. The engine keeps no store of its own. It is governance: it judges every act, and sends its commit to the stores that hold what it changes."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G18C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An engine starts from attachments given to it, as the command line gives them. Or it is pointed at a whole of attachments in a store, and attaches that store and then what the whole holds, in one step. Attachments are added and let go as it runs. Keeping them is a choice: they are holons, kept in whatever store one may write, and an engine started from them resumes where it was."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1AT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
