{"body":{"text":["Writing is granted by whoever attaches, never by a store: a dependency attached reads only. A commit is refused where a store is not attached to be written, and where it brings a type the store's shape does not admit. Within what an attachment allows, each place still says which programs may change it, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M7585EX7H7G1CP"}," tells."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1CS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How a commit says what it touched is not settled. Naming, for each whole it touched, that whole's commit before and its index after would let one whole's history be read without reading any other; which wholes keep an index of their own, every whole that holds, only those served as stores, or none but the store, with a whole's contents worked out when it is cut, waits until it is needed. Nothing here is built: a commit says what it changed, not which wholes it touched."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1J9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M757F3484D3000"},"text":["one act, one commit"]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1JY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Across stores the same holds: an act is one commit in every store it touches, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M7585EX7H7G1JY"}," tells."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1K1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Because it says only what, how it is answered is planned. Each step is taken when it costs least, all bindings counted, and `explain` says the plan: which order served each step, how much it read, and what was asked within a not."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1MF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A step that shares a variable with what came before can be asked two ways. It can be asked once for each binding, each time with that binding's values filled in. Or it can be asked once for all of them, with only its own values, and joined in the engine by the variables they share. The plan takes whichever reads less."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1PK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The index is about the size of the store, and costs about as much to build as reading it: about a third of a second for the main store. Shipping it would double what a reader fetches, to save that third. At the command line, which builds it for every call, a single find is slower than the same said as an expression."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1WE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Once it is built, a narrow question is answered in a millisecond or two, eight to seventy times faster than as an expression. A store's level, eighty-five thousand bindings, takes about 155 ms, against 466 when each binding was asked apart, and about 190 as an expression."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1Y0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Not yet: rules that recurse, for which `follow` stands; values in records nested in a body; a list's order asked in a clause, where today a list's items are facts without their place; the interface's sets answered through patterns; and bindings held as arrays, should a store's level need to be faster still."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G1ZQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How stores travel is the session's answer, not yet the author's: stores that belong to code travel with their package, since a version of the engine expects its own types; stores of knowledge are published as plain files from wherever they stand, read by an integration from any open address, so git served raw or a static host serves them, and nothing is built for them."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G296","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["- **What is attached**: the attachments the reader keeps, each its integration, what it is given, which ref, whether pinned to one commit, and whether it may be written, so an engine started from the home resumes where it was. Since 2026-11-09 each is kept by what the store is called here and where it comes from; the rest is not yet kept."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G2DD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It is the same as a home directory on one's own machine, holding what one attaches and what one mounts at one's root."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G2E6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Since every relation is a reference in a body, or in a type's mould, the engine keeps one index over the bodies and moulds of every store it reads: which values and references appear where. It is the engine's own, not the store's table of which version each holon is at. From any holon it answers what holds it, what it holds, what points at it, grouped by the type and key that point, and what has a given value. Visits by page, by day or by browser are answers of that index, so many things that look like dimensions are values."]},"id":"1M7585EX7H7G2JB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
