{"body":{"text":["An attached store is written only where whoever attached it said it may be. What one reads of others is read as part of the field and never written into. Someone else's runs are not in it and are not wanted; the reader's own runs go to the home. So what was published stays exactly what was published. One's own project, attached from its folder to be written, is written as the home is."]},"id":"1M758EV0R3YX1NM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A site built on glass elsewhere is its own repository: a store, with a page that loads one pinned build of glass and gives it one default, to attach this store and boot into the entry it holds. Glass, the client, is versioned as code, and publishes its own builds at pinned versions on its own Pages."]},"id":"1M758EV0R3YX1QG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
