{"body":{"text":["The home is the reader's own store: everything they do is kept there, apart from the stores they read, attached to be written. It is nothing special to the engine, which keeps no store of its own: the page attaches it every time, to be written, and it is kept in the browser's storage so a reload loses nothing, or, at the command line, in memory and gone when the engine stops. The engine reads it with the stores it reads as one field, and writes each change to where it belongs."]},"id":"1M758P91PN6H08V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Every source is reached through an integration: a truth of its own, in a format of its own, read into the field by a program, wherever the engine runs. Glass's own store is the native one, its holons read with no translation; files on a disk, files over HTTP and a peer streaming live are only ways of reaching it. A git repository, the browser's history or a video's data are sources of their own, never copied into glass's store."]},"id":"1M758P91PN6H0CY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Three things meet where a source is read. Its shape is what the field is once read: the types it holds, and nothing else may be written there. The integration is the bridge: a program that gives a field of one shape. And the integration takes a body, what it is given to find the source, such as a repository's address: an attachment's `given`. A store and its dependencies may say where they come from, their origin, optional and only metadata, which an integration's body may start from."]},"id":"1M758P91PN6H0FX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass's own shape is open: any holon may be written into it. A git integration's shape admits only its own types. The engine refuses a commit that brings any other type into a store of that shape, and what a shape asks beyond its types, as a commit's files all existing, the integration refuses as it writes."]},"id":"1M758P91PN6H0HT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An integration is a program, the engine's to run and govern like any other. Until programs run, the engine runs only the integrations it ships. The first is glass's own format, its files in a folder, at an address or in the browser's storage. A buffer, a store holding a stream for as long as it is declared to live, and git come next, each limited and able to run in the browser, so a repository can be browsed there with nothing downloaded. Whether code from the field may ever run on demand is to be talked through before anything runs; the author's lean is that it may not."]},"id":"1M758P91PN6H0ND","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The root README is the one way in. It says how to read through the engine with `ask`: the wiki whole, the last two sessions whole, and of those before only what a measure marks as not to be forgotten."]},"id":"1M758P91PN6H0RZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Tests first, and every finished piece read by a fresh agent, the author's, 2026-11-02.*"]},"id":"1M758P91PN6H0SG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Simplicity is the ground of quality. Glass's code is plain TypeScript, data and functions over it: it understands what things are, makes their purposes clear, and composes them without hiding either, so it reads as the primitives it serves. Code is reliable by that clarity, not by machinery added to it."]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E01T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-11: keep things simple, declarative; the ontological take rooted naturally in a functional approach, without convoluting away from vanilla TypeScript. With it he gave the direction he wrote under the rule for another project, whose principles this brief takes as glass's; functional programming, Unix and Rich Hickey influences, not authorities in place of judgement.*"]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E03Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Simple and coherent.** The language's ordinary means come first, and nothing beyond the language and the platform is reached for unless it earns its place: no framework stands between a component and the page, only glass's own small factory for its markup. An abstraction earns its place by the understanding it gives, not the lines it saves, and some repetition is clearer than machinery that couples what must change apart. A pattern already in the code is recognised before another is added, and judged by its reasons, not its familiarity; changing it changes it everywhere it stands. Like work takes like shapes, and different work may take different ones."]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E07H","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Data and functions.** Nothing is a class. A value is plain data, typed by what it is, and whatever makes one is a function that gives it. The core is pure: given its inputs, a function gives its result and changes nothing, and a field is a value, the next made from the one before. Effects stand at the edges, the files, the network, the browser's storage and the page, few and named."]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E0A0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**One purpose, named.** A function gives one purpose at its level, and its name says that purpose, in the field's own words: holon, whole, mould, store, attach, commit. A function is drawn out when it gives its caller an understanding without the mechanics beneath it, which is the rule's gradient in code. A file opens by saying in prose what it holds and why, and a comment says what a thing gives, never how it works line by line."]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E0CN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Each fact has one home.** A fact is referred to where it lives and never kept twice, and what follows from it is derived, not stored to be kept in agreement, as the field itself does. Data does the work that would otherwise be logic: a better shape takes away conditions and special cases. Transformations are described, a list mapped and filtered, a record built in one place, a choice as a lookup, and the flow runs one way, from source through what is derived to what uses it."]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E0FN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Structure before detail.** Plain steps with names and room: a blank line between thoughts, and nothing so dense that it hides the shape. Code is not shadowed before it settles."]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E0GQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Total and honest.** A pure function given what it cannot use gives null or nothing, so a guard can always be written. What is truly wrong is refused, saying in words what was wrong, and a failure is never taken for a result."]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E0J6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Each part to its own.** A module knows only the contracts of what it stands on, and the layers stand apart as the grounds say: the store, the engine, the language, the interface, the components. The code is kept in one form, and its types are strict."]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E0KS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
