{"body":{"text":["*No classes and structure before detail the author's, 2026-11-03, told in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75AA8AZ56E0PW"},"; the code read for its tone, the same day, told in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75AA8AZ56E0QE"},"; tests first and fresh readings his, 2026-11-02. Simplicity, composition, one home for each fact and whole steps from his direction, given 2026-11-11.*"]},"id":"1M75AA8AZ56E0R7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass's code is modules, each a folder at the root of its repository, with its store, where it has one, in a `.glass/` beside its code:"]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV00V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The project's own knowledge, this wiki, would be the store at the repository's root: the session's answer, where the author left unclear whether knowledge ships with the core. So it is: the main store is the root's own `.glass/`."]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV060","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["In OpenLight a module is a store, and what a store ships to draw itself is served from the store. As built, glass's components are holons in a store of their own, `components/.glass/`, made from their code, so a site attaches glass's store beside its own content and is drawn by glass's components, and anyone could draw a field with other components, or draw other fields with glass's."]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV087","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Built by the session, 2026-11-11, on the author's word: keep things simple. Packages were weighed and let go for now by a fresh agent's attack: the tests would have made two of them depend on each other, and relative paths ask for nothing.*"]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV09N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The format as it stands reasoned apart by agents, joined and attacked, the session's, 2026-11-08, on the author's read path: we get the latest index and then the commit history, but we don't get all of the other versions, until asked for. Its cases, and what it leaves open, are in `integrations/glass/vectors/README.md`.*"]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV0BD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The value an expression gives, read by agents at the command line through `engine/ask.ts`, the session's, 2026-11-10.*"]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV0C1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The spec could go straight into a store, but nothing could read it yet; that was the author's catch-22. So this wiki was written first as a folder of files, under the rule, and born from them. The birth ended on 2026-11-06: the holons are the source now, the files are gone, and knowledge enters through `author/`, an utterance at a time or a session in brief."]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV0E8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["`make.ts` writes every line by hand and hashes it with the platform's SHA-256, sharing no code with glass, so passing the vectors means agreeing with something other than oneself. Run it with `bun integrations/glass/vectors/make.ts`."]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV0FD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-01: for running locally, only the engine and the chassis would switch. A local engine stands since 2026-11-10: the stores the repository holds attached as folders, the home held in memory, and an expression asked of it by `engine/ask.ts`, the one way an agent reads.*"]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV0GZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store is any folder holding a `.glass/`, standing beside what it is about: a module's store beside its code, the paper's beside the paper, the project's own at the root of its repository. A static host that skips folders whose names begin with a dot, as GitHub Pages does without a `.nojekyll` file, is told not to. As built, the main store is the repository's own `.glass/`, holding `conversion/ids.json` beside its files, each old ULID's id, which no reader needs, and the others stand in the modules they are about; the site's build copies each out of its dot folder for the host."]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV0MB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How the code is laid out and run is said in the root README, under The code."]},"id":"1M75AXPMF5KV0MY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["On 2026-11-11 the principles the code was written by, scattered across the wiki and the sessions, were gathered into How the code is written, under The grounds, with the direction the author wrote for another project taken as glass's: simple and coherent, data and functions, one purpose named, each fact one home, whole steps."]},"id":"1M75B3GTKJK901R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then the plan's first step: the code made modules at the root, each store moved whole into the `.glass/` of what it is about, the main store the root's own. A fresh agent's attack let packages go for now, and the cuts of the stores wait for step 4, when a store can be taken away with its history whole."]},"id":"1M75B3GTKJK903Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's, in brief; the tenth session, under Sessions.*"]},"id":"1M75B3GTKJK9044","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store's line holds the act whole: its moment, every block it wrote in any store, once each by hash, what it took out, and what it says. The content hash is taken over those four alone, so it is the same in every store. Beside the act the line holds its predecessor and, whenever the act touched another store, by its blocks or by taking out alone, `own`: the hashes of the blocks this store keeps. So a store reading its own log back tells its own blocks from those of stores it never received, and a store an act left behind can be found from one it did not. No store is named in the commit: where a store is served may change, and a commit must not."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX315047","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G000142H"},"text":["the table"]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150A5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["An act mints its ids together, one run in a moment none of its stores has used, so what it brings into being may land in several stores at once. In each store the new holons it keeps, as far as they run one after another, are born there as that store's own run. Whatever else the act writes there arrives as moved, pointing back at the version before in that store, or at none. So a run never has a gap, and a store may say what it holds by its runs alone, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75FH2HX3150A5"}," tells."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150A8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An act lands in order: every block to every store, then each store's line, then each ref. Cut short after its blocks, it published nothing. Cut short among its refs, it stands in some stores' logs and not in others'. An act is refused if any store's ref has moved since it was read, if one store is given twice, or if it touches no store."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150CF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What an act takes out, it takes out of the field: its `gone` leaves every store that holds the holon, each store applying only what it holds. Letting a holon go from one store alone would be another act, not yet designed."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150DW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The log's past is not rewritten. A line written before 2026-11-11 keeps its `parent`, read as its predecessor, and its content hash is worked out the same way, so it names the same act; a line naming both is refused. The vectors that fix the format hold such lines with a commit written after them, to prove they still read."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150FW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Built on 2026-11-11, tests first, the vectors written by hand before the code. The design the session's, attacked by Fable as a peer, and it held only with changes: born told apart from arrived, a store's own run, `own` written whenever another store was touched, gone as out of the field. Fable read the code after, and found a gone lost on reopening after a commit cut into several blocks; it was mended with a test that failed first.*"]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150Q4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M757F3484D3000"},"text":["one act, one commit"]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150S6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["A line names the line before it as its `predecessor`; one written before 2026-11-11 names it `parent`, and reads the same. A commit has two hashes, over its content and over its history, so one act is the same commit in every store it touches, and where it touched several, each store's line says which blocks are its own: ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75FH2HX3150S6"},"."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150S9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store may hold an id only within a run of its own: the same moment as a block's first id, and fewer than its count past it. An act across stores mints its ids together, so without the count two stores would both claim the whole moment. Whether a moment is taken, which minting asks, is a check apart. A block entered before 2026-11-11 has no count, and is read by its moment alone."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150Z2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The count of each run the session's, 2026-11-11, built that day; a moment's check told apart from a run's by Fable's attack on the design.*"]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3150ZZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An id is fifteen characters that sort as text: nine of the moment of the commit that minted it, and six of a count that starts at a chance place in that commit and only goes up. An act across stores mints its ids together, one run in a moment none of its stores has used, and each store keeps its own run of them. So a commit's new holons in a store are a first id and how many, they sort as they sit, and a client knows without fetching anything whether a store can hold an id. Ids are unique across stores, so a store can be taken away, changed and brought back, and a reference into another store is written as any other."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX315142","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Ids minted together across an act, each store keeping its own run, the session's, built 2026-11-11.*"]},"id":"1M75FH2HX31514N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["`format.json` holds small stores written out byte for byte: changes applied in order to an empty store, and after each, the ref, the log and the blocks exactly as listed. Two commits written now: the first brings in a type and two holons; the second brings in one, edits one and takes one out. Then a copy written apart lands on them, changing no block. Then lines written before 2026-11-11, naming their parent, which must still read with a commit written after them. Then an act across two stores, and one that only takes a holon out of both."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX31517Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The session's, 2026-11-08; the lines written before and the acts across stores, 2026-11-11, written by hand before the code.*"]},"id":"1M75FH2HX31518M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass's own are named each by one word, as code calls them. Those that gather sets: `everything`, `type`, `children` and `parents`, what holons hold and what holds them, `points` and `pointers`, what they point at and what points at them, `search`, `named`, `store`, `types`, `group` and `flat`, and `since`, what a store wrote after a moment, read from its log's lines alone. Those that work with values: `get`, `keys`, `in` and `out`, `map`, `filter`, `fold`, `sort`, `follow`, the walk, and the rest. Every act is total: given what it cannot use, it gives null or nothing, so a guard can always be written; `if`, `case`, `and` and `or` work out only what they need. `and`, `or` and `not` are one lattice: of truths, logic; of sets of holons, meet, join and what else the field holds. Held in a mount, an expression is what the mount gives, and a component may gather in what it reads, so the same field can be looked at from as many angles as there are expressions, each drawn by whatever takes it."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3151EX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*`since` the session's, 2026-11-11, on the author's word that he be told of any change in certainty: with it, what moved since he last looked is an expression over the log.*"]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3151FZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Between such rounds the wiki is tended. At the end of each cycle a tender of briefs, an agent whose one purpose is that the briefs say under the rule what the work has settled, and lose nothing, is given what the cycle changed and brings the wiki to it."]},"id":"1M75FH2HX3151QM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A holon always has a residence: the root of a store, or a holon somewhere beneath one. A holon held by wholes in several stores is kept in each, its versions written into each store's blocks, so each store stays whole if it is taken away. An act that changes it writes its new version to every store that holds it, each pointing back at the version before in its own store, so one act may write different blocks for one holon, and the content hash covers them all."]},"id":"1M75FJPM0VTF02W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The governed way of working the author's, 2026-11-11: sound exploration has to take place for sound judgment to be made; if something is a question, make it, in the substrate; of any important shift in uncertainty and certainty he is informed, which does not mean that everything is blocked; is it truly sub if communication goes both ways; there might be one who just tends to the prose and briefs under the rule; utter care for compaction. The session's answer, tried first that day: the cycles, since it cannot compact itself, threads raised by any voice, what moved found by the function `since` and Fable taken as the peer.*"]},"id":"1M75FJPM0VTF0BZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Built so on 2026-11-11, the plan's third step: the engine starts from the attachments it is given, each saying whether it may be written, and holds nothing else.*"]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q93900Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A holon kept in several stores is read from the first of them, in the order they were attached, that truly keeps it: a store may say an id falls within its own runs and still not hold it, so each is asked."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9390CB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Where a commit is written the session's, 2026-11-11, its questions raised as threads first. Fable attacked the design and read the code after: the wholes that hold a new holon taken from the commit alone, ids given after it is known where each holon goes, a new holon following the whole that holds it, and nothing anywhere left pointing at what goes, are from its findings.*"]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9390K8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Built so on 2026-11-11: the engine starts from the home as an attachment like any other, and it is the one store the page and the command line attach to be written."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9390MA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M757F3484D30GH"},"text":["an attachment is what an engine uses"]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9390PB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["As built on 2026-11-11, the engine refuses a commit that would write into a store attached only to be read, or take a holon out of one, and names the store. Today the page attaches only the home to be written, so nothing else is. Where a commit goes among the stores is told in ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75HFN1Q9390PB"},"."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9390PE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M757F3484D30GH"},"text":["an attachment is what an engine uses"]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9390QT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["This is built in glass's own format, with its vectors, and since 2026-11-11 in the engine, which gives the format every store a commit touches. Which store keeps what is the engine's to say, and ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75HFN1Q9390QT"}," tells it. That gone means out of the field is built, and leans until the author says; the engine adds that nothing left in any store may point at what goes."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9390RW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Three questions stand open. How an act cut short is finished: an engine that finds it in one store's log and another store behind is to finish it where it may write, and otherwise say it is unfinished; what it does where that store has moved since is open. As built, the engine finishes nothing: after an act that fails it reads again the stores whose head moved. Which store answers for a holon kept in several: as built, the first attached that truly keeps it. And whether residence follows holding for a holon that already exists, so that a whole coming to hold it brings it into its own store, and one letting it go lets it leave: not built, and it waits on the author."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9390X1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*In the engine since 2026-11-11, the plan's third step, attacked by Fable before and read by it after.*"]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9390XP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Beside the sessions, measures grade what was said, so a later session can reason about what to read. Threads are the questions held open in the field. A question is made there when it arises, by any voice, the author's, a session's or an agent's: what it asks, the sentences it was raised in, and where it stands, open, leaning, settled or let go, as the author left it or as a session judged it until he says. A change in certainty is a commit that moves where a thread stands. So what the author is to be told is asked of the log: `and(type(@types/thread), since(\"main\", moment))` gives the threads that moved since he last looked, at the command line and in the interface alike. He is told, and the work is not held for it unless a thread needs him."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q939128","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A thread that needs him says so: it may say it `awaits` his word. The function `awaiting()` gathers the threads that do, and a component of their own draws each by where it stands, whether it waits on him and what it asks, and in full with the sentences it was raised in. So the address `?look=awaiting()` is where the author looks."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q93914A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*What waits on the author made a thing of the field the session's, 2026-11-11, on his asking three times what to look at: I'd like to see the most significant points that would concern my attention.*"]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q93915H","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M757F3484D3000"},"text":["one act, one commit"]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q93917C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["- **Finishing an act on a store that moved**: an act cut short among its refs stands in some stores' logs and not in others', and a store behind may have been written since. Not built with the engine on attachments, which only reads again the stores a failed act moved, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75HFN1Q93917C"}," leaves it."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q93917G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["- **Which store answers for a holon kept in several**, each holding its own versions of it. As built, the first attached that truly keeps it; whether that is right is open."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q93918M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["- **Gone as out of the field**: an act's gone takes a holon out of every store that holds it, and nothing left in the field may point at it. Built so, and leaning until the author says, a thread that waits on him; letting a holon go from one store alone is another act, not yet designed."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9391AJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["- **Residence following holding**: whether a holon that already exists arrives in a store when a whole kept there comes to hold it, with what it holds in turn, and leaves when no whole there holds it any longer, so every store stays whole if taken away; or whether a whole may hold, across stores, what another store keeps. Built neither way, and a thread that waits on the author."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9391CW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["- **The engine's contract with a store**: when the engine stops standing on glass's own format, every store asked through one contract that writes as well as reads, an act carried through it across stores of several integrations, and canonical text and hashing then the engine's."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9391ED","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Raised as threads on 2026-11-11, the session's, from building one act, one commit and the engine on attachments, and from Fable's attacks on both: finishing an act, which store answers, gone as out of the field, residence following holding, the engine's contract with a store, and a store's shape admitting a type. Settled the same day, as built: where a new holon resides, and that a holon is written where it is kept.*"]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9391J2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then the author began a governed way of working: cycles that each end with everything in the field and committed, questions made in the field as threads, a change in certainty a commit, Fable as a peer reading each design before and the code after, and a tender for the briefs. Under it the second step was built, one act, one commit in glass's own format, the vectors written by hand before the code. `since` was built first, so that a thread that moved is found, and the step's questions were raised as threads. Fable's attack changed the design, and its reading of the code found a gone lost on reopening, mended with a test that failed first."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9391NX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then the third step, the engine on attachments, in a second cycle the author asked to go on without a manual finger. The engine keeps no store of its own and starts from attachments, each saying whether it may be written. A commit is one act written where each holon is kept, a new one where the whole that holds it is, and what goes leaves every store that keeps it; it is refused where a store is only read. Its questions were raised as threads first. Fable attacked the design and read the code, and a new holon found not to follow its whole was mended with a test. One finding was kept for the author: residence does not yet follow holding for a holon that already exists."]},"id":"1M75HFN1Q9391T5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["One thing more is not built, and it is a question. Residence does not yet follow holding for a holon that already exists: a whole that comes to hold a holon kept in another store does not bring it home, and one that lets it go leaves it where it was. Whether it should is a thread that waits on the author."]},"id":"1M75HJHQQA7504B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["With every store rooted, the top of the field is seen three ways: what the engine has attached, the stores by their roots, or the unified field, the wholes of every store side by side. Seeing the field by its stores returns as one way among three, where the seventh session had let the field grouped by store go."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H08K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["This is built, on 2026-11-11, the first part of the plan's fourth step. Glass's store is given its root by what makes it. The main store, the paper and its readings were rooted in one act across the three, the same act in each log. The site's store was born with its root. Each root holds the top of its store and keeps glass's own shape, a holon of the type shape that names no types, and so is open. The main store stands on glass; the paper on main and glass; the readings on main, the paper and glass; the site on glass; and glass on nothing else."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H0C7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store's level is its root alone, and a route of names begins beneath it, so a root is never said in a route. A component, Store, draws a root as the wholes it holds and the stores it stands on, and an attached store's face leads to its root. The other two ways of seeing the top are functions: `roots()` gives the stores by their roots, and `unified()` gives what nothing holds once each root, and what it says it stands on, are set aside. A holon that nothing holds, landing through the engine in a store that has a root, joins what the root holds, so a root goes on holding all its top."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H0G0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Not built: an origin, which no root says yet; a commit refused by a store's shape; and a reference into a store not attached saying where it leads. Three questions were raised as threads. How a root is known: today by its type's name, store, in four places, so a type of that name anywhere would make roots. Whether the reader's home has a root of its own. And how a name reads now that a root makes it many: main names the root and two dependencies, so one writes `main:main`; and whether a dependency stands at a store's level for a route, as it does, or is set aside, as `unified()` sets it."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H0KR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Built by the session, 2026-11-11. Fable read the roots and found them right, and three things not yet kept: the paper and its readings saying they stand on glass, whose types their roots use; a holon nothing holds joining its root; and the maker of glass's store reading holding by mould. All were mended. The three questions are the session's.*"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H0NQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M757F3484D3000"},"text":["one act, one commit"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H0T8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Where a commit is written follows from what it changes. A holon already kept is written in every attached store that keeps it. A new holon goes where the wholes that hold it in the same commit are written, so it is born beside what holds it. One that nothing in the commit holds goes where the commit says, its `into`, or to the one store attached to be written, and is refused where neither is plain; where the store it lands in has a root, it joins what the root holds, in the same act. What a commit takes out leaves every store that keeps it, and the commit is refused while anything left in the field, in any store, points at it. So one commit may be one act across several stores, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75MBJC3E6H0T8"}," tells."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H0TB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G0001BQ6"},"text":["a full client, preloaded"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H0WM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["This much is built, on 2026-11-11, and the rest waits. Each store has its root, but an attachment's shape, its integration and what that is given are not yet said, and no type is refused by a store's shape. Starting from attachments kept in a store is built for a site alone: the page names the site's store, and that store's start offers the rest, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75MBJC3E6H0WM"}," tells. The command line attaches the stores it is given, a home to be written and every other to be read. No engine yet starts from the attachments a home keeps."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H0XQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00014VG"},"text":["taking a holon out"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H11B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Which block holds the latest of each holon is a table, and it holds no content, so one table is the whole field at one moment. Its blocks stand in the order of their first ids, each with its count of new holons, and since ids follow place, a holon is found by the last block whose first id is at or below its own. The exceptions are listed by id with the block that holds them now: holons edited since, and those an act brought in outside the store's own run. What was taken out is listed too, in runs where its ids follow one another, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75MBJC3E6H11B"}," tells."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H11E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Runs the session's, 2026-11-11: found wanting when the cut of the author's words was read before it was designed, and built that day with its vectors. Fable read it correct, and found the writing of runs quadratic and a run's count trusted too far; both were mended, with tests of a long run and of a checkpoint carrying runs.*"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H16W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The session's first way was to copy the main store's files whole, every block, log and history, and then let go in each store of what is the other's. Fable's attack found that this doubles what a reader fetches rather than dividing it, since a table never drops a block, and that main points into the author's words and so must depend on them. Fable leans to a store born from main's table: its first line a checkpoint of only the blocks its holons stand in, history's one home staying main, so `since` over the new store begins at the cut. Neither is built."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1CJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Whether the threads go with the author's words, or stay with the wiki in main as the field's own questions, now that any voice raises them, waits on the author too."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1DM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Read by the session and attacked by Fable, 2026-11-11; the lean is Fable's, not the author's. Both questions are threads that await his word.*"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1EF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Since the engine is headless, nothing ties the client to one store. It is a full client that comes preloaded with defaults, the stores its site offers and one entry, the mount it boots into, and it can attach any other store as well. A store that brings its own components brings code with it, so attaching one is a deliberate act, asked for and seen, and what it draws runs apart from the rest."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1GY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A site's page gives the engine one start: it names only the site's store. The engine attaches that store and reads its start, a holon of the type start that the store's root holds. The start offers the stores to attach, each by what it is called here and an address read from where the site's store is, each attached to be read; and it names the entry. Beside them the browser's own store, the home, is attached to be written. So which stores a site draws from is field data, and a site moved whole starts the same. The address may add a store, as `?attach=`."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1MH","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Built on 2026-11-11, the plan's fifth step. This project's site keeps its store in `site/.glass/`, made by `site/make.ts` before each build: its root, and beneath it the start, offering every other store the repository holds and naming glass's entry."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1NV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The start the session's proposal, 2026-11-11, built by it the same day; its details are not yet the author's. Fable read it and found the offers resolved against the worker rather than the site's store, the start a holon of no type, which the engine would refuse, the server unsafe for inherited names, and the stores offered said in a second place; all were mended.*"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1QZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M6YBY3G00019B8"},"text":["taking a whole away"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1TZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["As built on 2026-11-11, the modules are folders imported by relative path, with no packages yet, and each store moved whole: the engine's types and native functions are still in the store `components/` makes, canonical text and hashing still in `integrations/glass/`, and the main store still holds the author's words and the sessions beside the wiki. The site has a store of its own, `site/.glass/`: its root and the start its page begins from. The cuts wait on the author's word how a store taken away is born, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75MBJC3E6H1TZ"}," tells, and canonical text moves when the engine no longer stands on glass's format but on what it asks of any store. Which folder holds which store, by the name it is asked by, is still said once in `stores.ts` at the root, though each store's root now carries its name."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1WN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A cycle is a thing of the field, held by its session in order: the step of the plan it takes up, its purpose, the moments it began and ended, the utterances it spans, and whether it stands running or closed. The running one grows as each utterance is kept. Since it says when it began and ended, `since` tells what it wrote."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1YR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*A cycle kept in the field the session's, 2026-11-11, on the author's asking: are the cycles that run committed as proper sessions in the substrate?*"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H1ZM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field has no single hierarchy. In the store every holon stands flat, an id and its version; order and nesting live only in bodies, in a brief's flow and sections. So the root is no holon of the field's own making but a mount: what the reader is looking at, held as data. Glass ships one as its entry, and it names no content: it gives what is attached, the stores the field is, each seen from outside and pressed to go to that store's root, which says what the store holds. A site that would open on its own words ships an entry of its own."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H236","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The page names only its site's store, whose start names the entry, and everything else is reached from it by reference: what the entry offers is what everything beneath it looks for, the search, the functions, the components, the types and the material glass ships, each but the search and the material a whole holding its own. A name is looked up only within a whole that holds it, so nothing depends on what a page calls a store. At the root the address says nothing; it says where one looks only once one moves, and letting go of the last part is the root again."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H26M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Not yet built, though the briefs describe them: what is attached is kept in the home, but no engine starts from it yet: the page names its site's store, whose start says what to attach; run, await and cancel wait for programs; a reader's own branch of a pulled store; components run in the page itself, not apart, which is why only the components the entry offers and the home's are run."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H28Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Where the reader looks is the page's address, the truth of it. One holon is said by its route, its store and the names down to it from beneath that store's root, as `?place=main/The+wiki/Glass/The+store`, so an address reads as where one is, with the holon's id beside it, so a link whose names have since moved still leads there, and is said again as it stands; a holon whose way down passes one with no name, or whose names find more than it, is said by its id. Anything else is said as an expression in the language, as `?look=level(store(\"main\"))`, the same an agent types at the command line; and beside either, the component it is looked at with, where one was chosen, as `&with=`. Both stand in the query, so any host that serves files serves every address. What an address says and how it reads back are pure, given the names they need, so the language can change without anything that holds expressions changing. At the root the address says nothing. The root mount is offered the place the address names, or, where it names none, where the entry looks; it holds only what is the reader's, the component it calls and what it offers, their favorites and settings. To look somewhere else is a new address, a step in the browser's own history; back and forward are only the address changing, and nothing is written to go back, for commits are a line and are never undone. What the reader has looked at is kept in the field as their history, a holon in the home that each move adds a visit to, when and what, said as text, so a visit points at nothing that can be gone; going back adds none. This is where the browser and the field meet, an integration, kept in the interface until glass runs programs. A reader that is not the root, as one laid over another place, is a mount like any other, and needs no address. A mount found within what another draws, as the entry pressed in a list, is shown, not run: what it is called, the component it calls, and what it gives, pressed to look there; and a mount never moves to itself."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H2N7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**How a store's shape admits a type**: how a commit is refused where it would bring in a type the store's shape does not admit. Each store has its root and its shape now, glass's own and open, and nothing is refused yet."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H2PP","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**How a root is known**: today by its type's name, store, in four places across the engine, the language and the interface, so a type of that name anywhere would make roots. One home for that fact is wanted, perhaps glass's own type by reference."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H2R8","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The home's root**: whether the reader's home has a root of its own, as every other store has, so that what the interface writes into it is held by something."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H2SA","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Names a root makes many**: main names the root and two dependencies, so one writes `main:main`; and whether a dependency stands at a store's level for a route, as it does, or is set aside, as `unified()` sets it."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H2TN","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
