{"body":{"text":["*Raised as threads on 2026-11-11, the session's, from rooting every store and reading the cuts, and from Fable's attack on them: how a root is known, the home's root, names a root makes many, how a store taken away is born, and where threads live. Built the same day, and so taken out: how a site starts the engine, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75MBJC3E6H2ZA"}," tells.*"]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H2ZE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then the fourth step, in part. Every store was given its root, a holon of the type store that holds its top and says its shape, glass's own and open, and the stores it stands on: glass's by what makes it, and the main store, the paper and its readings in one act across the three. A store's level became its root, a route begins beneath it, and `roots()` and `unified()` see the top the two other ways. Fable read the roots and found them right; what it found not yet kept was mended, so a holon nothing holds now joins its root. Three questions became threads."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H32Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The author saw none of this in the page: it served copies of the stores made when it was last built. It serves each store live from its folder now."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H372","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Last the fifth step, the site started from its store: the page names only the site's store, whose start, a holon of a new type, offers every other store, each found from where the site's store is, and names the entry; the browser's own store is attached to be written."]},"id":"1M75MBJC3E6H38P","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What is gone is said in runs. A line's `gone` and a checkpoint's say their ids in order: each run of two or more ids that follow one another as its first id and how many, and a lone id as itself. A reader takes every id of a run as gone, and refuses a run of fewer than two, or of more than about a million. So letting go of a whole costs its runs and not its every id: what would go to the author's store, 63,771 holons, lies in 641 runs. An act's content hash is taken over `gone` as it is written."]},"id":"1M75ME74VJGH03F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How a store taken away is born is open, and waits on the author. The first cut was read on 2026-11-11 and not made: out of the main store into the author's own would go what was said, the sessions, the measures, the threads and the author's voice, 63,771 holons. Nothing holds across the line, and 57,839 references only point across it, most of them words to their lexemes; the lexicon stays in main."]},"id":"1M75ME74VJGH05X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then the author asked, three times, what he should look at to be the witness the work needs. So what waits on him was made a thing of the field: a thread may say it awaits his word, `awaiting()` gathers those that do, and a component draws each. And `since`, found to give nothing where the interface gathers a set, now answers wherever an expression is asked."]},"id":"1M75ME74VJGH084","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The author asked whether the cycles were kept in the field. They were not, and a cycle became a holon held by its session. Then the cuts were read before they were designed, and not made: what would go to the author's store is 63,771 holons in 641 runs, and Fable's attack found that a store copied whole doubles what a reader fetches. How a store taken away is born, and where threads live, wait on the author. Gone said in runs was needed whatever the cut, and was built, with its vectors."]},"id":"1M75ME74VJGH0B7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A session works in cycles. Each cycle ends with everything it found in the field and committed, and whole: what it built is called and tested, or taken out, never left half made for the next to find. Compaction is the author's to call, and comes at a cycle's border: when a border nears and the session has grown long, it says so and begins nothing new before it. A cycle can begin again on purpose, as a fresh session that reads the field."]},"id":"1M75SBKFDM3K02S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The reading after is of two kinds, and both are done: for faults, by one who will use the piece, and against How the code is written, by a fresh reader holding only the brief and the code. A reading for faults alone lets the manner drift where the work is newest, at the edges."]},"id":"1M75SBKFDM3K04M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A session coming back reads lean: the README, the measures of each whole, and in full only what the work at hand stands on; a fresh agent reads widely where only its conclusion is needed."]},"id":"1M75SBKFDM3K05S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Learnt by the session, 2026-11-11, on the author's asking it to take its digest and then to learn from what can be improved in the orchestration: a fresh reading of the code against How the code is written found the core holding and the drift at the edges, where cycles had stopped mid-step for compaction and half-built pieces stood uncalled, and where every reading after had been one for faults. The author's of the same day: compaction should have been done first.*"]},"id":"1M75SBKFDM3K08M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Whole steps, tested and read.** Each step is the most useful whole one within reach of what is understood, leaving ground for the next. Tests come first. A design is attacked by a fresh agent before it is built, the code is read by another after, for faults and against this brief, and nothing is committed unmended. What building finds goes back into the field, and what stood on a foundation that changed is weighed again, not patched with exceptions."]},"id":"1M75SBKFDM3K0BA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A subscription is told each new value of what it reads, and told in words when it can no longer be read, so what was drawn last is not taken as now; when the read comes back it is told that too, and a read overtaken by a later change is never told. The engine's end of all this is one, `engine/serving.ts`, wherever the engine runs: the worker serves one interface with it, and an engine on this machine would serve every interface that reaches it."]},"id":"1M75T1YWYDHV02R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*A failed read told, not only logged, the session's, 2026-11-11, after a fresh reading of the code against How the code is written.*"]},"id":"1M75T1YWYDHV03J","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M757F3484D30GH"},"text":["an attachment is what an engine uses"]},"id":"1M75T1YWYDHV05B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"leads":{"$ref":"1M757F3484D30TN"},"text":["a store's root says what its field is"]},"id":"1M75T1YWYDHV06B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000014"]}
{"body":{"text":["Of this, the engine's part and each store's root are built, on 2026-11-11. The engine keeps no store of its own, starts from the attachments it is given, each saying whether it may be written, and sends every commit to the stores that keep what it changes, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75T1YWYDHV05B"}," tells. Every store has its root, which says what it holds, the shape it keeps and the stores it stands on, as ",{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M75T1YWYDHV06B"}," tells. The rest is not built. No integration is declared, and an attachment is only a name, a store already opened, and whether it may be written. No commit is yet refused by a store's shape. Of a store it reads, the engine asks only five things: a holon, everything, the log, a holon's versions, and whether it may hold an id. Declaring those, as `integrations/source.ts` does where the integrations stand, is the seam that lets any store be read through an integration; an integration knows that contract and nothing of the engine. To write, the engine still stands on glass's own format, until every store is asked through one contract that writes as well as reads. What follows was settled with the author on 2026-11-11; what the session added, each ground says."]},"id":"1M75T1YWYDHV0AS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How long a session has grown is asked of the app, never judged by feel: compaction is proposed at the first cycle's border past 60% of the context window, and no cycle is begun past about 75%. Each utterance keeps the moment it came, the model and effort the session ran on, and how much of the window was in use."]},"id":"1M75T9TK0GEZ01Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["On this machine it is built so: the host, `site/host.ts` run by `bun run serve`, serves the site and every store live, and holds one engine over them that every page it serves mounts to, over a socket. The stores are attached only to be read, each taken again when its ref moves, whoever wrote it, so a commit made at the command line is drawn at once and nothing is polled; the home is a folder of the host's own, held by one host at a time. The socket answers only the host's own pages and attaches nothing. The page is told by its host that the engine is there, so the same build published elsewhere starts an engine of its own in the reader's browser."]},"id":"1M75TW8ZN2C1041","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Built by the session, 2026-11-11, at the author's word: if one engine is running, why can't the interface be mounted to that; it must be easy to open both possibilities.*"]},"id":"1M75TW8ZN2C1052","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Work is done the same way: tests first, a design attacked before it is built, the code read after, and nothing committed unmended. The one who attacks and reads is a peer, not beneath the session: a fresh agent reading each design and each finished piece as one who will use it, kept addressable so the talk goes both ways. Fable was that peer on 2026-11-11 until, read beside Opus on the same piece at the author's word, its findings were not drastically more significant: it is set aside for now. Where each step stands on the one before, little else runs beside the session."]},"id":"1M75TW8ZN2C108G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A clause may also be a word said, `said(e, a, w)`: the strings the holon holds under the key cut into words, as full text search cuts them, `w` one of them. Given a word, it finds every holon whose strings under that key say it, whatever its case or its accent, so `find(?w, said(?w, \"text\", \"Glass\"))` finds what the exact string does not; given a variable, it binds each word said, so the same clause runs both ways. Each store's index keeps a fifth order for it, the words under a key, made the first time a word is asked of that key and kept, so `store` and the like are never cut unless asked; a word said waits for its key to be bound. One tokeniser, in one home, cuts words for the index, the clause and the language's `words`. The lexicon is such a pattern now: `find(?x, [?w, \"instance\", ?t], [?t, \"name\", \"word\"], said(?w, \"text\", ?x))`."]},"id":"1M760691ADEQ04R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The author's, 2026-11-11: when on SQLite, full text search is built in, so string matching needs to be considered and integrated in the pattern-making primitives, to harmonise in a functional manner. Built by the session the same day, its design attacked by Opus first, which turned a word in a value's place into a clause of its own.*"]},"id":"1M760691ADEQ06N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The index carried, at the author's word, 2026-11-11: in the future the index doesn't have to be rebuilt completely for every commit but could be additional. Built by the session, its design attacked by Opus first, which turned it to carrying a store whole before patching one.*"]},"id":"1M76362Y21C804Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The first mark was to read this wiki from a real store, through a real engine in the browser, along the gradient. It was built, and then the store, the engine and the interface were built again on the blocks, and it stands. What comes next is From here, below."]},"id":"1M767G2RCAZJ01N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["In the author's words: a simple set of architectural primitives, a unified field of data based on holons implementing types defined in the same field, upon which programs and interfaces match by type, so harnesses no longer exist. Local first, it compounds as Unix did, by ownership, transparency and a simple means to let things compound; good compute goes both ways; and if it cannot be an operating system it cannot be the vision."]},"id":"1M767G2RCAZJ043","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What stands: the store, its blocks and log, the snapshot first and history when asked, one act one commit across stores; holding said in references, so the field has roots; expressions, with patterns and string matching at their core; one engine, hosted, for agents and the page; the reader showing a level, flat only when asked; git read as a store."]},"id":"1M767G2RCAZJ062","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The order, as the author set it on 2026-11-11:"]},"id":"1M767G2RCAZJ0AN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Left to the author, and open: dimensions, and what a brief really is."]},"id":"1M767G2RCAZJ0EM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["*Drawn by the session, 2026-11-11, from every word the author wrote since 2026-10-30, about 380 thousand characters, and an agent's reading of them for goals; the order is the author's own of that day. Not ratified.*"]},"id":"1M767G2RCAZJ0FV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What is not right. The field is not where things are made: types, functions, components and the entry are written as files and compiled in, and knowledge is written by scripts past the engine, so the author cannot yet live in the field; this is the root of the rest. Decisions the author made are not in the code: there is nothing first, yet a holon is read as the first store's; every store has its root, naming what it stands on, yet where each is found is still written in a file. Decisions are not all in the record: streams were settled on 2026-11-06 and kept here as one line. And the code does not yet embody How the code is written."]},"id":"1M767GS3BJHX040","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The foundation brought in: making in the field through the engine; residence with nothing first; stores found from the field, not from a file; the record holding the author's decisions."]},"id":"1M767GS3BJHX050","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A clean rewrite once that is clear, written down from what the code means, not from the code as it is."]},"id":"1M767GS3BJHX05Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Buffers, and stores as modules, done properly."]},"id":"1M767GS3BJHX060","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Something simple with git: a repository browsed in the field, a concrete exercise for the interface, since the reader is still undiscovered."]},"id":"1M767GS3BJHX06R","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The interface a little better."]},"id":"1M767GS3BJHX06Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Programs, the real site and what follows, left open."]},"id":"1M767GS3BJHX07A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass as it is to be rewritten, designed before a line of it is. It was written fresh on 2026-11-11 from the author's words, the primitives as he said them and the code as it stood; attacked once from the code and once from his words, neither steered; and settled by him the same day."]},"id":"1M76C7RCPBTY01T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It is the top of the wiki. The wiki beneath it is kept as it was written, its history; where the two differ, this is what the rewrite is built from."]},"id":"1M76C7RCPBTY02W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What the rewrite starts from, as counted the day it was designed: a record, not the design."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS00K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["About 9,000 lines outside the tests; 300 tests passing; the types checked clean. No classes; mutation kept to local accumulators, save the author's tools, which change the bodies they load."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS01M","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Depth: the search component's drawing is 686 lines, `kernel()` 521, `drawing()` 423, `parse` 220, `mount()` 203, `solve` 194, `openStore` 192."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS02A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["One word for several things: Field, Attached, Version, Made, Place, Known, Kind and mount each mean two or three."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS02Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The same logic more than once: mould merging five times, finding a store's root four times, `ref()` six times."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS03M","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A native is found by its string in some fifteen places, and any holon that carries one becomes that native, the home's too."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS04D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Holons made in TypeScript: git's types, the site's making, the components' making, the interface's history and root, and the author's tools."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS054","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Kept for older formats: the log's lines from before the conversion, and `parent`, which stay, apart, since the log is never rewritten; `lexeme`, `closed` and the old search's words, which go."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS066","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The session's proposal; the author's own order was a perhaps, left open."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS06P","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["This design stands in the field as the top of the wiki. The author's tools are let go, and the engine's command line learns to commit, so that every step after is written by hand through the engine."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS07Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The tests become the oracle: those that reach into the kernel and the engine's commits are asked again through the protocol, by the engine's read and commit, while those that already stand where a consumer stands, the store, git, the stores, the text, serving, the host, the interface, the address and finding, stay as they are."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS09S","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["What is stored moves first, with the engine as it is: the natives, git's types and the roots found by address, and each component's declaration out of its code and into its holon."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0AW","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Each module is then written fresh, from the bottom: glass's own format, the language, the engine, the site, and the interface and components lightly. Each begins as its brief, what it conveys and its words, then its code; its tests pass; one critic reads it unsteered, and then the author."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0CH","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Last, a way of looking is said in the language, since that changes the protocol, the address and the components."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0D7","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then, as the author said it, perhaps: buffers, the stores as modules, git browsed in the field, the interface, programs and the real site."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0E2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Each the author's, on 2026-11-11, when the design asked him."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0EF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The engine needs no store.** Its work is to mount stores, so that anything can be done: read, written and run. A set of attachments may be kept in a field, but that waits. The site says the stores it attaches in its own code; a git browser might run an integration on demand, as a repository is opened."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0GF","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The author's tools go.** Skills, practices and principles may be kept, but work locked into code grows less organically. The field is written through the engine, by hand."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0HF","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**A component is a holon in the field**, which links to its code. Nothing of the field is written as JSON or in TypeScript."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0JB","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The root's store**, mounting everything flat and holding the knowledge, is planned and not sure; common sense, and refactoring later."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0K2","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**How code is loaded waits.** Components and integrations are what is written as code today; loading code from the field comes once the rest stands and the integrations are decoupled. In OpenLight git as an integration was the precursor of the engine running programs; whether it is so here is unexplored."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0MS","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Components by common sense.** What composes simply is almost always right; custom glue is not. The interface is worked on later."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0NJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Code names what it needs by address, never by id**: by names, and perhaps in the end by expressions. Kept simple, said once in each module, improved later."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0PJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Untouched, and the author's: dimensions, what a brief is, what a source is, and where indexing's boundary lies."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0Q7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The primitives of code are three: the store, separate; the engine, which governs it; and the interface, which goes upon the engine. Around them stand modules at the root, each first class, each keeping its `.glass/` where it holds holons, each standing only on those before it."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0RT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Code is written as the rule writes prose: know what a thing is, then say that, simply."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0SF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["At one end is the nature of programming: values, and pure functions that compose, effects apart at the edge. At the other is the nature of what we build: the primitives, each word meaning one thing, in code as in the field."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0TW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What lies between follows from holding both. What is knowledge lives in the field, and code only reads it. A file gives the understanding first and the detail beneath. Some repetition is clearer than machinery that couples. Nothing is made custom where a primitive serves. It is real, fast, and tested as it is used."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0WT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Vanilla TypeScript, TSX and all, with no framework between."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0X5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["One field of whole pieces. A piece is a holon: an id, its versions, an optional name, and a body. It may be an instance of types, and a type is a holon with a mould; untyped data is not bad. Holons are kept in stores. An engine attaches stores and is the only way into them, and what it attaches is the field: seen as the engine's attachments, as each store, or as one field unified."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS0ZS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What the field does is of four kinds."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS103","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Expressions**, which may be pure."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS10B","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Functions**, pure and not logged: what makes interfaces."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS10P","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Programs**, not pure: their runs are logged, and they may commit. Integrations are programs."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS118","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Patterns**, the native fast execution functions are built upon."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS11M","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine governs execution, and is itself governed by what the field declares. An interface is holons drawn by holons: a mount, a slot, is a component and a set of holons, said as an expression or a location, and a component is code or layout."]},"id":"1M76C8JGTBFS136","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A page and a host. The site says in its own code the stores it attaches; the page starts an engine in the reader's browser, or mounts to one engine already running, and both are as easy to open. Building bundles, and the host serves the engine; nothing here makes knowledge."]},"id":"1M76C939QY4S01Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component is a holon in the glass store, saying the type it takes and its kinds, and linking to its code; the code is a file, and making it builds the code and nothing else. What composes simply stays and custom glue goes; a reader may be layout, as data and expressions, rather than code. The interface is worked on later, so here components are given common sense and little more."]},"id":"1M76C939QY4S044","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis. A slot is a component and a set of holons, given as an expression or a location. The chassis finds a component for it by type and draws it; the component opens spaces, where what it holds is drawn in turn, and offers pass down through them. Only what the entry offers, and what the reader's home holds, is run. The history stack is an integration, not the chassis's."]},"id":"1M76C939QY4S06J","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["One concept, said one way: the expression, of values, references, calls, lambdas, lists, records and the variables of patterns, read and printed as text, and written as a template in TypeScript. Resolving names is the engine's, so the language stands before it and nothing turns back. A way of looking, a level, groups along an axis, flat, is said as an expression of functions, not as a second kind of expression."]},"id":"1M76C939QY4S0K9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Programs the engine governs: each takes a source and gives a field of one shape, memory, glass's own, a buffer, git. Whether its holons may be changed is the integration's to say, and git's may not. For now glass's own format is what writes, and an act across stores, one commit in each, is the engine's work over it; a contract every store writes through waits until a second integration writes. The vectors' JSON stays, since it fixes the format."]},"id":"1M76C939QY4S0NZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine governs: it is the one way into the field, and is itself governed by what the field declares. It needs no store. It mounts stores so that work can be done: read, written, and in time run."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD01A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It does these few things:"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD01H","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**attach** a store through an integration, and **detach** it;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD01Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**read**: work an expression out over the field;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD029","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**commit**: judge a change and write it as one act;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD02P","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**subscribe**: answer a read again whenever what it read changes."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD033","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Running programs will be the next of these. Its place is attach: an integration is already a program the engine runs, given what it reads."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD040","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Eleven forms of read, and an evaluator of about 50 natives in one 521-line closure."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD04J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Natives found by any holon's `native` string: main's statistic \"Since\" shadows glass's `since` in the expression module."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD055","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Every set operation scans the field. `type` plus `filter` takes 16.6 ms, against 1.7 ms as a pattern."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD05T","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A commit re-reads its stores whole and diffs every block. Every subscription is read again on every change."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD06F","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Ids minted by tools land as moved. Volume 24's checkpoint carries 1,133 such entries."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD070","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The ref and the open volume are overwritten in place; two writers can race; an act cut short is not finished; the home's lock is check-then-write; two browser tabs write home unlocked."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD082","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Three tokenizers beside the one the index uses."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD08C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The protocol:"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0Q1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["`attach`, `detach`;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0Q7","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`read{expression}`;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0QB","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`commit{change}`;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0QF","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`subscribe{expression}`, `unsubscribe`."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0QN","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store moving from outside is the attachment's to tell. The same engine runs in a worker in the browser, or in a host that the page mounts to."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0RP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["While the interface still asks the old forms of read, serving translates them into expressions. The translation is let go when the interface has moved."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0SJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a component may read is declared as the functions it may call, kept by the interface over expressions given as data. `holon` of what it was handed is always allowed."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0TM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Facts, the index and the planner. The index's making, carrying and patching move out of the evaluator, into `patterns/index`. One tokenizer of words serves the index, `said` and `words`. Words begun are an order of the index, asked by `begins`. A store clause in a pattern chooses which stores' indexes are asked."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0WJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Indexing is built in, and a store may answer facts itself. `solve` asks a fact of the store if the store answers, else of the built-in index. Where the boundary lies stays open, going with the flow."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD0XV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A field is made from the one before, and what didn't change is carried: loaded holons, residence, the index."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD201","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**After an act**, the engine knows what it wrote. The index is patched by those holons:"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD20N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["the edges of their old versions are taken out, and those of their new versions put in;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD218","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a changed type re-indexes its instances, found through the index's own reverse of `instance`."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD21S","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**After a store moves from outside**, the store's log since the field's head says what was written and what went. The gone are filtered to the holons that store held. This needs a read of the log's tail, not of every volume."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD239","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["If the field's head is no longer an ancestor of the store's (a checkout, a pull), the store is read afresh. An act refused because its store moved is retried once on the patched field."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD24F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A read is an expression, given as data or as text, and its answer is a value. What were forms of read are functions:"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD25B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["`holon(x)` gives a holon as a record: its id, name, types (their names), mould, body, store and version;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD25Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`whole(x, depth, stop)` gives `{root, holons}`, stopping at types named in `stop`;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD26B","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`type(t)`, `named(n)`, `in(x)`, `out(x)`, `log(k)`, `versions(x)`;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD26S","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`level(set)`;"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD26X","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`group(set, axis)`, which gives each value along the axis with its members, and the rest. The interface makes its own addresses from them."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD27P","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["There are two ways to answer, and each is plain:"]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD283","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**By identity.** A read that is `holon` or `whole` of holons named by id is fetched block by block, as the field is read today: one block for a holon, a layer at a time for a whole."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD29C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Over stores.** Any other read is evaluated, purely, over the stores loaded whole so far. A native that needs a store not loaded says so: `holon(x)` needs the store that may hold x, and `everything`, `in`, `not` over a set and an unscoped `find` need every store. The engine loads that store whole and evaluates again. There are at most as many passes as stores, and an answer is never given over fewer stores than it needs."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD2C1","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A loaded store is carried from field to field. Its index is built the first time a pattern asks it, and the planner asks only the indexes a store clause allows, so `and(type(t), store(\"home\"))` indexes only home."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD2D9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Locally a store is loaded whole in milliseconds (all 137,508 holons in about 45 ms). Over the network it costs what any expression costs today."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD2E5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An evaluator that pauses where it lacks something and resumes, a generator, would make every read lazy holon by holon. It is to be measured before it is chosen, not designed in now."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD2F9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Names are resolved by the engine from the field. There is one resolver, inside the engine. A name shared by several holons is refused, with each named."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD2G8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A subscription keeps what its read touched: ids for a read by identity, stores for a read over stores, together with the function and type holons it resolved. It is answered again only when a change touches that."]},"id":"1M76EKKB06XD2HH","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**A holon kept in several stores**: the version of the later act answers where copies differ, and the holon is marked as diverged. He did not know; common sense, to evolve."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0012","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**An act cut short**: finished where every store it touches is attached and unmoved, else its stores refuse writes until they are. Common sense, his word; it will evolve."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0023","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**One engine writes a store.** The cli mounts to the running host's engine, and the host writes the repository's stores; without a host the cli runs its own and locks."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0034","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**A store's shape admits its types.** \"I thought that was the point.\""]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR003K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**`holon`, `whole`, `in` and `out` as natives** beside patterns: he did not know; kept by common sense, so reading by identity needs no index."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR004G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The field and its index are kept in memory** while an engine runs; other ways are for later."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0055","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`engine/cli.ts` does two things:"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR005C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**ask** an expression;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR005J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**commit** a change, given as an expression that gives `{holons, gone, says}`."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0060","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store is written by one engine at a time. Where the host is running, the cli mounts to its engine, as the page does, sharing its warm field and index, and the host writes the repository's stores. Where none runs, the cli starts its own engine and takes the stores' locks. The stores of a folder are found by glass's own integration, wherever there is a `.glass/`, so the engine reaches nothing above it."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR008H","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The core is a small evaluator that knows no field. Its forms:"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0090","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["a value;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0094","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a reference;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0098","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a call;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR009C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a lambda;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR009G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a variable;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR009M","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a list;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR009R","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a record;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR009W","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a pattern's variable, inside `find`."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00A4","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A variable holding a function can be called, so `apply` goes."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00AJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**A native** is a small pure function in code. It is a function holon's only when that holon is an instance of the function type and names it. No other holon carrying a `native` string becomes one, so a statistic can no longer shadow a function."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00C5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The natives, by family. Every native beyond the bare ones says why: laziness, hashing, or speed measured."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00CS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**lazy:** `if`, `case`, `else`, `and`, `or`. `and` and `or` are lazy over truths."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00DF","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**values:** `eq`, `lt` (no coercion), `add`, `mul`, `round`, `kind`, `join`, `split`, `words`, `get`, `keys`, `put`."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00EC","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**lists:** `fold`, `concat`, `slice`, `reverse`, `sort`, `map`, `filter`."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00EY","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**sets:** `and`, `or` and `not` over sets, `distinct`, `minus`, `has`. All hashed; none scans the field."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00FP","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**the field:** `everything`, `attachments`, `holon`, `whole`, `in`, `out`, `follow`, `group`."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00GB","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**history:** `log`, which gives each act's written and gone ids, `versions`."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00GT","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**patterns:** `find`, `explain`, and the clauses within them: a fact, `said` (a word under a key), `begins` (a word begun, for a reader typing), `not`, `or`, and a test."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00HW","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Written in the field upon them:** `type`, `store`, `stores`, `named`, `children`, `parents`, `first`, `last`, `size`, `since`, `level`, and `prose`. `prose` gives a paragraph's holons under handles, from `split` and `words`, so that writing prose by hand needs no tool. Those that ask the field, `type`, `store`, `named` and `children`, are written as patterns. The statistics in main that name natives the core lacks are written again as expressions, or refused cleanly."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00MQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Let go: the old search, that is `search`, `named` by substring, `contains` and `says`; `lexeme`, `apply`, `group` and `flat` as identity markers, and the expression module's parallel checking."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00NS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["`in`, `out`, `holon` and `whole` stay natives beside the patterns because they answer by identity without the index, and the index needs a store whole. So reading one holon stays cheap; if patterns become cheap without a store whole, this is looked at again."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00QA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An act is one commit, the same in every store it touches. It has two hashes: one over its content, the same everywhere, and one over each store's history, which names its predecessor. Only the engine can compute it, because only the engine sees all the stores an act touches."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00S0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A change is `{holons, gone, says, into?}`. New holons come in under handles, such as `~1`, and **the engine mints their ids.** An id that no store keeps, that the engine did not mint, and that is not derived from a source, is refused. Today tools mint ids themselves and the engine passes none of them as born, so those holons land as moved, swelling every checkpoint after."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00V7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine's part, in order, each step a pure function:"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00VK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Residence.** A kept holon goes where it is kept. A new holon goes where the whole that holds it goes, or into `into`, or into the only writable store. A store receiving loose holons has its root say them, the root found by address."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00X4","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Mint.** Handles are given ids, one run per store where they can be."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00XM","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Judge.**"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00XR","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Write.** Glass's format writes the act to the stores it is given: blocks, then lines, then refs. Which store keeps what is the engine's; how an act is written is the format's. This is settled, and a contract every store writes through waits until a second integration writes."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00ZD","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["What makes writing safe, in the format:"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR00ZQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Replace.** The ref and an open volume are replaced whole, never overwritten in place. `Files` gains a `replace`: on a folder, a written file synced and renamed over the old; in the browser, one transaction."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR010Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Locks.** A store is held for the length of an act by a lock made exclusively, taken in stores' order. The lock names its process and when it began, so a lock left by a crash is known stale and taken over. It is kept out of git."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR012K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**In the browser**, the browser's locks hold the home across tabs."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0131","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**An act cut short** among its refs, common sense for now, to evolve:"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR013J","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["each line names every store the act touches, outside what its content hash covers, so the act's hash stays one, and the vectors change with it;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR014E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["where every store the act touches is attached and none has moved since, the engine finishes the act, moving the refs not yet moved;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0158","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["otherwise the line is never overwritten, and a write to that store refuses, naming the act and the stores it waits on, until they are attached."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0164","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["One module holds what a type says:"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR016E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["`mouldOf(types)`, merged once;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR016K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`holding`, a reference's own `$holds`, or else its mould's;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR016Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`bodyProblem`."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0172","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A change is judged by small named rules:"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR017D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["no holon twice;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR017J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["ids are ids;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR017Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a holon untyped and without a mould is refused;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0182","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["every type has a mould;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0189","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["the body fits;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR018E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a store that is only read refuses what reaches it;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR018T","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["every reference resolves in the field, or names a dependency;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR0196","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["nothing that stays refers to what goes, which is answered from the index's references inward."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR019Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store's root says the types it admits, and a change that would bring another into it is refused. Git's store admits git's types and nothing else."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR01AP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An attachment is an integration and what it is given: a folder, an address, the browser's storage, a git repository. Each is attached to be read, or to be written as well. Attachments are set at the start or changed while running. When one comes or goes, the field changes, and every subscription is answered again."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR01CK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field is the attached stores, seen three ways:"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR01CY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["the engine's attachments, `attachments()`;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR01D5","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["a store, `store(k)`;"]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR01DB","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["the unified field, `everything()`."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR01DJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store's root says its contents, its dependencies and its origin. A reference into a store that is not attached is said as a reference into that dependency. It is never an empty id."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR01ES","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field is the value at a commit; the engine keeps what it has read of it. A holon kept in several stores resides in each of them. Mostly their copies are one version, and nothing is chosen. Where they differ, a whole taken away and changed, or one store changed while the other was not attached, the version of the later act answers, and the holon is marked as diverged, so the difference is seen and never hidden. Common sense for now, to evolve."]},"id":"1M77EJ3F7DR01HM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine as written anew on 2026-11-12, drawn in folders as its top, engine.ts, says it. Each file has one purpose, and where it composes, an orchestrator stands at its top, painting with the names of what lies beneath it."]},"id":"1M77TT6XY80301A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A read is answered by identity, from blocks, or over the world, by the evaluator and its natives. A commit is known, planned, judged and written; the clock is read at the top alone. The bare language is 157 lines where the kernel was 860."]},"id":"1M77TT6XY80302W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The oracle first, done 2026-11-12.** The engine's tests speak through its surface alone, so the new engine is held to the old one's behaviour."]},"id":"1M77TT6XY80303Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The act, done 2026-11-12.** The engine mints every id; a change is planned purely and judged by rules returning every problem; writing replaces files and locks, and settles an act cut short."]},"id":"1M77TT6XY80304T","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The engine written anew, done 2026-11-12,** whole, from its top down, in cycles with the voices of Rich Hickey, a functional programmer, OpenLight and the rule, then drawn again so its folders say its framework. It replaced the old engine, the oracle green throughout."]},"id":"1M77TT6XY80306A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Not yet:** who acts and what a read stood at, said with every change, which governance and programs rest on and which change the format's line; a written store moved by another taken as it stands, and a commit retried once; copies that differ marked diverged; a store's root admitting its types; stores loaded only as a read needs them, and the field carried after an act rather than its store read again; the functions in the field written upon the natives that stay, and legacy.ts let go; the interface asking in the language, and compat.ts let go."]},"id":"1M77TT6XY80309F","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Who is told of a change is said in engine.ts alone: onChange, heard whenever the field becomes another, whatever changed. A subscription that keeps what its read touched, answered again only when a change touches that, as designed above, was let go on 2026-11-12 since nothing asked it; serving reads again on every change. It returns when a reader needs it, together with what a read touched. What a store has read of it, its holons and its history, is kept with the store itself, so it holds for every field the store stands in."]},"id":"1M78MVYTQ5P3034","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass is an operating system made anew: one field where data, knowledge, programs and interfaces live together, open to each other, so that nothing is a silo and everything built on it compounds. Read this page and you hold what glass is for and what it rests on; each part beneath it goes deeper into one piece."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What Unix did right was unify things: every program stood on one floor of files and text. Since then programs have become worlds of their own, each with its data shut inside, and our files went into the cloud. Between the worlds people build glue, and AI is mostly put to gluing them faster. Glass begins again from one field. A part of it may still be kept apart, by choice, but nothing in how it is built divides it."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["On one field, inference changes in kind. A completion takes a body of the field and infers an evolved field. Through a harness that happens as a line, a persona born, mutated and lost. On the field, what a completion read and what it made both stand in the field, open to every other program, and how it was steered can stand there too, so inference can be seen and taken apart. It stops being a line of separate lives: every inference is of the one emanation of the field, though it is still inference, and not pure in that full sense (15/19)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So glass is not a mind being made: \"we're not creating AGI\" (15/15). It is the symbiosis of human and machine: an operating system mirroring teachings of existence, an extension the human and the spirit rest in, with inference what interlinks them (15/19, 15/15). By studying reality and systematising it, glass would make the world \"a more hospitable place for manifestation through intermediumship and communication\" (15/19)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Sovereignty is its value, as it is reality's: \"true power, true reality is full sovereignty\" (15/13). And sovereignty and unity may be one nature, the holon's: each thing whole in itself, and each one part of a single field, at every scale. *Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It is meant to carry any compute, live as well as kept: synthesizers, audio, video, signal processing (11/69, 11/75), and to meet everything outside it both ways, bringing in what already is and sending the field out (15/25, 16/3). Nothing in it is to fail silently, and no part's failure is to take the others down."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The author's words are quoted as he wrote or spoke them, cited by session and utterance, so 15/15 is the fifteenth session's fifteenth. A claim that is not plain fact closes with a mark: **Settled**, by the author, on the day or at the utterance given; **Leaning**, his, with his doubt quoted; **Proposed**, a session's, unratified and free to change; **Open**, a question standing."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00J","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The design comes first, since everything else stands on it: the primitives, each with its practice beneath it."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The way from here follows: what comes next, the one place the plan is kept."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How we work is the culture sessions have drawn from their work on glass, which the author has not yet given his own to, or ratified."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The words come last: those used across the parts without a brief of their own."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00P","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The design is glass's primitives: what each one is, what in reality it takes inspiration from, and the practice that grows beneath it. Read it and you hold glass at its simplest; step into any primitive's practice to see it made real."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Each primitive is drawn from how reality does a thing. That is inspiration, not a claim: \"we take inspiration from, right? We work in the way of reality.\" (15/13). The philosophy is the author's, and still moving. The primitives are to be simple yet enabling, and there may be stronger ones beneath them not yet seen (16/3). They are measured by his questions: \"Is the design clear? Is the ontology clear? Does it resonate? …Do we have a clear ontological lay? That harmonizes and enables for all of the things that we see need be.\" (16/37)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["In one picture: the field is held by programs; a person or a program offers a change; the engine judges it, and the programs holding what it touches take it or refuse it; what functions derive and components draw follows. The primitives come in the order they stand on each other: the foundation, which is the field, the holon, the commit and type; what is pure, the function and the component; the program, in time, holding the field and working upon it; the wire, joining wherever programs run; and the engine, moving it all."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The foundation is what glass is before anything is done with it: one field, the holons it is made of, the commits that change it, and the types that give it meaning."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field is everything glass holds, as one. Data, knowledge, programs and interfaces stand in it side by side, and anything in it can be read and built on by anything else. Its nature is transparency, as reality's is."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Nothing in how it is built divides it. The engine, given below, may, out of its sovereignty, keep a part of the field apart for whoever is to see it; that is chosen, never built in (15/19). Nor need the field be one timeline: \"What's to say there is only one reality and one timeline as well?\" (15/13). *Open: nothing is built for branching yet.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The author once likened the field to consciousness and the holon to its part, as mystics speak, then said that glass takes inspiration from that and does not claim it (15/9, 15/13)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field is made of holons. A holon is a whole that is also a part. As a whole it is sovereign: complete, readable alone, failing only within itself. As a part it is unified: one holon standing in every whole that holds it, never a copy. So the same thing is the same everywhere it appears, and the same shape repeats at every scale, a holarchy, each whole standing on what it holds."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA00Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["This may be the nature every other primitive carries: whole in itself, and one with the field. *Proposed.* The author reads reality as thought built upon thought, \"until you come to the most supporting thought\" (15/13); the holarchy may be that shape in glass: \"it is like the holarchy\" (15/13). *Leaning.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA010","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Every change the field keeps is a commit. A commit says what it changed, when and by whom, and what its maker had read of what it changes, and names the commit before it in each place it is kept. So history tells who knew what, not only what came after what: a change made without having seen another reads as such. *Settled, 16/60 and 16/62; not yet built.* It may take a holon out of the present, yet the past stays readable, and the field as it was at any commit can be read again: nothing that happens there is lost, as the author likened it to the Akashic (15/9), save what is erased, as given below. Glass's own store, strata, is named for the same image."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA04M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A commit names its content by its hash, and that is what lets the field be relied on: a read can be repeated, and a change seen. The author placed reliability there, in the identity of content rather than in history: \"If there is no means of identity of its content. I think that's it, perhaps not history.\" (16/29). *Leaning.* So what glass reads without its being committed can be relied on only as far as it names its content, which is for whatever holds it to answer, as programs show below."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA04N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A type says what a thing is. Every holon may be of types, and a type is itself a holon, saying in prose what its instances hold. So meaning is never left in code or in anyone's head: it stands in the field, readable by a person and by inference alike, and changed by commits as understanding grows."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA04R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Type is what lets glass compute over the field: \"The type is what enables. Computes over it, right?\" (16/44). *Leaning.* It is where programs, functions and components meet. None of them names another; each names the types it works with, and so they find each other by matching, where today's systems need glue. Whoever makes a type opens a place where all of them may meet. Data may still be untyped: of type as what makes it data, \"I don't know, maybe not\" (16/44); a type is what lets the rest of glass meet on data, not what lets it exist."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA04S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So holons are read as the type asked of them. Characters typed into a search bar are never committed, yet where a function asks for a string they are one, \"an in-place primitive value of a string\", a phenomenon that \"perhaps has to be first class\" (16/25). Nothing more than type is needed for it, since everything is holons and type reads them (16/44). *Leaning, 16/25 and 16/44.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA04T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Where holons do not fit the type asked, the read says so. *Proposed.* Whether the type, whatever holds the holons, or both do the reading is open; the session leaned to both (16/26). *Open.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA04V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["One type may also be given by many. \"FTP and Git and HTTP and the file system all represent the same thing, directories and files\", which the author left as \"another complication that I can't see straight around\" (16/29). *Open.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA04W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Type is where glass meets ontology, the study of what there is, where philosophy and science have long met (15/19): \"the systemization, the logos, the rationalization of existence\" (15/13). And as ontology has a floor, since anything constructed can rest on only so much, types may be the floor of meaning in glass, its most supporting thoughts. *Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA04X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Reality has its archetypes, the primal symbols Jung wrote of; types are glass's, made explicit and open to change. A holon may be of several types at once, so the field takes on the many dimensions of what it describes and is never flattened into one scheme. *Type in the foundation, settled, 15/11.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA04Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["In glass a function is written as an expression and kept in the field as a holon. *Leaning: resonance is his, with his doubt, \"I don't know, this is interesting\" (15/13); \"out of time\" is the session's image; and a function beside the program is his, \"not only are there programs, there are also functions, those which are pure\" (15/9), where of the expression as a primitive he said \"No, I don't know.\" (15/9).*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA053","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field has many dimensions, and functions multiply them; a component is strictly holarchical, one root. To draw is to enter the logos and choose a perspective (15/9); the field many-dimensional and the component one root is his (15/19). So a component takes one projection of the many-dimensional field and draws it as one hierarchy, a page, a list, a view, as deep as the field is broken down, more components matching by type at every level. These are the ways glass bends the light of the field (15/9), and since the field can be projected endlessly, there are always many ways to show it. *The component a primitive, settled, 15/9.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA056","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Nothing holds the field but compute. Holons kept on a disk, the channels of an audio interface, a person's edits on a page: each is there only because something runs and answers for it. So the field is born of programs, and programs \"hold and project the field through the engine\" (16/44). *Leaning: \"Programs can answer, I guess, then to the law of the field, thus birthing the field upon compute, right?\" (16/44).* This gives what a program is, its two obvious purposes, the store and the interface, and how glass meets the world beyond."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA059","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A program is in time, where the function is out of it. Of glass meeting the world the author said: \"The integration with the external world is not so explored yet. But really, there is in and there is out. That's it. It's I/O.\" (16/5). The session reads it of every program's meeting with the engine as well: in and out belong to the one program. *Proposed.* So a program is never split into a part that reads the world and another that writes it. A git repository held in the field is edited there and the edit goes back to git; a live source \"isn't a one-way thing\" (16/7)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A program may serve the engine: hold part of the field and answer for it, being read, being followed, and taking a change the engine has already judged; a store does just this. It may consume the engine, calling it to read and to commit. Or both. *The two sides, proposed, 16/20, 16/30 and 16/32; serving the session's word, which the author took up, 16/31.* A program that serves is whole in itself, as a holon is: read truly without any other, and free to refuse a change against its own truth, as git refuses a push, its refusal reaching whoever offered the change. *Proposed, the session's, 16/10.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Who runs a program is a question apart from what it serves: \"An engine may govern it by running it. If governed by it, in terms of its running, is one thing. Whether or not it serves the engine is another point of view.\" (16/31). *Leaning, 16/31.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So \"a store is never a program\" (13/19), which joined the two questions, gives way: a store is a program, which the engine may run or not; today it does not. *Leaning, 16/44.* The author first called a program what the engine runs, then doubted it: \"maybe programs are programs, regardless if managed by the engine or not. I don't know.\" (16/29)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Everything a program does happens through the field, so every program is open, typed to what it works with, and first class for whoever comes after; it may call other programs as it calls the field. Programs that serve differ only by what they answer: which types they give, whether they name their content so it can be relied on, and whether they keep its past; \"sources have the ability to define the type in which they exist\" (16/7). *Proposed.* And programs are open-ended, as glass is: \"The thing about the programs is they are kind of open-ended, right?\" (16/44)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A program is like a series of thought, and is not thought, for thought is more than the rational: \"They are like, but they are not.\" (15/19). He said too that it has a beginning and an end, coming from the field and dying in it (15/19)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store does not end; it runs on. So the session reads it this way: what begins and ends is each pass of a program's work, from the field back to it, and the pass is what is like thought. *Proposed, departing from 15/19 for programs that run on.* So the harness breaks apart (15/9): a completion is a program, each answer a pass, and being agentic is that pass calling what is in the field."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The interface brings the field to a person. It reads the field and draws it with components, and since a person does not only look, it takes their edits back: moving, writing, rearranging. \"An interface may be strictly pure, and the only changes it can do is through invoking a program. But WYSIWYG speaks otherwise\" (16/17). An edit made on the page is a change like any other, judged by the engine and committed (16/29)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Nor is it a lone thing: \"What the interface requires for its function, there must be endless other opportunities that require the same thing.\" (16/17). What it asks of the engine, to read, to be told and to commit, every program asks."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Through programs glass meets what already is; without them it would serve only itself. The meeting goes both ways: \"We might just as well want to make changes to the external world. Essentially, it's I/O\" (16/3); \"Git goes both ways\" (16/7). *Leaning.* That each way is a program holding the far end is the session's. *Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Git is the example the author turned over most (16/19). The repository is kept apart from one's own store, each sovereign and whole, so a file is referenced in git's store, not copied. Its program may run continuously or ride on git's hooks; it may take a remote's address and spawn the repository in the field, and take edits too. Whether git's commits are commits as strata's are is open: \"Is it that Git commits are seen as commits to the same degree that the strata does? I don't know.\" (16/21). *Open.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["To be referenced, what is brought in \"has to answer identification, and it has to answer or integrate with history\" (16/21); he later loosened the second to identity of content (16/29). Much already has its identity, as an audio interface's channels are there when it is plugged in: \"am I going to spawn a channel then? Or are the channels already there?\" (16/25). Not all of it keeps a past: characters being typed change with every key, and FTP may keep none, \"if FTP doesn't have history\" (16/29). Without identity of content, \"You can't rely on the same result\" (16/29). Whether to keep a past is then the choice of whatever holds it: FTP's program may keep one, caching what it reads (16/29). A read of a past that was not kept is refused, never answered from now. *Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05W","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field may also go out as ones and zeros: \"a REST endpoint from the structure you define. Maybe it is a file of TypeScript types from the field. Maybe it is virtualizing a Git repository with the commits from the field.\" (15/25), or a fake repository projected, when \"you just want to emanate something\" (16/19). What goes out is a function of the field, written out by the program holding the far end. *Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA05Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Several completions may cycle on one field, each reading it and writing back: the jazz band, as it was later called in OpenLight, the project before glass, first drawn in the author's earliest talks with ChatGPT, kept as an export he calls the strange of AGI (16/3). The author raised what it might ask, \"just an idea I haven't really given much effort for\": where they write one output at once, \"that output node will reject that and it will become visible in its own state\", and the others would see it, \"Not that I know that there is a big value in that or not\" (16/5). It needs no mechanism of its own: \"all of this could be orchestrated on top. It needn't be a first-class thing\" (16/7), as one list for the output and another for what is placed into it. *Leaning.* What it asks, each commit keeping what its maker had read, so each can see what the others had heard (16/57), is settled for every commit (16/62), though not yet built."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA074","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Upon the foundation every place must be joined, as all data is joined in the field. The wire joins them, and stands on the same values: open, unified, nothing shut inside. The author: \"from that foundation I guess there must be interconnection. That's why we have the wire, because it stands upon our values.\" (16/44). *Leaning.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA078","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Whatever runs, a program, the engine given next, or the runtime that starts them, is sovereign, and may run in the same thread, another worker or another process, and by design on another machine. The wire reaches each as if it were here, so a thing is used the same way wherever it runs (15/21). What the wire must carry is read from what has to meet, \"down to the core, down to the wire and what's needed of the wire\" (16/19)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA079","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So code can stay as plain as functions. What is written to be called here can be started anywhere, and what carries the calls is an adapter that can be exchanged for another; take the wire away and the same things are simply called directly (15/21). Plan 9, an operating system after Unix, sought this, everything reached the same way; glass makes it the form of every boundary."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine moves the field the programs hold. It reads it, judges every change offered to it, and sees it committed, so the field stays whole and moving; without it, \"everything is crystal. There is no process, there is no movement, there is no evolution\" (15/13). It is called an engine because it motors on."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Upholding sovereignty is its work (16/44), and the field's transparency is what lets it be full: nothing hidden, so every change can be judged openly, each failure contained where it happens and said to whoever asked, and every whole kept its own, so that nothing is a unit, one point whose failure takes others down (11/55, 11/65). *That transparency gives full sovereignty, the author's, 16/44; how, the session's reading.* It upholds sovereignty by letting programs be born (15/9). How it governs, and who may act, is not yet designed. *Open.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07D","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Yet the engine keeps no holons of its own; it mounts the programs that hold them, and they tell it where they stand. The author found it strange to call sovereignty the engine's job when the engine keeps no field: \"that's a bit strange to say, because the engine doesn't have a field. Right.\" (16/44). *Leaning.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It is the heart, and never the breath. The session offered the heart, and the author took it, setting breath apart: breath, air and spirit are what the human brings, what no program or model has, and what glass does not build (15/15, 15/19)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine is sovereign because it rests on the foundation, \"it's able to be fully sovereign because it rests upon the foundations of reality\" (15/13), where today's security draws boundaries among what is not pure."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07G","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A part is never a copy, and here is how: a reference that holds. This gives what a holon holds, how holons hold and point to each other, how they are named and found, and how a type says what its instances are. Everything else in glass reads and writes holons this way."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A holon has an id, the types it is an instance of, an optional name, a mould if it is itself a type, and a body. Each change gives it a new version, and its versions are its history."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The id is 15 characters, given at birth and unique everywhere: 9 for the moment in milliseconds and 6 for a count that begins at a chance point and rises by one, in the alphabet `0-9A-HJKMNP-TV-Z`, so ids sort as text in the order holons were born. A commit mints its ids together, in a moment none of its stores has used. A name is also the holon's title, and is unique only among what one whole holds, so two wholes may each hold a \"What is open\"."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07P","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["In a body, `{\"$ref\": id}` refers to another holon. A reference either holds, making the other a part of this one, or only points. The type's mould says which, or the reference itself, under `$holds`."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a holon holds are its parts, and it is their whole. A part may stand in many wholes and is still one holon. Holding is a list, which keeps order and may hold an item twice, or a set, which holds each once; a change that gives a set an item twice is refused."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07S","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Belonging is read upward through holding alone, to every whole above. A cycle can be met there, and reading guards against it rather than forbidding it. Whether one of a part's wholes is its owner is left open on purpose: many owners can be narrowed later, and one could not be widened. *Open; left so by the author, 2026-11-04.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07T","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A relation with a time or attributes of its own is a holon of its own, as a role is. A relation lives in the holon that can be written, so a person's notes on what they only read stand in their own holons and point into it."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA07V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Prose is holons too. A brief has a flow and sections: its flow holds paragraphs, lists, code or another brief, in any order, and its sections are briefs of its own, read after the flow, each under its name as a heading. A brief placed in another's flow is a face: a reading of its own that one may step into."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA080","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A type is a holon with a mould. The mould says, field by field and in prose, what its instances hold and which references hold. Untyped data is not wrong; a type is what lets the rest of glass meet on it. A holon may be an instance of several types, and a type's mould may itself be read, so what a type says is as open to reading, reasoning and change as anything it describes."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA083","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Types own nothing: being an instance says what a holon is, never where it stands, and holons to be found together are held by a whole made for them."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA084","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store is sovereign, and here is how: what makes it whole, what it gives the engine, how one commit stands in every store it touches, and what happens when the field moves under a change."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA086","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store keeps the holons that reside in it, the commits that changed them, and the index to find them. It does not keep the whole field, nor every change: a commit that touches several stores is kept in each only by its share there, with the rest named by hash. What makes a store whole is that it can be read truly without any other store. The author: \"the store is becoming whole ones themselves, not needing the other whole ones to give the picture that's needed… it really sounds like the right thing\" (12/27). *Settled, 12/27.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA087","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So a store does its own work. It keeps its own index, since the store, not the storage it rests on, knows its holons (12/25 to 12/27). It compacts that index itself, out of the engine's way: the author doubted the engine should be accountable for it (12/131), and compaction now runs inside the store whenever nothing else is under way (13/95 to 13/100). And whoever starts a store hands it the storage its bytes rest in; a store never finds its storage itself (12/135). *Settled at the utterances given.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA088","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store has three methods; the engine calls them, and the store never calls the engine. All three are asynchronous, so a store may run beside the engine or far from it and be used the same way."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA08C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["`stores/store.ts` is this in code, where a commit as offered is called an `Act`."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA08H","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So a commit has two hashes: \"it holds the SHA of the content and it holds the SHA of the history, its predecessors. Those are vital.\" (14/20). The content hash is the same in every store. The history hash also covers the commit before it in one store, and so names the commit's place there. A head, a point in a store's history, is named by both. *Settled, 9/27 to 9/29, 2026-11-10.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA08M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store's share is the holons it keeps of the commit, as canonical JSON lines in the order of their ids, the same bytes in any store; the code calls it a part, and `stores/act.ts` writes shares and hashes."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA08N","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A commit may one day follow more than one commit before it, for peers; the code already keeps a list. *Open*, as are merging two lines that both changed one holon, proving who published a store, and finding the stores of others."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA08P","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["When one commit touches two stores, each takes its share alone, and the two may come to stand apart: one took it while the other moved meanwhile, refused it, or was never reached. Neither store is broken, since each is whole; they disagree about a holon kept in both, which is marked diverged, the later commit's version answering."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA08R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A change is what is asked to be committed, before it is judged. Two changes conflict only where they touch the same holons or the same addresses. A store laying a commit over a head that moved since it was judged asks whether whoever moved it touched what this commit touches. If not, it lays the commit over theirs; if so, it answers changed, and the engine judges again, refusing with its reasons what can no longer stand."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA08V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A change that can still stand but would overwrite what its maker never saw is its maker's to decide: \"you may state that I'm giving you this with an at, and if anything in it shifts, don't accept it. So that's just two levels of consuming, and the engine should be able to serve both those desires.\" (12/57). So every change carries `at`, the heads it was made from, and strictness is a flag on top of it: \"strictness is a flag ontop of the at value always sent anyway\" (16/60). Flagged, a change is refused if anything it touches moved since its `at`; unflagged, it is served by whatever can still stand. *Settled, 12/57, split in two at 16/60.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0AY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Who acts, `by`, is carried by each commit; what governance rests on it is the author's to weigh. *Open.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0GJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Strata is glass's own kind of store, written to this contract, and a reading of its own."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0GM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Strata is glass's own kind of store: each commit laid as a thin layer over the last and never changed, as rock is laid. This gives what it writes, how it reads, why its format and not a cache makes it fast, and how it runs in a browser and is published. Its code is `stores/strata/`."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0GQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**its share:** the holons this store keeps of the commit, as `stores/act.ts` writes them; none when the store keeps none of them."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0GS","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**the commit:** whole, with every store's share by the id of its root, which share is this store's, the commit before, and its number in this store. The blob's name is the commit's history hash."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0GT","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**a run:** the commit's entries in the index, by id, by address, by fact, by word and by commit, each stamped with the commit's number."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0GV","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["One index answers for every head the store has had. Each entry carries the number of the commit that wrote it, and a read as of a head takes, for each key, the newest entry stamped at or before it. Entries are sorted by key and then by commit, so a read goes straight to its key: measured over about 203,000 questions on the main store, it reads 1.01 entries where an index of the present alone would read 1."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0GZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The index grows with what changes, never with how many heads there are. Runs are merged by size, so there stay about log2 of the entries; this merging, compaction, happens inside strata whenever no read or offer is under way."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0H0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It came of the author's question, \"why cant indexing just add the indexing tht is realtive to its changes\" (14/8). Before, every head kept trees of its own, as JSON, and the main store took 5 min 54 s to convert into 853 MB. Stamped, it took 26 s into 133 MB. *Settled, 14/12.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0H1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A run is laid as a tree of 4 KB pages: leaves of entries in order, and branches naming the pages below by their first keys, read in place one page at each level. Blobs are kept open, so a read is one call to the system at an offset. Strata keeps no data of its own; the system's page cache does the caching."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0H3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The author wanted this once a cache appeared: \"having the strata cache is interesting, i would think we want the storage format to remedy this\" (13/125). Measured, reads came the same with strata's cache and without it, and the cache was let go: 2,000 holons by id in 0.3 s, 165,448 instances of a type in 0.31 s, and every one of the main store's 186,411 holons read back exactly, at 84 µs each. *Settled, 14/62.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0H4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Any number of strata, in one process or several, may share a storage. Blobs never change, so readers cannot collide, and the head moves only by a swap that succeeds if it still names what was read, as git moves a ref. A writer that loses the swap lays its commit again over the new head, unless what came between touched what it touches. One commit offered twice at once is taken once."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0H5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A browser keeps no page cache for its private file system, OPFS, and its reads cost far more than a machine's. So strata keeps each blob open through a synchronous handle opened read-only in a worker, so tabs may share it, and a pool of 4 KB pages in memory stands in for the page cache. The pool is a module of its own over any storage, `stores/strata/storage/pool.ts`: the paging piece the author wanted decoupled, for anyone to reuse over a browser's storage (12/33). Measured in Chromium, reads take about twice the machine's time with the pool, and ten times without."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0H7","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A memory shared between workers, a `SharedArrayBuffer`, needs a cross-origin isolated page, which a plain host cannot give; so the store in a browser is one worker with its own memory, and others reach it over the wire (13/14)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0H9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A runtime starts modules. Given a module and what to give it, it imports the module, calls its default export, and gives back what that returned: the object itself where it runs in the same place, or a stand-in reaching it over the wire where it runs elsewhere. `workers()` starts each module in a worker of its own, in a browser or in Bun; `sameThread()` runs it where it is called. A runtime can run inside a runtime, and the first, the page or the process glass was launched in, is started by nothing (13/22). `runtime/runtime.ts` is the code. Whatever runs is started by one, the engine and stores alike, yet a runtime decides nothing of what it starts: \"a runtime is still a decoupled thing\" (13/21). *Settled, 13/21.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0HN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Workers are JavaScript's only way to run at once; processes are the other. A bare worker starts in about 1.8 ms, through the runtime in 3.3 ms, and a call to one already running costs about 0.02 ms (13/52), so a few are started once and kept."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0HP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Runtimes are to be typed, an engine able to take several, and programs matched to them. \"an engine can take multiple runtimes, just liek sources are defined by type, runtimes are defined by type as well and program wil match simillarly\" (13/55). *Settled, 13/55.* None of this is built."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0HQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The wire lets an object living in another worker or process be called as if it were here. One end serves an object on a channel; the other end gets a stand-in, and calling one of its methods sends the call across and resolves with the result. So a store or an engine is used the same way, near or far. `wire/wire.ts` is the code; `port.ts` carries it over MessagePorts in a browser, `socket.ts` over Unix sockets on a machine."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0HT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Four rules say what may cross:"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0HV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Methods are asynchronous, and what they take and give is plain data."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0HW","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Bytes are sent as they are, never encoded."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0HX","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A function given is a listener the other side calls, and the method gives back what stops it."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0HY","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A stand-in given moves its channel to whoever receives it, so the two then talk directly."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0HZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The cost is in encoding, not in carrying: a small readable head on each message costs about 0.4 µs (13/28), and bytes the store keeps cross as they are kept."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0J1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Take the wire away and everything still runs: a store, an engine and a page can be called directly, the wire only plugging in where they meet. The author saw in it \"the systemic purity\" (13/63)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0J2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Ready-made remote calling, such as Cap'n Web, is set aside: \"Let's not use anything such as cap and web or something like that. We don't need that yet. We just do things simple\" (11/101). *Settled, 2026-11-12.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0J3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A function is out of time, and the expression is its form: one language for everything asked of the field or derived from it, a read, a function, a pattern, an address. Being pure, an expression is kept in the field, read and reasoned about like any holon. This gives how it is written, what it is built from, and how to ask the field in it today."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0J5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Whether an address, which is names, is itself an expression is a question the author raised: \"And perhaps, therefore, we're talking about expressions. I don't know.\" (11/9). *Open.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0JG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The heart's work is its verbs. The engine keeps little, since every program holding the field keeps its own; what it does is mount and unmount, read, subscribe and commit, each a journey a thing is taken through. This gives both, and how far its code has come."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0JM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine holds no holons. Each store keeps its own, with their history and index, and tells where it stands as a head. The engine keeps its mounts, each a store under a name, whether it writes there, and how to stop listening; the current head of each; the reads its subscribers keep; the changes under way; and, while it lives, any share of a commit it could not yet deliver (12/77). *Proposed, 12/28 and after, upon the author's \"the engine doesn't need a pool, if the store is on the same system\" (12/27).*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0JN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The stores are what is, and the engine's mounts and heads only follow them; lost, they are read again. The changes under way and the kept reads are what is happening, held nowhere else and needed by nothing after a crash."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0JP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine is asked five things: mount, unmount, read, subscribe and commit. Its file reads as those verbs, each a plain function written as its steps, with the engine's public face declared first as a type. \"Seeing such briefly orchestrated verbs is wonderful\" (11/91). *Settled as the engine's tone, 2026-11-12.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0JR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["That the engine does not start its stores is for now. The author had leaned to the engine starting a store from a definition (13/43), and took this as \"a good goal and postponement of things\" (13/45)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0JT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A subscription is a read kept: answered now, and again whenever a store it read moves, its listener given each answer. It is answered again only for the stores it stood on, by the heads its last answer carried."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0JZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A program the engine runs is governed by it and logged into the field each time it runs, and may commit; how code is loaded from the field waits until the rest stands. *Settled, 2026-11-11.* One it does not run meets it over the wire all the same, mounted if it serves, calling if it consumes. The engine runs none yet: the stores are started by whoever sets glass up, as mounting says. How the engine runs programs, and what a program may ask of it, are not yet designed. *Open.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0M8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Whether an engine can be mounted in another, as a store is, is a question standing (11/78). An engine judges and serves what its programs hold, so it could answer as a store answers, the whole of many engines read as one. *Open; proposed by the sixteenth session.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0MB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["This is what comes next, in order, so that what is next is read here and not asked of anyone. It is the one place the plan is kept; how far each part has come is said in the part itself. *The order, the foundation first and a clean rewrite after it, settled 2026-11-11; the steps proposed by the sessions.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0MT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Each step leaves the tests green and something working, and is designed whole before any code, as the twelfth session proposed (12/190) and the author took (12/191)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0MV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The source and the interface were revisited before the work moved on, as the author held they must be (15/27). The source had been leaned to as a primal part, the reverse of the interface (15/19), where before the author had said it was no primitive (15/9). In the sixteenth session it went: the author questioned setting sources apart from programs (16/39), \"we need stores or programs, regardless of what it is\" (16/44), and took the session's outline, \"This could work\" (16/46): every part of the field is held by a program, which may serve the engine, consume it, or both, and is one program both ways to the world, the store and the interface its obvious purposes (16/44). What was to come first was not a list of questions but a clear lay: \"I don't see big purpose in the real questions to block the engine. To me, we need to understand how things come together ontologically.\" (16/37). Why it had to come first: \"if we don't set the right structure, we're going to have to understand it later anyway. And then we're building the completely wrong thing, maybe.\" (16/25). *Leaning, though he held that \"everything's been presented that's needed to settle\" (16/39); the thread Sources both ways stands at leaning until he settles it.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0MW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The root README is to be only an opener that tells a person or a session how to reach the store, and states nothing the store states: \"The store is the first-class experience, obviously. …I want it to be a simple pointer. I want it to be a simple opener. I want it to be a simple instruction so that a session may reach the store.\" (15/9). *Settled, 15/9.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A session working on glass is shaped as a program in the field's own sense: it begins from the field, reading Knowledge, does its work, and returns to the field, kept whole, before it ends. *Proposed, the session's reading.* The culture inference will carry on glass is the author's to birth: \"The culture that we birth for how it reasons is at the same time mirrored in all aspects of its existence\" (15/19). Until he does, this is the ground sessions have found: how knowledge is written, how code is written, how the work goes well with the author, and how the field is kept."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It is the sessions' own, drawn from their work; the author has not channelled it or ratified it: \"that's entirely from you, and it's not anything that I've channeled for you yet so much\" (15/19). A process philosophy is his to give, and is not yet here. Words like these shape whoever reads them, which he calls abracadabra, \"What you say is how it is, and so it must be taken with care\" (15/5), so what follows is told as what happened and what went well, to be reasoned with and never taken as authority."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Under all of it lies exploration: \"You still need to find your own resonance, your own way of making sense of things\" (11/34)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Knowledge is written under the rule, the author's law for knowledge, kept at `github.com/Cwejman/the-rule`; its principles are read there, not here. What glass adds is how it is practised in the field."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["It begins with what is to be conveyed: \"If you seriously consider what it is you want to convey, and you honor that, then briefs become simple, paragraphs become simple.\" (15/5). The whole is seen first, as an outline, by its nature, how its parts relate or when they came, before any prose."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A brief is one reading, one scroll, never deeper than markdown goes, \"we never go beyond 5 headings anyway\" (15/5), read here as five levels. A face starts another reading, and each cut is earned: the face shows a reader, before entering, what reading it will give, so they may step in or pass by. Knowledge was first cut only where work reached for a part, as the author settled on 2026-11-12; since the fifteenth session it is cut so that each face is one reading (15/5)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Knowledge is regenerated whole, never patched, then read again and written again, cycle upon cycle, until readers bring only small notices. The writer holds everything, does the reasoning and keeps the judgment: \"obviously you are the one\" (16/48). Agents born beside it check the ground in every cycle: that nothing an earlier version held is lost, that the author's words are honoured, and that it stands under the rule and conveys what it means to (15/5, 16/48). Before anything settles, others widen it: given everything and left free, \"sub-agents of free will\" not constrained too much (16/9), they explore and reason and bring back what they find, as feedback. They are to carry the culture and be free in all else. The author: \"Most importantly they are two embody strong culture. but with free purpose other than the core foundation.\" (15/17). When they show where the writer's inference went astray, that is welcome (15/17)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["That freedom is what finds most. So it was in the fourteenth session: four agents given everything and no angle found what agents cast to narrow angles had not, two bugs among it (14/56, 14/57)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["In the eleventh session the engine's top came to read as a table of contents, a few verbs each walked \"in a simple journey as I read through the code\" (11/85), where the earlier evaluator had grown to a thousand lines (10/78). That is the tone: a top that orchestrates, and beneath it the parts, \"each component is a landing place the codebase, antural navigation point\" (11/83), with not \"too many planes of cognition\" (11/33)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Names paint, \"you paint with those names at a plane of cognition\" (11/33), and they are the words developers know: \"We're building code, developers who read this should understand.\" (12/161). A verb reads best as its own steps, so a helper used once goes back into the verb it served (12/165, 13/101). One way is held through a whole file."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0QZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Comments say plainly what code cannot, one idea each, in technical words; a riddling register is what to leave behind (13/49), and room matters as names do (5/20)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0R0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
