{"body":{"text":["What glass learned from others is ground, never authority. Rich Hickey is the voice he reaches for (12/125, 13/33). From Datomic, Hickey's database: storage that only keeps, a past never changed, an index of all history. From Erlang: a failure contained where it happens. From Git: commits known by their content. And OpenLight, the author's earlier project: \"openlights is good for grounding though it is not to be taken as authority\" (7/22). *The schools, proposed, 11/72 and 11/74.*"]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0R9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What goes well is embodying, not reciting: \"I want you to embody my directives\" (11/3). That means starting from what is, not from how it was before, since a session is drawn to the old shape: \"you will be biased to generate something that is similar to how it was before. …I encourage you to not\" (15/7). It means understanding his words rather than cutting them up and saying them again (15/11), and not repeating them verbatim either (15/13). And it means not stating as fact what he only takes inspiration from, which \"might even push people away from understanding it\" (15/13)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RB","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Things go well when what is built is designed in dialogue first, \"understanding what you want to design before you write it\" (11/3), top down and from scratch (11/27, 12/5), with variants he can weigh, since \"how can I feel secure in what you present?\" (11/71). Yet \"we don't need to churn so much before\" (11/25), and a design looks past the piece at hand, to \"running programs and th elarger scope\" (11/29)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["When he is not following, fewer words help, and one picture. In the twelfth session long answers to his \"I don't understand\" lost him (12/59); short ones, each a single fact, brought him back (12/54, 12/55). He reads as his time allows (11/36). In the sixteenth session it held again: \"I'm not reading that wall of text\" (16/11), and what is said is grounded in the context, the field's records and what was said, never left floating (16/13)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What is settled is held, and a session's proposal does not overrule his lean (12/11). Yet what he has not settled may still move: \"it's not to say you can't progress and evolve this topic\" (16/19), while he takes time to \"find my own comprehension around things\" (16/27). The fourteenth session found again, under his question, the commit the same in every store, which strata had lost (14/20, 14/21); the storage handed in, and the format and not caches, had slipped the same way (12/135, 14/50)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RE","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The reasoning is the session's to do, and it can: \"You can have, we can have one exchange that is shit, and I can say the right things, and then you can cut through everything and it can be crystal clear. You definitely can. It's just not 100% secure that you will be able to.\" (14/28). Trust is kept by not running ahead of what was agreed (10/76), by answers neither lowballing his question nor opening what he did not ask (11/77, 11/79), and by going on \"not needing a manual finger\" (10/13). Reasoning that only follows, or hands his question back, fails him: \"Your reasoning is flat, simple, and you bounce back questions. You have an inherent capability to connect dots and present strong reasoning.\" (16/9); \"You're following things blindly. That is absolutely not your role.\" (16/25). Nor is a lay of his own ideas built up for its own sake: a concept that does not earn its place is let go, as reference was as a primitive of its own (16/44), and a slicing that does not help him think is not his (16/39)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Skepticism runs both ways, \"My claims are not. To be taken for granted.\" (7/8), and its ground is honesty: \"honesty and transparency are paramount for this interplay\" (10/8)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a session knows is in the field; memory is off, \"OpenLight had to set this boundary early\" (2/6). A session is kept whole in his words, every utterance as said, its answers by their essence, read against the transcripts by blank agents before it is trusted (11/105, 13/129). A stretch with a clear arc is marked as a cycle and condensed above it, so it need not be read whole (12/77), and the paths a session opened are kept as chosen or noted."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field is written today by the author's tools in `author/`, through the engine: `session.ts` keeps a session, `append.ts` adds an utterance, `thread.ts` raises and moves a thread, and `rewrite.ts` rewrites briefs; `author/README.md` says how. They go once the command line can commit, as the way from here orders. The author's direction is away from such scripts, which are rigid, toward clear types and structure and practices held as skills, so an agent knows how to work and does the work with the engine directly (15/31). One such practice: when Knowledge is regenerated, it keeps its id, and every sentence whose text is unchanged keeps its holon."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Reading every session to be aligned is \"going to be a debt soon\"; \"we haven't purified the knowledge\" (15/1, 15/3). Knowledge is that purifying, regenerated whole when the sessions have moved past it. How far the code has come changes quickly, and the author doubted keeping it here: \"That makes it very short-lived because it now has to stay true to everything. I'm not sure we want that. But maybe it's valuable.\" (15/7). *Proposed:* each part says it in a line, mended as the code moves."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A question becomes a thread: \"if something is a question, make it. In the substrate.\" (10/8). What a session did is committed before it ends, and no session starts on another's uncommitted work: \"We never want to start off a session with local changes.\" (4/2)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RN","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The words used across the parts without a brief of their own, each with its one meaning here; the primitives are given in the design. A word is gone over before what it names is built, and may change once it is (11/101)."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**whole:** a holon as what holds its parts."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RR","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**part:** a holon as what a whole holds; it may stand in many wholes."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RS","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**change:** what is asked to be committed, before it is judged."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RT","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**mould:** what a type says its instances hold, field by field."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RV","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**address:** a route of names through wholes."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RW","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**unit:** a single point whose failure takes others down; what glass avoids."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0RX","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**serve:** of a program, to hold part of the field and answer for it: be read, be followed, and take a judged change."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0S3","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**consume:** of a program, to call the engine's verbs, working upon the field."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0S4","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**pass:** one stretch of a program's work, from the field back to it."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0S5","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**integration:** a program holding something outside glass, both ways."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0S6","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**buffer:** holons whose changes are never committed, as characters being typed or an audio channel; read as a whole, of a type."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0S7","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**source:** the author's word, settled at 13/21, for what the engine mounts, leaned to as a primitive (15/19); since the sixteenth session, a program serving the engine."]},"id":"1M7JND1XQPFA0S8","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`read(head, question)` answers as the store was at a head: a holon by id, many holons at once, or one by address; a whole, a holon and what it holds to a depth, as far as the store keeps it; the facts matching a pattern, the holons saying a word, a holon's versions, the commits before the head, or whether a commit was taken. It answers in the store's own bytes, decoded only by whoever uses them."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC806A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`offer(commit)` puts a commit to the store, which answers accepted, with its new head; refused, with every problem; or changed, when something the commit touches changed after it was judged, so it must be judged again."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC807G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["`subscribe(listener)` tells the store's current head, and every later one, whoever moved it."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC807Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A commit's content is one everywhere: what it says, when, by whom, what its maker had read of the stores it touches, what it removes, and every store's share of it. Each store it touches keeps that content, naming every store the commit touched and the hash of its share there, though only its own share's holons; and each keeps it at its own place in its own history, after whatever commit came before it there."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC80AF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Making a commit all or nothing across stores was weighed and let go: a shared head, drafts activated later, two-phase commit, sagas, a primary store. Each makes one store depend on another, and none closes the gap; each only moves it. So the engine tells whoever committed what landed, and keeps a share it could not deliver while it lives. \"We're choosing to postpone the problem because we don't see an automagical solution to it. Fine. …Acceptable.\" (12/77). *Settled as hygiene, not a solution, 12/77.*"]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC80DD","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What is built is less. The engine tells whoever committed where it landed, and what each store it missed answered. Nothing yet marks a holon diverged when a commit lands in one store and misses another, nothing finds the later commit's version, and nothing keeps the share that was not delivered."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC80F4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**mount:** the engine's verb: to take a running program that holds the field, a store as it is written today, and follow its head."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC822K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**verb:** what the engine is asked: mount, unmount, read, subscribe, commit; each a journey."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC8234","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**subscription:** a read kept, answered again when what it stood on moves."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC823K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**at:** the heads a read stood on; with a change and kept in its commit, the heads of the touched stores it was made from, empty when made without reading."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC824M","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**when:** a commit's moment."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC824V","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**strict:** of a change, refused if anything it touches moved since its `at`."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC825C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**touches:** the holons and addresses a change writes or places; changes meet where these overlap."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC825Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**refused:** a change answered with the rules it broke."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC826A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**changed:** a store's answer that what a change touches moved since it was judged."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC826V","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**worker:** one of the engine's threads, all the same, each with its own connection to every store, that reads and takes a commit through judging, minting and offering."]},"id":"1M7K34ED9ZC827T","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A maker hands back the `at` its read answered; the engine keeps of it only the heads of the stores the change touches, so a commit names nothing of stores it does not stand in. It may be empty, for \"of course somthign must be able to commit without reading\" (16/62): an importer, a recording, the command line, a test. A store the maker never read has no head in it. The engine checks that each head given is in its store's history, so no maker can claim to have seen a state that never was. Every commit keeps its `at`, so history shows what each maker had seen of what it changed. *Settled, 16/60 and 16/62, upon the session's answers 16/59 and 16/61, the check among them; that only the touched stores' heads are kept is the session's, 16/53, not yet weighed by the author.* It is in the code: a commit's moment is called `when`, the session's name, which the author found acceptable (17/17), and its `at` names each touched store's head by the store's root, within the content hash."]},"id":"1M7K3SXRBT110DX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["For reading, strata holds beside its blobs only the head it last read and each commit's number: a commit never changes, and the runs listed for a later head answer for every earlier one, their entries being stamped. A head asked of that is newer, or a blob gone missing under a read, has the head read again. Holding the head was weighed against 14/62 and taken: \"Head in memory sounds fine\" (17/35). *Settled, 17/35; holding each commit's number is the session's.* Many keys are answered in one sweep of each run, the keys sorted, each page read once. One question by id takes 16 µs where it took 51, and the whole of Knowledge, 14,067 holons, 83 ms where it took 368."]},"id":"1M7K3SXRBT110HZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The workers are started on the runtime the engine is given, so the engine has one path with workers or without. An engine without them gave the author the ick: \"Single-threadedness just gives me the ick. The engine is supposed to be reliable.\" (12/171). The session answered that one heavy read would hold everyone, and one gone wrong would stop everyone. *Proposed, 13/55 to 13/60.*"]},"id":"1M7K3SXRBT110ZV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["They are one pool, every worker the same, reading and committing, and the engine's own thread keeps only what must be one: \"I want as little as possible to be on the main thread of the engine\" (17/7). With more than one worker, reads and commits each hold at most all but one, so neither leaves the other waiting. *Settled, 17/7 to 17/15, upon the session's answer 17/10.*"]},"id":"1M7K3SXRBT11124","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The author asked, of checking only at the end, \"do you really need to do the full work only to by the end realize if a batch has to be redone though?\" (11/61). So what a change touches is known from the change alone, before any work, and it waits only on changes it meets (11/59). Rules over more than the holons a change names, such as a pattern over a whole type, would need its reach widened or such changes taken one at a time. *Open.* A change is judged at most three times in all, then refused as changed. *Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M7K3SXRBT111AK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Mounting takes a store already running, the one kind of program the engine is written to mount, started by whoever set glass up, near or over the wire. It gives each of the engine's workers its own connection to the store, and subscribes to the store's head; each move records the new head and reruns the reads that stood on that store. A store that stops is unmounted. Whether the engine writes to a store is said on mounting. *Settled, 2026-11-11.*"]},"id":"1M7K3SXRBT111XM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So that divergence is never silent, a read asks every store for every holon it reads, and where two stores keep one differently its answer names the holon as diverged beside its value: \"transparency is important, not silent lies\" (17/17). For now the first store mounted that keeps it gives the value, and the later commit's version is not yet found. *Proposed, 17/20, built 17/40; the author let reads ask every store until divergence is marked, 17/61.* Where the mark is to be kept is not yet designed. Once it is, a read may ask for a holon only where holding says it lies, since a commit puts a holon in every store whose wholes hold it: a part in the store of the whole that holds it, and what is only pointed to in that store and the stores it stands on. *Open; the thread Where divergence is marked.*"]},"id":"1M7K4179QB62087","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Addresses are first class beside ids. Of two holons given one name in one whole at once, the author said: \"colliding addresses really shouldn't be possible. I mean, the store is based on addresses\" (12/61). So a commit is known to touch the addresses it places, a whole and a name, as well as the holons it writes, and a change placing a name its whole already holds is refused. *Settled, 12/61; the refusal built in the new engine by the eighteenth session.* Code names what it needs by address, never by id. *Settled, 2026-11-11.*"]},"id":"1M7KPZ2J0MZ701X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A pattern reads holons as facts, `[e, a, v]`: what a holon is an instance of, its name, its store, each value its body holds under a key, and what it holds, under `$holds`. `find` gives what makes its clauses hold, variables shared between clauses being the links; `said` finds a word under a key whatever its case or accent, or, of a holon known, the words it says there; `explain` says the plan."]},"id":"1M7KPZ2J0MZ7037","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A change is taken through its steps to become a commit. First its turn, among the changes under way that touch the same holons or addresses, or put new holons into the root of the same store, the one it names or the only one written, and only those, strict or not, since one under way may yet be refused. Then, on a worker, it is judged against the field, every problem at once, its `at` checked to name heads its stores have had, a name it places in a whole refused where the whole already holds it, and, where it asks for strictness and its `at` names only heads its stores have had, refused if what it touches moved since. Then its ids are minted, after judging, so problems speak the caller's own names for holons not yet born. Last it is offered to each store it touches. Refused, it returns its problems as a value, never thrown. Where it landed in none and some store answered changed, it is judged again at the heads they answered with; where it landed in some, it returns where it landed and what each other store answered, or that it failed."]},"id":"1M7KPZ2J0MZ7081","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A refusal is expected: a change broke a rule, and is answered with every problem. A failure is unexpected, storage gone, a hash wrong, a fault: it is said to whoever asked, and one read's failure never reaches another. A store failing a read fails that read, saying why; for now every read asks every store, so a store that fails fails every read. A store failing as a commit is offered is said beside where the commit landed. Nothing fails silently."]},"id":"1M7KPZ2J0MZ709C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Two primitives are pure: the function, which derives from the field, and the component, which draws it, its purity proposed here. Each gives the same for the same, and changes nothing; what is in time stands on them. Both are applied alike, by a use, and both declare alike what they take; their types say who carries them out, the engine a function, a chassis, what draws components on one surface, a component."]},"id":"1M7R53AYWWN102C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Taking arguments belongs to a type, never to a holon as such: a holon with holes is no longer complete, readable alone, nor the same everywhere it appears. A type opens holes in its instances by its mould, function and component first; a program is started, never applied. The author put it to the archetype, \"Unless it's up to the archetype whether or not it can be a function or not\" (18/81), and asked whether taking arguments is only templating: \"There is nothing actually run, right? That is still up to the type you declare and whoever handles it\" (18/83). *Settled, 18/93, upon the session's answers 18/82 to 18/88.*"]},"id":"1M7R53AYWWN1060","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A function is pure: given the same, it gives the same, and changes nothing. It is out of time, the same truth sounding whenever it is struck; the author hears resonance in it, truth that is there \"without necessarily the series of thought\" (15/13). Because the field is one truth, all that follows from it can be derived by functions and never stored twice, and every function multiplies the ways the field can be seen. Turning holons of one type into another is a function too, found by the types it takes and gives, which may be asked of it as anything may be asked of a holon: \"I don't see anything special with function\" (18/93). *Proposed; how it is found, settled, 18/93.*"]},"id":"1M7R53AYWWN107M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The call within an expression, the mount, and the statistic, an expression a brief holds and reads wherever it is drawn, were each an application of their own, and become this one: mount already said of itself that it is a call, and the statistic that it waited for functions to be holons to call (18/82). A use is no instance of what it applies, since a type says what keys its instances hold, and every use holds the same keys whatever it applies; and a holon may be an instance of several types, where a use applies exactly one thing (18/64, said simply at 18/66, from OpenLight's own reason). The author asked why it could not be an instance of, and took the separate type with the rest (18/65, 18/93). *Settled, 18/93.*"]},"id":"1M7R53AYWWN10H3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Beside the one-line form above, any holon may be written whole in plain text, as the author found helpful: \"the way of using the honest HCL for hold-ons, it is helpful\" (18/77). The type comes first and then the name; within, every line is a key and its value; a block written at a key is held there, and `ref(x)` points. Lisp, whose text is its tree, was weighed and let go as hard for people to read (18/77). *Leaning, 18/77; a readable spelling for definitions is a path the session noted.*"]},"id":"1M7R53AYWWN10RF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A native over values gives null for what it cannot use, so a guard can always be written; a malformed pattern is refused, its failure the read's answer. A function is found as any holon is, by asking: what it takes and gives is in its body (18/93). *Settled, 18/93.*"]},"id":"1M7R53AYWWN112Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component shows the field. It is a holon, declared once and realized for each surface, in code on the web, in Swift on a phone, or wholly in the field as layout and data: \"to declare and define a component for different types of chassis is definitely important\" (18/31), though only the web is built now. It is found by type: given what is to be shown, the component whose type fits takes it, and opens places within itself where further components take what it points to. It draws what it is given and the field; a person's edit, or anything else that changes, is the interface's doing, given among programs."]},"id":"1M7R53AYWWN115M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A use may offer, as the author held of mounts, \"you may add offers, right? And they propagate down the tree\" (18/15): what it offers fills an optional input of that type in every use beneath it that was given none, the nearer before the farther, and not in the interface alone, as a function formatting a date wants a locale (18/70). *Offer among a use's keys, settled 18/93; how it fills beneath, proposed 18/70.* A component opens a place for each value that refers further, and what stands there is shown by whatever fits it, so each component draws its projection of the field as one holarchy, as deep as the field is broken down. A component is a pure function of what it is given and of the field."]},"id":"1M7R53AYWWN11F6","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["After these: programs beyond the store and the interface, a pass of a completion first among them, then integrations both ways; and what the engine may ask of a runtime. *Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M7R53AYWWN127V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The foundation is built, and the field is kept in five stores, all in strata. The engine, written anew, reads and commits over them, every expression in them now written as uses, and the interface draws on it at `/`; the earlier engine and its format are gone, and every other program is still to be built."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS01V","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Erasing is still possible: a store may be let go, and taking holons out of a store will be needed (15/21). The lexicon was so erased: cleared at the author's word, \"Actually, do clear the lexicon. Do clear it.\" (18/105), and stripped from history on the session's reading of the author's \"read the history of the lexicon\" (18/105, 18/106); git alone still keeps it. Commit is kept as the developer's word on purpose, plain where plain serves (15/9)."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS039","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An address is a route of names through wholes, `Knowledge/The design/The foundation`, and may begin at a store, `@glass:prose/brief`. A reference is an id, so moving or renaming a holon changes no reference, while an address finds it by its names."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS04M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A paragraph holds its sentences and a sentence its words; a word is what comes before it, its text, and what comes after. The text is made from the holons each time it is read and never stored. Nor is a lexicon stored beside them: the words prose uses are derived, by `lexicon()`, and the lexicon once stored, a second source of truth already apart from the first, is gone: \"of course we won't have a stored lexicon\" (18/103). *Settled, 18/103.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS063","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A type's mould may also declare an `input`, so that its instances are applied by a use and filled by what each use gives: function and component first, others when a real case asks, a brief with holes perhaps, or a program's configuration, filled and ready to start, the program itself started, never applied (18/84, 18/86). An instance fills its type's mould by being stored, and so can be cited and indexed; what a use gives is derived, and kept only if a program commits it. *Settled, 18/93, upon the session's answer 18/86; which types open holes beyond function and component waits on a case; built for function and component.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS06Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An expression is uses held within each other. A **use** is a holon of the type use: it names what it applies, `fn`, a function or a component, and holds what it gives it, `args`, in order: values, references to holons, and further uses. A use is held where it is consumed, at its place in the args of the use that takes it, and so it is namespaced there, as any held holon is: \"It is simply namespaced\" (18/89). It needs no name, and is seen inline (18/69). One that is reused is named and pointed at, and to point at a use is to take what it gives: \"Reusing is the same thing as patching into its output, really\" (18/57). Change it, and every use that points at it follows. A lambda becomes a small function held where it is written. *Settled, 18/93, upon the session's answer 18/92; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS079","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["An expression is pure, and depends on nothing in the engine. Its parts being holons, the interface can take it apart and edit each one, as a bar shows a query's steps as pills (18/71, 18/72); an input that takes a use is given the use itself, and any other what the use gives (18/70). *That rule proposed, 18/70; built.* At what grain an expression looks upon the field, and upon its commits, is the author's to continue: the thread Grain and detachable depth (18/55). Every expression in the stores is uses now, moved over once for good, and the engine reads uses alone. `language/text.ts` reads text into uses and prints them back, as glass's natives `parse` and `print` do; `print` writes a pipe as nested calls, so only text written as it writes reads back the same."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0A1","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A use is written as a function's name with its args in parentheses. `@` names a holon by its id, its name, or a route of names, which may begin at a store: `@glass:prose/brief`; `@\"…\"` is a name with spaces. `x => …` is a lambda, `m.key` what m holds under key, and `a | f(b)` is f(a, b). Lists are `[…]`, records `{key: …}`, strings stand in double quotes, `?x` is a pattern's variable, and `//` begins a remark."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0AZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A function is a holon of the type function. Its `input` is the list of what it takes, each a placeholder of the type it takes, held at its place and named so the function's body can point at it, and matched by its type, never by its name or a key: building structure with a record's keys is \"proprietary and it's not of the principles\" (18/25), and a whole config is given as a whole: \"define it as a whole on a reference\" (18/27). One that may be left unfilled is marked so on its link, `$optional`, as holding is marked `$holds` (18/71, 18/72). A function names a native, run by the engine, or holds a use as its body, built upon other functions (18/57). The mould's `takes` gives way to `input`, the author's choice: \"Perhaps input is the most pure of them\" (18/89); what a use gives it is its `args`. What can be applied is found by its type's mould declaring an input, not by a type named function; and a use whose args do not fit its function's input is refused when judged, the problem saying why, as \"it gives pair 4 args, and pair takes at most 3\"; a placeholder is a hole of its type, holding nothing, its type's mould not asked of it. *Settled, 18/93, upon the session's answer 18/92; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0DG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A function may name its `reverse`, and two that name each other are a pair, each the way back of the other: \"maybe functions can come in pairs if they both name each other in their reverse\" (18/61). Parse and print are one, steps and chain another. Pairs joined in an expression make a larger function that goes both ways (18/55). Through a pair, a view written back gives a change proposed, which the interface offers as a commit, so an edit stays the interface's doing (18/88, 18/89). The way back is built: a value proposed where a drawing stands walks back through placeholders, through `each` item by item, and through any function naming its reverse, to a `get`, whose holon it changes, as typing in the bar and removing a pill reach the query. *Settled, 18/93; built, a function naming a reverse that does not name it back refused, and one of a pair never let go alone.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0FV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Natives are small pure functions in code, in families: the lazy ones, `if`, `case`, `and`, `or`; values; lists; sets, which are hashed; holons, `holon`, `whole`, `in`, `out`, `follow`; history, `log`; and patterns; and the pairs glass ships, `parse` and `print`, `steps` and `chain`, with `each`, `group` and the way back, `back`. Beside them stand legacy natives, `type`, `store`, `named`, `children` and `since` among them, kept only while functions written in the field still call them. Everything else is written in the field upon the natives."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0HT","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine asks each store's index for the facts of each clause and joins them itself, planning each clause by what it fixes, a holon, a key with its value, or a key alone, since a store does not say how many facts it would give. The author saw no way around the engine's joining: \"The only alternative is the engine holding everything in memory, which doesn't make sense according to our principles.\" (17/27). *Leaning, 17/27, upon the session's answer 17/28; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0KM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["`engine/ask.ts` mounts every store the repository holds on an engine here and asks it one expression, read into uses by the native `parse`: `bun engine/ask.ts 'text(@Knowledge)'` reads this space as prose, in about 0.7 s, and `outline(@Knowledge, 3)` gives its shape. A holon comes back by its route and what it is, as `@Knowledge (brief)`. What each function does is asked the same way: `find(?f, [?f, \"instance\", @glass:language/function]) | map(f => {name: f.name, says: f.says})`."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0NR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store keeps. It holds holons with the commits that changed them, sovereign, and strata is glass's own. Of the purposes a program has, it is the first the author named: \"the store is an obvious purpose, and the interface is another one obvious\" (16/44). The field here is kept in five stores, cut from the history of the four before them, and the engine is written over them."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0PJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The field this repository holds is five stores, each a strata store, each found by the `.glass/` beside what it is about. Glass, at the repository's root, holds glass's own types grouped as wholes, store, language, prose and interface, with the functions and components it ships. Wiki, in `wiki/`, holds Knowledge, the threads and the old wiki as it stood, and keeps the root id of the store once called main. Author, in `author/`, holds the author's words, As it was said, the sessions, the measures and the statistics, and paper and paper-readings stand beneath it. *Proposed, 18/104, the author answering it point by point at 18/105; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0T5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass stays one store, its things namespaced within it as wholes, so each may later be loaded and depended on alone: \"It actually has its own structure, so maybe that's fine because we're namespacing inside the store anyway\" (18/105). The store holding Knowledge is wiki: \"Maybe we want to call it wiki\" (18/105). Measures and statistics stand with what they relate to: \"they should probably be stored with where they are\" (18/105); the cut put the measures with the author, since every one points at a session. *Leaning, 18/105.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS0X4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["They were cut from history, not copied at its head: each old commit, replayed in order, was written once across the stores it touched, 575 in all, every holon placed by the whole it last stood in, and the five together were found equal to the old field, holon for holon, each reading true alone. *The cut, settled 18/105: \"Sounds fine to create a cut file for now\".* The lexicon, both lexicons, their lexemes and the 111,011 references words made to them, was cleared at the author's word, \"Actually, do clear the lexicon. Do clear it.\" (18/105), and stripped from all of history as if never written; that it went from history and not only from the present is the session's reading, at 18/106, of the author's \"read the history of the lexicon\" (18/105). The cut ran once, and its script went, its run kept in history."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS11X","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Then, committed through the engine, every expression was written again as uses, once for good; glass's types were grouped, a second function type and the paper's own prose types let go for glass's, and the markdown forms and the types nothing used let go. Git keeps only each store's history, about 48 MB, and each index is rebuilt from it. *Proposed, 18/104; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS141","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The old wiki still stands in the wiki store, as The wiki, kept as it stood. The author would let it go if it holds nothing Knowledge does not, since \"it's still available as commits in history, so if you want to read it you still can\" (18/105). A blank reading found Knowledge carrying all its live substance, and absent only reasoning: the survey of formats and why glass's own, why paragraphs are holons, the relation kinds carried from OpenLight and why each was dropped, and taking a whole away. *Open: whether that reasoning comes into Knowledge first awaits the author.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS17C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Each store has one root, a holon of the type store. The root holds the store's first holons, from which the rest is reached; names the stores it stands on, its dependencies; and names its shape, the types it admits, where a shape naming none admits any. Nothing in the root says where or how the store is kept, so a store moved or served another way is the same store. Two stores may depend on each other. *Settled: dependencies 2026-11-10, shape 2026-11-12.* The engine judges the shape, as it judges every commit."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS17Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["How a bare id finds the dependency it lies in is not yet designed. A whole was taken away once, when main was cut into stores by replaying its history, as the stores here tell; how a whole taken away is born as a store of its own, by the field's own working and not a script run once, is not yet designed either. *Open.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1A5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["All of strata's data is in two storages, its history and its index, each of blobs named by the SHA-256 of their bytes and never changed, and a head, the only thing that changes. For each commit it takes, strata writes:"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1B9","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The history's head is a short text naming the latest commit; the index's names the runs that make up the index and the commit they reach. An offer moves the history's head and indexes its own commit; compaction moves only the index's. The commits are the history and the index is derived from them: an index missing, behind, or from a history replaced catches up from the history on the first read or offer, about 13 s for the wiki's, and `stores/strata/rebuild.ts` rebuilds one whole."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1E2","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A rebuilt index answered 262,000 questions on the wiki and 669,000 on the author's store as the live one did. So git keeps each store's history alone, 19 MB for the wiki against 40 MB of index left out, and the index is rebuilt on clone."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1FK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The site's build writes each store as it stands, its history's head and its index's and every blob they reach, gzipped, to `strata/<name>/`; the browser unpacks each with `DecompressionStream` before checking it against its name. The index is fetched, never built, since building would cost every visitor. What a read waits on is fetched at once, and, when a store is loaded whole, the rest after it, the index first. The store once called main came to 12.4 MB over the wire where it had been 119.8; its index arrives in 0.2 s and every blob in 4.6 s, reads answered all the while."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1HV","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Noted, not done; the index trailing the commits, noted here before, is done as what it writes gives, though an offer still indexes its own commit."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1JQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A published store could be loaded a page at a time, by HTTP range requests."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1K8","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Runs a merge replaced are kept 10 s for readers elsewhere, which the author found \"a little bit hacky\" (14/38), and are left behind when the process that merged exits first. Shares and runs that no head names are left for a sweep, and no sweep exists."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1MT","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A merge holds whole runs in memory, and owes a streaming merge for stores bigger than memory."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1ND","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A store compacts only after its own process offers to it, so a store rebuilt and then only read keeps the runs it was left with, never merged further."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1PC","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["A miss, an id asked of a store that keeps none of it, costs a sweep of about two pages a run, and most of it is making and sorting keys. A filter per run, or runs merged more eagerly, would save a few milliseconds a read and bend what 14/62 and 14/12 settled. The author asked a free-will panel before either bent what is settled (17/43), and the panel let both go for now (17/44). *Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1RZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The browser's queue and gzip path are checked by a bench, not by tests, and only in Chromium; the fallback for browsers without `createWritable` has never run."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1SW","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Glass's earlier format, blocks and a log in each module's `.glass/`, is gone with the earlier engine; what it held is in strata, and its code stays in git's history."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1TX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["So the interface is a program, the other obvious purpose (16/44), with what is primal in it the component: \"The interface is a primitive, sure, for it has components\" (16/17). *Leaning, 16/44.* His doubt stands beside it: \"An integration is a program. That's the traditional view of OpenLight. But again, doesn't make the interface a program. I don't know if I'm ready to stand by that.\" (16/23). It runs today over the engine, at `/`."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1V8","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component draws one projection of the field as one holarchy, and the interface is many of them within each other, placed on a page. This gives how a component is found and placed, what the page decides and what it does not, the reader it draws, and what is left of the home and the site."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS1WA","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component is a holon, and says in it only what it says, its `input`, and its body where it is data. The code that realizes it on the web is kept by the web's chassis, found by the component's id and never its name, in `interface/web/realized.ts`; a chassis on another surface keeps a map of its own. *Where web code lives, the session's, at the author's word \"use common sense\" (18/95, 18/96); built.* Some components, as the reader and search, are defined wholly in the field, as layout and data (15/19). *Components as holons, settled 2026-11-11.* A component declares its `input` as a function does, a list of types matched by type (18/27), and is applied by a use, which names it and gives it what it is to show; mount folds into use, \"I'm fine with the dropping mount until we feel the need of it again\" (18/71). *Settled, 18/93; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS21C","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A use naming no component is drawn by the one whose first required placeholder takes a type of the field the value fits: a brief draws as a brief. A component over a kind of value alone, a list or a string, is drawn only where a use names it, since many take one shape for different ends; the one taking any value comes last, showing any holon as its values, so nothing is left unshown. One found by type is written into the use as its `fn` where the use's store takes the change, and found again each time where not; where several fit, a chooser lists them and the person's pick is drawn, never guessed. *Picked once and written, proposed, 18/88; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS25E","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Layout as data was held to the test of the search bar, which takes a query and shows its steps as pills: `steps` gives the query's steps, `each` makes one use of the pill per step, and a list lays them beside an input; removing a pill flows back through the way back of each, then `chain`, then `print`, into the address (18/72). The pill and the input are code at the leaves, the arrangement around them data. \"If it can't, then we have a problem with layout as data\" (18/71). Built, the test came out mixed: the arrangement is data, the reader laying search above the answer and search laying the text's steps as pills beside the input, both shipped in glass, while the leaves, pill, input, list and answer, the ways back through each, steps and chain, and dropping an item from a list when its × is pressed are code (18/98). *Proposed, 18/72; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS27M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Completion in the bar is code within the input leaf: after `|` it offers the functions the field holds, with what each says and takes, and after `@` holons by name, each read through the engine as any question is; only the bar's arrangement is data. It may become a component of its own, taking the text and given its options by a read, so it can be swapped and seen by the inspector. *Proposed, 18/104.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS2A5","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What components say of themselves is in their holons alone; the declarations in their code are gone. *Settled, 2026-11-11; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS2AX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The page hosts and decides little: it starts the engine and each store in a worker of its own, mounts the stores, and draws its root read, Reader given the query's text, turning the address, back and forward, into what it draws. Which components show, and how they are laid out, are read from the field. It is `site/page.ts`, served at `/`."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS2D0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The query is a buffer, holding only the present, kept as one with the address, `?q=`: loading, back and forward type the address into it, each change replaces the address, and pressing Enter or following a link pushes a step, so a link moves within the page and the engine keeps running. Each keystroke goes back from where the input is drawn to the buffer's text, which alone is written. The page names its stores in its own code, as the author leaned: \"the site that we want built will define its stores in the sites. ts i would think\" (11/7), and took at 18/17: \"on point three: ok\". *Settled, 18/17.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS2GP","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The reader is what the page draws: a component of data laying search above the answer, both given the query's text, search parsing it itself so the way back ends in `print` and lands in the buffer. *Text and not a use, the session's, at the author's word \"use common sense\" (18/95, 18/96); built.* Search lays the text's steps as pills beside an input that continues them: typing `| something` adds a step, anything else asks anew, and Backspace in the empty input takes the last step back to edit. Pressing a pill's × proposes the steps without it, back through `each`, `chain` and `print` into the address, which keeps names. The answer follows on Enter, not as one types."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS2MM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Right-click shows that place, as the author asked, \"to be able to see that particular mount\" (18/99): the component drawing it, what it was given, the uses it was reached through, as Reader› List› Answer› Value, and the holon it shows, by name, type, store, the language's name for it and its id. Its last line opens the reader's own layout, so the site's layout can always be found; Shift gives the browser's menu, and a phone a sheet. With no query, the page starts from the stores. *Asked by the author, 18/99; what it shows the session's, found \"more helpful\" at 18/101; built.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS34F","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The home was the reader's own store, written by default. The site's home under `bun run serve` is gone, since which pages one visited is the browser's own history: \"Yes, lets rely on the history stack instead.\" (18/17). *Settled, 18/17.* The page still mounts a home of its own in the browser's storage, written to, which the session let go in word (18/96) and the code not yet. *Open: whether it goes wholly.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS36Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A site is a page that starts glass upon stores it names in its own code. This project's site is built from every store the repository holds, read as it stands, nothing converted; `bun run serve` serves each store live from its folder, and every page starts its own engine over what it is served, so a page opened after a commit made by the author's tools reads it. The site store, `site.json` and the attachments are gone, as the author took (18/17)."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS39K","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A buffer is holons whose changes are never committed: characters being typed, an audio channel. \"Buffers they don't have commit\" (11/73); forty-eight thousand samples a second are not forty-eight thousand commits. Its information is external, found as channels are or made as one spawned for a string (16/25), and read as a whole it is of a type, as the characters are a string: \"a buffer may be a string. What's the problem?\" (16/44). Some of what a buffer gives, a recording or a preset, may be committed, and when a commit refers to a buffer, whatever refers to it keeps it for a lifetime the buffer declares. *Proposed, 11/70 and after.* Whether a commit naming one keeps the value or only the pointer is open. *Open.* One is built, the string buffer."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS3AX","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The string buffer was built before the interface, as the author asked: \"let's build buffers before building the interface\" (18/15). It is a store in memory, in any runtime, keeping the store's contract: an act replaces what it touches and moves the head, and nothing earlier is kept. It keeps the names of its heads, so a change's `at` is checked as any store's, but not what they held, so a strict change made from before the present is refused, since it cannot tell what moved; one not strict is taken. A string is one holon whose body holds its text, as the page's query is."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS3EC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The wire makes all places one, and here is how: four rules for what may cross, and runtimes that start whatever runs. Stores and the engine are written this way; other programs are to."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS3ET","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine, `engine/`, the language and strata's core are written to web standards, so they run in a browser as on a machine; only what reaches a machine's files and sockets uses Node's modules, in Bun. *Proposed; the author asked whether it should (11/99).*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS3G0","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A read is uses worked out over the stores, as they stood when it began, carrying any holons of its own not yet in a store, as a query typed reaches the engine uncommitted. It runs on the first free worker, so a slow read holds up only its own. The holons it asks for within one turn are asked of every store as one question, so a walk asks once a layer, and it waits only on what it does not yet hold. It answers its value or its problem, the holons it found diverged, and `at`: the head of every store it read, as an ETag names a version."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS3H4","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The engine, `engine/`, is the one engine: the earlier engine, its page and components and its format went once the stores moved, and the new engine took its path. It reads uses alone. A read carries holons of its own not yet stored; a function's input is bound to a use's args in order and by type, an optional placeholder filled from the nearest offer of its type; a lambda is a held function; and what can be applied is what its type's mould says takes `input`. A use whose args do not fit is refused at commit, by the same matching the evaluator binds with. Pairs are judged, and the way back walks a value proposed to a change."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS3N3","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Its commits are judged, minted and landed in strata, tested with stores that fail, refuse or answer changed every time, with many changes, and with two engines over one storage at once. The page at `/`, the command line and the author's tools all read and commit through it, and 257 tests pass. Before the earlier engine went, the new one was held to it question by question over every store: 60 the same, 11 refused by design, and 6 apart from the migration itself. It runs on Bun 1.4.4, since Bun 1.3.11 lost a message now and then on MessagePorts between workers."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS3RF","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Reading Knowledge as text grew slower over uses: about 0.37 s before them, 0.46 s after on one thread, and about 0.7 s at the command line now over the five stores, the time spread over walking each use and one round trip to the stores a layer, with no single hotspot; a brief's sections take about 0.4 s on the site. It is to be measured again where the interface shows which reads matter. Still between: `language/text.ts` keeps the earlier form of expressions for its own tests alone."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS3VC","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The interface shows what components drew of what functions derived from the field, and subscribes, so it will be told when that changes. Someone, a person on a page or a program, offers a change. The engine sees what the change touches, waits only for changes under way that touch the same, judges it against the field and its types, gives what is new its ids, and offers it to every program holding what it touches, across the wire where they run apart. Each takes it or refuses it against its own truth; a store keeps its share as a commit, moves its head, the point its history has reached, and tells the engines listening. Whatever was refused, by the engine or by a program holding what it touched, reaches whoever offered the change. The holons stand changed; the functions derive again; the components draw what is now. *Proposed; the engine's part of it runs, save divergence, as said under A commit across stores, and the interface is upon it, though the only change it yet offers is to its query.*"]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS3WG","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What is open stands in the brief it is about, with its lean, so it is read where it matters. Questions held as threads in the field are asked of it: `find(?t, [?t, \"instance\", @wiki:types/thread]) | map(t => {name: t.name, stands: t.stands})`."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS44M","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**native:** a function written in code."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS44X","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**use:** a function or a component applied to what it is given, a holon held where it is consumed."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS45K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**input:** what a function or a component takes, a list of types, each named for pointing within."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS467","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**placeholder:** a hole of a type, held at an input and named for pointing within; it holds nothing."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS46W","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**args:** what a use gives what it applies, in order."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS479","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**pair:** two functions that name each other as their reverse."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS47P","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**way back:** a value proposed where a drawing stands, walked back through what gave it to a change that would give it."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS48F","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**chassis:** what draws components on one surface, the web or a phone."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS48Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**realization:** a component's code on one surface, kept by that surface's chassis by the component's id."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS49H","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**root:** a store's one holon of the type store, naming its dependencies and shape."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4A3","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**shape:** the types a store admits."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4AC","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**dependency:** a store another store's field stands on."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4AQ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**storage:** where a store's bytes rest: blobs by hash, and a head; a strata store has two, its history and its index."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4BG","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**head:** a point in a store's history, named by a commit's two hashes."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4C0","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**share:** the holons one store keeps of a commit; a part, in the code."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4CH","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**diverged:** a holon two stores hold differently, after a commit landed in one and not the other."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4D5","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**strata:** glass's own kind of store."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4DE","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**history:** in strata, a store's commits and shares, all that git keeps of it."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4DZ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**index:** in strata, the runs derived from the history, rebuilt from it when missing or behind."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4EJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**run:** in strata, a sorted piece of the index, its entries stamped with commits."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4F3","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**compaction:** merging runs, so fewer are read."]},"id":"1M7Z36D2Q5RS4FD","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["Of the views the earlier page had, brief came back as code, since reading Knowledge is the point; session, thread, utterance, board, timeline and cycle fall back to the plain value view, to return as data if missed; face and full wait. A brief reads its first paragraph as the rest, the lede let go at the author's word (19/5), and its sections read through. *The session's, at the author's word to use common sense, 18/96.*"]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A400R","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The site is published as the repository's pages on GitHub, built from main by its workflow at every push, on the author's own domain (19/25). The build copies each store and prepares its index; that the published site might instead read the repository itself, as git serves it in plain files, is the git integration's to show (19/21, 19/24)."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A40RW","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["No way is built now: the reading of git went with the earlier engine it was built on, and git comes back first, as given beneath. Writing back, and every other way below, is still to be."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A40SR","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**page:** what hosts glass in a browser, and decides little."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41DW","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**reader:** the component the page draws, search above the answer, given the query's text."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41ED","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**pill:** one step of a query, shown in the bar."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41ET","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**breadcrumb:** where the page stands, from home through the wholes above the holon the reader shows, each a way up; at rest, the top of the page."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41FR","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**λ:** the expression button at the breadcrumb's end, opening the bar in its place."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41G9","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**inspector:** what right-click opens: the place clicked, the component drawing it, the uses it was reached through, and the holon it shows."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41H2","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**look:** how a chassis draws its components, shipped beside them, the tokens it is made of opened as variables."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41HR","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**home:** the start of the page, the field's roots, where every breadcrumb begins; the page also still mounts a store of that name in the browser."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41JN","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**site:** a page that starts glass upon stores it names."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41K2","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**brief:** a holon of knowledge giving one understanding, the smaller ones beneath it."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41KJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**face:** a brief placed in another's flow, the start of a reading of its own."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41M4","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**thread:** a question held open in the field, with where it stands."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41MK","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**session:** a stretch of work with the author, kept whole in his words."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41N3","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**cycle:** a stretch of a session with one purpose, marked and condensed."]},"id":"1M82J5SES5A41NJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["The author reviewed the page and asked it to be a good experience, not only proof that rendering works (18/99, 18/101, 18/103), and the nineteenth session polished it under his eye. It uses the full width with one margin, prose alone keeping a reading measure, on one spacing scale. At rest the top of the page is where it stands: a breadcrumb from home, *Glass*, through the wholes holding the holon shown, each a link, or the query's text where the answer is no holon, with λ at its end, the expression button; at home, λ alone, small and to the left (19/9, 19/11). λ, a press on the line, or `/` opens the bar in its place, its pills and input, the pills wrapping where long; Enter on what is typed, Escape in the empty input, or a press outside the bar returns to the breadcrumb, and taking a pill out keeps it open (19/15). *The breadcrumb that opens, proposed by the session (19/8) and shaped by the author, \"for now, I want something sane\" (19/9, 19/11); the keys the session's; built.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P05Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The bar and the breadcrumb float over the page with no surface of their own, only their controls washed, so opening one, pills wrapping or a narrow page moves nothing, and only the answer scrolls, passing beneath them: gone behind their text, it fades in below them and fades out at the foot, itself and under no overlay, so no edge is felt, since \"you're never to feel that there is an actual div with the fill\" (19/5); an overlay in the ground's colour showed as one over cards, which are another colour (19/7, 19/16). What is shown stays until the next answer is ready, and the breadcrumb, the content and the scroll to the top change in the one moment nothing still waits to be read, so nothing flashes or jitters (19/13). *Asked by the author, 19/5 to 19/16; how, the session's; built.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P0AK","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Sizes stand in one register: small for keys, the breadcrumb and the bar, which saves space as the rule's surface's toolbar does; body for cards, fields and text; a lede in the body's size; card titles a step above it; and headings for prose alone, on a ratio of 1.35 from body, which the author offered (18/103), h4 to h1 a tenth larger since (19/5), h5 at the notch and 1.25 on phones. Links are known by their colour, never underlined, and a card pointed at takes the link's colour at its edge and a slightly other tone, \"as if a piece of glass was tilted just a little bit differently\" (19/7). A card says what its holon is: a brief's first paragraph, what a type says, a text's words, or the counts of what it holds. Lists fill the width by their children, as cards, rows or a table, chosen per place and remembered. A record keeps short values beside their keys, gives long content and every list of holons, however short, sections of their own, the session's answer to the author's question why the wiki's contents showed as no cards (19/7), draws a number or a truth answered alone as a figure (19/11), and ends in what refers to it, so there are no dead ends. *Asked by the author, 18/101, 18/103, 19/5, 19/7 and 19/11; a record ending in what refers to it the session's, accepted at 18/103; h5 at the notch and 1.25 on phones proposed, 18/104; built.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P0EY","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The page's root, Reader given the query's text, is a line of its own code, so the top of the page's holarchy stands in no store; only the layouts it reaches, Reader's and Search's, are held uses in glass (19/17, 19/18). A store of the site's own, web based and with persistence, perhaps begun from the site's code and needing no dotfile in the repository, is to come once components can be changed. *Leaning, 19/19: \"one that i guess is a web based one, with persistance\".*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P0HS","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component's look is the chassis's too, and shipped with the components, not with the site: \"the components look probably should be shipped with them. That's the component's responsibility\" (19/15). Styling has its degree, the author said, while what looks wholly different may want other components; so the look's variables are opened, to be tuned, by a knob component perhaps, and later taken from the field (19/15). On the web it stands in `interface/web/look/`, a stylesheet a component, beneath them the page's ground and the tokens; one built stylesheet and the faces are what a site links. The material, a stylesheet kept as text in glass that nothing read, was let go with its type: \"I don't see the point of the material\" (19/13, 19/15). *The look shipped with the components, its variables opened and the material let go, the author's, 19/15; its layout the session's; built.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P0PM","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The nineteenth session set the way back to it. The author asked that running locally and on the web both work, leaning away from build hacks though \"not sure here what is right yet\", and guessed the published site would read git from the actual remote (19/21); the stores and code the browser loads are to be \"rock solid\" (19/23). The session proposed one integration reaching git two ways: on the machine, the repository and its working tree; published, departing from the author's guess, the repository served as plain files, git's dumb HTTP, read from the site's own origin, since GitHub's git endpoints, as the session understood them and has not yet tested, give a page no leave to read them, and its API allows a visitor sixty questions an hour; every object, named by its hash, checked as it is read (19/22, 19/24). *Proposed; the published reach to be tested first.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P0VJ","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Its holons are directories and files, the repository's tree navigable as it is, one store on the start page, and a holon with code showing its code (19/19). A file has an id and a name, \"the name naraully just because its namespaced adress, the id might have to do with git hashes or something\", and its history comes with the integration, though it may wait (19/23); the session proposed the name its path's last step and the id derived from the path, the blob's hash naming each version (19/24). A holon pointing at a marked file the author sees value in, a dynamic needing more exploring and grounding (19/23). The session proposed that the stores, being files in the repository, be read through the integration, locally and published alike, each store's index the one output prepared beside them, and that code read from git be drawn by a code component, running it waiting until components can be changed (19/20, 19/22); locally, the author added, it might \"perhaps even be HMR thourgh the integraiton it self\" (19/23). *The aim, the author's, 19/19: leaning, \"Is that too much to ask for a simple session?\"; the rest proposed; none built.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P11Z","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The old wiki's fate:** whether The wiki, kept as it stood, is let go, as the author leaned to if Knowledge holds all it does (18/105), and whether the reasoning it alone holds comes into Knowledge first. *Open, awaiting the author.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P13D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The git integration:** the linked code of holons seen, the repository's tree navigable as it is, one store on the start page (19/19); read-only first, as the session proposed."]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P14D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Reading git from a browser, tested:** a repository served as plain files read from a page, with no proxy and no limit, before building on it (19/24)."]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P15B","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The stores read through git,** locally and published alike, the build no longer copying them (19/21)."]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P15Y","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Then the threads** standing open, divergence first among them: when a commit lands in some stores it touches and misses others, the holons it wrote marked diverged, the later commit's version found to answer, and the share not delivered kept while the engine lives, as settled at 12/77. *Open: where the mark is kept, and so whether a read may then ask for a holon only where holding says it lies; the thread Where divergence is marked.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P18G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The command line able to commit,** so the field is written through the engine by hand and the author's tools in `author/` go. *The tools going, settled 2026-11-11.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P19H","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Holons read as the type asked,** as the buffer of characters is read as a string."]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P1A4","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The engine, the interface and the stores were merged onto main and the site published (19/25); the expressions as uses, the buffer, the interface and the site on the engine, the stores in strata and components declared in their holons, the steps before these, are built, as each part says. The order now is the session's, the git integration first at the author's word (19/19). Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M82JA8FQN2P1C9","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}